const FICHAS={"pellets-cercal-alentejo":{"corpo":"<p>A fire at the pellet factory in the Cercal do Alentejo Business Zone began on 21 July, starting in a silo that burst, spreading to wood stored outside and to a neighbouring rural area. It was only brought under control ten days later, on 31 July.</p>\n<p>The Juntos pelo Cercal civic movement says residents were exposed to toxic smoke for more than two weeks, with complaints of respiratory problems and eye irritation, and warns that the village's proximity to the factory leaves the community \"always exposed to harmful factors\" from the industrial zone.</p>\n<p>The movement is demanding the immediate suspension of the factory under current conditions, an independent environmental impact study on human health and the ecosystem, and public participation in decisions about the territory.</p>","fontes":[["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/nao-conseguimos-respirar-movimento-alega-problemas-em-cercal-do-alentejo-devido-a-incendio-em-fabrica-de-pellets"],["RTP","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/economia/incendio-na-fabrica-de-pellets-em-cercal-do-alentejo-continua-ativo_n1670870"],["Notícias ao Minuto","https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/2834597/movimento-alega-problemas-respiratorios-em-cercal-do-alentejo"]],"stat":"","link":"https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/nao-conseguimos-respirar-movimento-alega-problemas-em-cercal-do-alentejo-devido-a-incendio-em-fabrica-de-pellets","linkL":"Read on Correio da Manhã"},"jardins-se-porto":{"corpo":"<p>A public petition, \"Not even the Cathedral is safe?\", has gathered over 1,800 signatures calling for the preservation of the Diocese gardens on Porto's Sé hill. According to the petitioners, the Major Seminary gardens will disappear under a new construction started by the Cathedral and the Seminary, whose owners changed a project approved as \"monastic accommodation\" into a 3-star hotel, keeping essentially the same building.</p>\n<p>Porto City Council intends to refuse the local accommodation licence for the development, holding that the Seminary's current function is not compatible with a fully independent and autonomous hotel activity.</p>\n<p>The Diocese of Porto says it is in dialogue with the council to find solutions that fit within the building permit already issued by the Council and that respect the site, located in Porto's historic centre.</p>","fontes":[["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/08/10/peticao-com-mais-de-1-800-assinaturas-pede-preservacao-dos-jardins-da-se-do-porto/"],["Viva Porto","https://viva-porto.pt/mais-de-1-800-assinaturas-pedem-para-travar-hotel-nos-jardins-da-se-do-porto/"]],"stat":"","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/08/10/peticao-com-mais-de-1-800-assinaturas-pede-preservacao-dos-jardins-da-se-do-porto/","linkL":"Read on Observador"},"agueda-eucaliptos":{"corpo":"<p>Quercus's Aveiro regional branch is denouncing new eucalyptus plantations near homes, waterways and roads in parts of the Águeda municipality hit by the 2024 wildfires, including a plot adjoining the home of a victim of the September 2024 fire. The GNR's SEPNA nature-protection service confirmed the existence of authorisations issued by ICNF under the legal framework for afforestation and reforestation actions.</p><p>Quercus is demanding ICNF urgently revoke licences in sensitive areas, inspect existing plantations, suspend or reverse risky situations, and follow through on measures announced after the 2024 fires to convert the landscape. </p><p>Águeda's municipal council says it set clear restrictions on fast-growing forest species in sensitive areas through its Municipal Master Plan, but accuses ICNF of systematically ignoring those rules when issuing afforestation permits.</p><p>On 19 September 2026, Quercus, the Floresta do Futuro (Forest of the Future) movement and the Póvoas Local Development and Protection Association (ADPLP) organised a protest walk against wildfires in Valongo do Vouga, in the municipality of Águeda, under the slogan \"Stop the Inferno, Create a Future\", the second initiative of its kind. According to Lusa, dozens of people demanded the removal of what they call a \"powder keg\" spread across the country \"in the form of planted and abandoned eucalyptus and pine plantations\". Along a walk of about six kilometres, participants visited land where local associations and communities have planted native species in areas previously taken over by eucalyptus and invasive plants, and removed eucalyptus trees near the villages. \"Our native forest burns less, burns more slowly. It also burns, but it burns less. And it is possible to control the fire much more easily\", João Camargo, spokesperson for the Floresta do Futuro movement, told Lusa.</p>","fontes":[["Quercus: Quercus denuncia novas plantações de eucalipto no concelho de Águeda em áreas afetadas pelos incêndios","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/07/09/quercus-denuncia-novas-plantacoes-de-eucalipto-no-concelho-de-agueda-em-areas-afetadas-pelos-incendios/"],["Agroportal: Quercus quer revogação das licenças de plantação de eucaliptos em Águeda","https://www.agroportal.pt/quercus-quer-revogacao-das-licencas-de-plantacao-de-eucaliptos-em-agueda/"],["Notícias de Águeda: Quercus denuncia novas plantações de eucalipto em zonas sensíveis de Águeda","https://noticiasdeagueda.sapo.pt/quercus-denuncia-novas-plantacoes-de-eucalipto-em-zonas-sensiveis-de-agueda-e-pede-revisao-urgente-das-autorizacoes/"],["Jornal da Bairrada: Águeda: Quercus denuncia novas plantações de eucalipto em áreas de incêndios","https://www.jb.pt/2026/07/agueda-quercus-denuncia-novas-plantacoes-de-eucalipto-em-areas-de-incendios/"],["Notícias de Águeda: Dozens gathered in Águeda to demand changes to the forest and more fire prevention (19 Sept. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://noticiasdeagueda.sapo.pt/dezenas-juntaram-se-em-agueda-para-exigir-mudancas-na-floresta-e-maior-prevencao-dos-incendios/"],["Lusa (in Correio da Manhã Canadá): Dozens in Águeda demand removal of the \"powder keg\" in the forests (19 Sept. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://www.correiodamanhacanada.com/incendios-dezenas-de-pessoas-exigiram-em-agueda-remocao-de-barril-de-polvora-nas-florestas/"]],"stat":"Plantations next to the home of a September 2024 fire victim","link":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/07/09/quercus-denuncia-novas-plantacoes-de-eucalipto-no-concelho-de-agueda-em-areas-afetadas-pelos-incendios/","linkL":"See Quercus statement →"},"biomassa-fundao":{"corpo":"<p>The Fundão Biomass Plant has operated since 2019 in the Fundão Industrial Zone, next to the homes of Sítio da Gramenesa.</p>","fontes":[["Quercus: New Fundão biomass plant shows evident negative impacts (8 Mar 2021) (in Portuguese)","https://quercus.pt/blog/2021/03/08/nova-central-de-biomassa-do-fundao-apresenta-impactes-negativos-evidentes-quercus-apela-a-intervencao-urgente-do-ministro-do-ambiente/"],["Notícias da Covilhã: Agreement between residents and the Fundão Biomass Plant (21 Jan 2025) (in Portuguese) (photo source)","https://noticiasdacovilha.pt/acordo-entre-moradores-e-central-de-biomassa-do-fundao/"],["RTP/Lusa: Fundão biomass plant and residents reach agreement (in Portuguese)","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/lusa/central-de-biomassa-do-fundao-e-moradores-chegam-a-acordo_n1627661"],["SÁBADO: Repórter Sábado, Fundão Biomass Plant breaches agreement and residents live with open-air ash (28 Mar 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.sabado.pt/video/detalhe/reporter-sabado-central-de-biomassa-do-fundao-incumpre-acordo-e-moradores-vivem-com-cinzas-a-ceu-aberto"],["Notícias da Covilhã: Fundão Biomass Plant rejects accusations of non-compliance (8 Apr 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://noticiasdacovilha.pt/central-de-biomassa-do-fundao-rejeita-acusacoes-de-incumprimento/"],["Mais Beiras: Fundão, CDU demands guarantees for the quality of life of Gramenesa residents (10 Apr 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://maisbeiras.sapo.pt/fundao-cdu-exige-garantias-para-qualidade-de-vida-dos-moradores-da-gramenesa"],["Análise Social, 61 (258), 2026: Luís Silva, Noise, smoke, ash and dust: environmental injustice and local struggles around a biomass plant in Portugal (in Portuguese)","https://revistas.rcaap.pt/analisesocial/article/view/40955"]],"stat":"Operating since 2019 · court agreement of Jan 2025","link":"https://www.sabado.pt/video/detalhe/reporter-sabado-central-de-biomassa-do-fundao-incumpre-acordo-e-moradores-vivem-com-cinzas-a-ceu-aberto","linkL":"Watch the report on SÁBADO","cronologia":[{"data":"2019","texto":"The Fundão Biomass Plant starts operating in the industrial zone next to Sítio da Gramenesa; residents begin reporting noise, smoke, dust and ash.","fonte":"https://www.sabado.pt/video/detalhe/reporter-sabado-central-de-biomassa-do-fundao-incumpre-acordo-e-moradores-vivem-com-cinzas-a-ceu-aberto"},{"data":"2021-03-08","texto":"Quercus points to the plant's \"evident negative impacts\", with high noise and dust from wood chipping, and asks the Environment Minister to intervene.","fonte":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2021/03/08/nova-central-de-biomassa-do-fundao-apresenta-impactes-negativos-evidentes-quercus-apela-a-intervencao-urgente-do-ministro-do-ambiente/"},{"data":"2025-01","texto":"The residents' association and the company sign an agreement ending the court cases: the plant undertakes to comply with noise rules, install acoustic barriers, carry out work on homes and pay compensation.","fonte":"https://noticiasdacovilha.pt/acordo-entre-moradores-e-central-de-biomassa-do-fundao/"},{"data":"2026-03-28","texto":"A SÁBADO report shows residents still living with noise, dust and ash and reporting that the agreement has not been honoured.","fonte":"https://www.sabado.pt/video/detalhe/reporter-sabado-central-de-biomassa-do-fundao-incumpre-acordo-e-moradores-vivem-com-cinzas-a-ceu-aberto"},{"data":"2026-04-08","texto":"The company rejects the accusations, says it has invested over a million euros in measures and blames the delays on some residents refusing access and on the Council.","fonte":"https://noticiasdacovilha.pt/central-de-biomassa-do-fundao-rejeita-acusacoes-de-incumprimento/"},{"data":"2026-04-10","texto":"CDU demands that residents' rights be respected and that the competent authorities carry out inspections.","fonte":"https://maisbeiras.sapo.pt/fundao-cdu-exige-garantias-para-qualidade-de-vida-dos-moradores-da-gramenesa"},{"data":"2026","texto":"A study in the journal Análise Social uses the case as an example of environmental injustice in the energy transition.","fonte":"https://revistas.rcaap.pt/analisesocial/article/view/40955"}],"contexto":"The Fundão Biomass Plant has operated since 2019 in the Fundão Industrial Zone, next to the homes of Sítio da Gramenesa."},"artilharia-um-campolide":{"corpo":"<p>The former Artilharia Um barracks in Campolide gave way to a real-estate project of seven plots and 683 housing units, developed by Novo Banco, on about five hectares next to Amoreiras.</p>\n<p>The Artilharia Um Movement contests the Environmental Impact Assessment exemption granted to the project, even though it exceeds the legal 500-unit threshold that normally requires such a study, and filed a formal complaint with the European Commission against the Portuguese State.</p>\n<p>A residents' petition, with over 400 signatures, is being reviewed by Lisbon's Municipal Assembly, while the case is also being examined by the Public Prosecutor's Office.</p>","fontes":[["Observador (in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2026/08/18/movimento-civico-artilharia-um-queixa-se-a-comissao-europeia-sobre-projeto-urbanistico-em-lisboa/"],["ECO (in Portuguese)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/05/07/moradores-de-lisboa-lancam-peticao-contra-projeto-urbanistico-na-zona-das-amoreiras/"],["Notícias de Lisboa (in Portuguese)","https://noticiaslx.pt/2026/08/18/queixa-a-comissao-europeia-lisboa/"]],"stat":"683 housing units · exempted from EIA","link":"https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=artilharia-um","linkL":"See the petition"},"penajoia-almada":{"corpo":"<p>The Penajóia neighbourhood, in Monte da Caparica, grew mainly over the past two years, on land belonging to IHRU, the Institute for Housing and Urban Rehabilitation. The housing crisis and unaffordable rents pushed families from Cape Verde, Angola and Guinea-Bissau, along with Brazilian and Portuguese families, into self-construction. About 160 households, roughly 350 people, now live in the neighbourhood, including 60 children, six newborns, 17 teenagers, elderly people, chronically ill residents and pregnant women, without public electricity, piped water or sanitation.</p>\n<p>IHRU began demolishing unfinished structures in January 2025. In December of that year, organizations again reported a case of forced demolition and eviction without rehousing: a family with three minor children was left without adequate housing after a demolition, and was even threatened with having the children removed while staying temporarily in a guesthouse.</p>\n<p>In December 2025, Almada City Council announced that the Ministry of Infrastructure and Housing would schedule a meeting for January to present a plan to halt the neighbourhood's expansion and find a housing solution. IHRU insists there will be no demolitions without alternative housing solutions, but residents, who wrote a letter to the council titled \"We are Almada too\", remain under threat.</p>\n<p>The same pattern documented in Beja and Loures repeats here: a racialized community, mostly of African origin, without access to basic environmental infrastructure, water, electricity, sanitation, and subject to evictions without a guaranteed housing alternative. This is environmental racism, even though the Portuguese press mostly frames it as a housing crisis.</p>","fontes":[["Renascença","https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2024/12/10/bairro-da-penajoia-almada-se-tivesse-outras-condicoes-nao-estava-aqui/404757/"],["Observador (demolitions begin)","https://observador.pt/2025/01/23/irhu-comecou-esta-quinta-feira-a-demolir-construcoes-inacabadas-no-bairro-penajoia-em-almada/"],["Observador (forced eviction, Dec. 2025)","https://observador.pt/2025/12/20/organizacoes-denunciam-novo-caso-de-demolicao-e-despejo-forcado-sem-realojamento-em-almada/"],["Balai (Cape Verdean community)","https://www.balai.cv/noticias/sociedade/portugal-imigrantes-cabo-verdianos-dos-bairros-da-penajoia-e-raposo-em-almada-vivem-sob-o-medo-da-demolicao/"],["RTP (\"We are Almada too\")","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/pais/tambem-somos-almada-moradores-do-bairro-da-penajoia-escrevem-carta-a-camara-municipal_n1693112"],["DN (IHRU guarantee)","https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/almada-ihru-garante-que-nao-havera-demolicoes-sem-solucoes-habitacionais"]],"stat":"About 350 people, 60 children, without water or public electricity on state-owned land","link":"https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2024/12/10/bairro-da-penajoia-almada-se-tivesse-outras-condicoes-nao-estava-aqui/404757/","linkL":"Read on Renascença"},"pedreiras-beja":{"corpo":"<p>Bairro das Pedreiras was opened in January 2006 by Beja City Council to rehouse about 50 families, roughly two hundred people, who had been living in shacks in the Bairro da Esperança. What was meant to be a temporary solution became permanent: two decades on, dozens of self-built shacks have sprung up around the original brick houses, without piped water, sanitation or electricity.</p>\n<p>According to Público, about a thousand people, over 200 children among them, live in conditions the newspaper describes as \"sub-human\": no drinking water, accumulated rubbish, dry scrub where snakes and rats breed, and temperatures above 38°C in summer with no relief. The neighbourhood sits next to the council's kennel and materials yard: the animal shelter's facilities were renovated while the families remain in shacks.</p>\n<p>Beja City Council carried out a new survey of the neighbourhood in 2025, but residents and journalists point to two decades of neglect by successive local and national governments. The Portuguese press describes the case as anticiganismo (anti-Roma discrimination). Internationally, the same pattern, basic environmental infrastructure denied to a racialized community, is called environmental racism: a term still rarely used in Portugal, but one that describes exactly the same phenomenon.</p>","fontes":[["Público (2023)","https://www.publico.pt/2023/08/22/local/noticia/familias-ciganas-beja-vivem-barracas-animais-dispoem-novas-instalacoes-2060768"],["Público (2018)","https://www.publico.pt/2018/01/23/local/noticia/secretarias-de-estado-chocadas-com-condicoes-da-comunidade-cigana-no-bairro-das-pedreiras-1800469"],["Diário do Alentejo","https://diariodoalentejo.pt/pt/noticias/22183/camara-de-beja-faz-novo-levantamento-do-bairro-das-pedreiras.aspx"],["Jornal Mapa","https://www.jornalmapa.pt/2025/12/08/habitar-na-precariedade-o-anticiganismo-que-se-constroi-em-betao-e-zinco/"],["Renascença","https://rr.pt/fotoreportagem/pais/2025/10/08/os-invisiveis-ciganos-vivem-esquecidos-no-meio-do-lixo-em-beja/442175/"]],"stat":"About 1,000 people, over 200 children, without water or sanitation","link":"https://www.publico.pt/2023/08/22/local/noticia/familias-ciganas-beja-vivem-barracas-animais-dispoem-novas-instalacoes-2060768","linkL":"Read on Público"},"girabolhos":{"corpo":"<p>The Girabolhos Dam project, on the Mondego River between Seia and Gouveia, has been relaunched to public tender after decades on hold. The Government presents the project as a response to flood risk in the region.</p>\n<p>GEOTA disputes this justification, pointing out that the dam's profile and location would not have contained the water volume responsible for the recent floods used to justify the project.</p>\n<p>The \"Rios Livres\" public petition calls for the project to be reassessed in light of its impact on aquatic wildlife and the natural dynamics of the Mondego River.</p>","fontes":[["GEOTA","https://www.geota.pt"],["Petição Pública: Rios Livres","https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=geota-rios-livres"],["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/ambientalistas-lancam-peticao-contra-construcao-da-barragem-de-girabolhos-no-mondego"],["Renascença","https://rr.pt/especial/pais/2026/06/24/em-girabolhos-todo-o-mundo-esta-de-acordo-com-a-barragem-concurso-arranca-a-15-de-julho/475639/"],["Seia Digital","https://seiadigital.pt/2026/07/14/governo-lanca-concurso-para-a-barragem-de-girabolhos-ministra-do-ambiente-anuncia-nova-fase-do-projeto-em-gouveia/"]],"stat":"Tender relaunched","link":"https://www.geota.pt","linkL":"Learn more at geota.pt"},"biometano-torres-novas":{"corpo":"<p>Gasdaterra plans to build a biomethane production unit in Árgea, in the municipality of Torres Novas, with an estimated investment of 18 million euros, to treat around 98,000 tonnes of waste a year and produce 6.5 million cubic metres of biomethane.</p>\n<p>Residents, backed by the Residents Commission, are contesting the site, just a few hundred metres from the village, over heavy traffic, air emissions, the risk of bad odours and well contamination. Torres Novas Municipal Assembly united against the project, and the Residents Commission called a protest vigil.</p>\n<p>The public consultation ran until 3 July 2026 on the Participa portal, but residents are asking for a further in-person public session and an unfavourable opinion from the Portuguese Environment Agency on the proposed site.</p>","fontes":[["O Mirante","https://omirante.pt/politica/2026-05-27-central-de-biometano-projectada-para-torres-novas-gera-contestacao-e-preocupa-autarcas-316867ff"],["Médio Tejo","https://mediotejo.net/assembleia-municipal-de-torres-novas-une-se-contra-unidade-de-biometano-em-argea/"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/17/comissao-de-utentes-convoca-vigilia-contra-unidade-de-biometano-em-torres-novas/"],["Ambiente Online","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/contestacao-a-unidade-de-biometano-em-torres-novas-ganha-forca-com-apoio-de-moradores-e-autarcas"]],"stat":"","link":"https://omirante.pt/politica/2026-05-27-central-de-biometano-projectada-para-torres-novas-gera-contestacao-e-preocupa-autarcas-316867ff","linkL":"Read on O Mirante"},"sintra-cascais":{"corpo":"<p>The Sintra-Cascais Natural Park includes the Cultural Landscape of Sintra, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Sintra Council is revising its Municipal Master Plan, which sets where building is allowed in the municipality, including in the Park's areas.</p>","fontes":[["Parques de Sintra: Cultural Landscape of Sintra, World Heritage (in Portuguese)","https://www.parquesdesintra.pt/pt/paisagem-cultural-de-sintra-patrimonio-unesco/"],["Sintra Notícias: Sintra master plan revision begins amid controversy (25 Jun 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://sintranoticias.pt/2026/06/25/revisao-do-pdm-de-sintra-nasce-sob-polemica-e-divisao-politica/"],["24notícias/SAPO: Environment Minister rules out declassifying the Sintra-Cascais Natural Park (7 Aug 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://24noticias.sapo.pt/atualidade/artigos/ministra-do-ambiente-afasta-risco-de-desclassificacao-do-parque-natural-de-sintra-cascais"],["Sintra Notícias: Left Bloc questions Government on urban pressure in the Sintra-Cascais Natural Park (23 Sep 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://sintranoticias.pt/2026/09/23/be-questiona-governo-sobre-pressao-urbanistica-no-parque-natural-de-sintra-cascais/"],["Petição Pública","https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT132295"],["Finis Terrae","https://finisterrae.pt"],["Notícias de Lisboa","https://noticiaslx.pt/2026/07/25/peticao-contesta-urbanizacao-prevista-no-parque-natural-de-sintra-cascais-na-revisao-do-pdm/"]],"stat":"","link":"https://finisterrae.pt","linkL":"Learn more at finisterrae.pt","cronologia":[{"data":"1995-12-06","texto":"The Cultural Landscape of Sintra is listed by UNESCO as a World Heritage Site.","fonte":"https://www.parquesdesintra.pt/pt/paisagem-cultural-de-sintra-patrimonio-unesco/"},{"data":"2026-06-23","texto":"Sintra Council approves the start of the revision of the Municipal Master Plan, with votes from PSD, an independent councillor and Chega and the PS voting against. The terms of reference go to a 90-day public consultation.","fonte":"https://sintranoticias.pt/2026/06/25/revisao-do-pdm-de-sintra-nasce-sob-polemica-e-divisao-politica/"},{"data":"2026-07","texto":"The Finis Terrae association delivers to Parliament the petition \"Against the Urbanisation of the Sintra-Cascais Natural Park\", asking Parliament to monitor the revision of the master plan.","fonte":"https://noticiaslx.pt/2026/07/25/peticao-contesta-urbanizacao-prevista-no-parque-natural-de-sintra-cascais-na-revisao-do-pdm/"},{"data":"2026-08-07","texto":"The Environment Minister rules out declassifying the Park, saying there is no intention of making any change to it. Finis Terrae had warned of the park's \"de facto extinction\" under way on the ground.","fonte":"https://24noticias.sapo.pt/atualidade/artigos/ministra-do-ambiente-afasta-risco-de-desclassificacao-do-parque-natural-de-sintra-cascais"},{"data":"2026-09-23","texto":"The Left Bloc questions the Government on the surveillance of the Park and on the possibility of extending building perimeters within it.","fonte":"https://sintranoticias.pt/2026/09/23/be-questiona-governo-sobre-pressao-urbanistica-no-parque-natural-de-sintra-cascais/"}],"contexto":"The Sintra-Cascais Natural Park includes the Cultural Landscape of Sintra, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Sintra Council is revising its Municipal Master Plan, which sets where building is allowed in the municipality, including in the Park's areas."},"costa-terra-melides":{"corpo":"<p>Between Tróia and Melides, in Grândola, the Costa Terra luxury resort occupies an estate of about 850 hectares on the coast, developed by Discovery Land Company. Private security, fences and identity checks restrict access to public beaches in the area.</p>","fontes":[["Dunas Livres Association (in Portuguese)","http://dunaslivres.pt/"],["ECO: Government requires owners between Tróia and Melides to guarantee beach access (9 Jul 2025) (in Portuguese)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2025/07/09/governo-obriga-proprietarios-entre-troia-e-melides-a-colocar-sinalizacao-e-garantir-acesso-a-praia/"],["DN: Solution for closed beaches in Grândola may not be ready before summer (27 Oct 2025) (in Portuguese)","https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/soluo-para-praias-fechadas-em-grndola-pode-no-estar-pronta-antes-do-vero-admite-ministra"],["O Setubalense: Quercus questions Government on free access to Grândola beaches (8 Jun 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://osetubalense.com/local/grandola/quercus-questiona-governo-sobre-reposicao-do-acesso-livre-as-praias-de-grandola"],["Quercus: statement, 10 Aug 2026","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/10/quercus-exige-explicacoes-a-ministra-do-ambiente-e-ao-presidente-da-cm-de-grandola-sobre-barreiras-e-controlo-de-acessos-em-praias-de-melides/"],["Público: seven beaches with conditioned access","https://www.publico.pt/2025/07/09/local/noticia/maioria-praias-grandola-lei-cumprida-ha-irregularidades-2139630"],["ECO: the millionaire revolution on the Alentejo coast","https://eco.sapo.pt/especiais/revolucao-milionaria-no-litoral-alentejano-construcao-toma-conta-dos-45-km-de-troia-a-melides/"],["Postal: the beach that costs €42","https://postal.pt/nacional/conheca-a-praia-a-sul-de-lisboa-cujo-acesso-custa-42e-e-onde-uma-sombra-pode-chegar-aos-200e/"],["TSF: minister promises to resolve Galé-Fontainhas","https://www.tsf.pt/sociedade/artigo/condicionamento-ao-acesso-a-praia-da-gale-fontainhas-vai-ser-resolvido-nao-esta-de-acordo-com-espirito-de-praia-publica/18114955"],["Tal&Qual: Mexican CostaTerra owners denounced in Europe","https://talequal.pt/mexicanos-do-costaterra-denunciados-na-europa/"],["LPN: petition for the Tróia Peninsula","https://www.lpn.pt/pt/cidadania/campanhas/pela-preservacao-do-patrimonio-natural-da-peninsula-de-troia"],["Quercus, 17 Sep 2026: appeal to the Environment Agency on Grândola beaches (in Portuguese)","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/09/17/quercus-apela-a-apa-para-nao-se-deixar-intimidar-por-ameacas-de-promotor-imobiliario-sobre-as-praias-de-grandola/"],["O Setubalense/Lusa, 17 Sep 2026: Quercus urges firmness from the Environment Agency (in Portuguese)","https://osetubalense.com/local/grandola/quercus-pede-firmeza-a-apa-perante-contestacao-aos-acessos-as-praias-de-grandola/"]],"stat":"7 beaches with conditioned access in Grândola","link":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/10/quercus-exige-explicacoes-a-ministra-do-ambiente-e-ao-presidente-da-cm-de-grandola-sobre-barreiras-e-controlo-de-acessos-em-praias-de-melides/","linkL":"Read the Quercus statement","cronologia":[{"data":"2020","texto":"The Dunas Livres movement is formed by citizens concerned about tourism expansion on the coast between Tróia and Melides.","fonte":"http://dunaslivres.pt/"},{"data":"2022","texto":"The movement becomes the Dunas Livres Association and joins ten environmental organisations.","fonte":"http://dunaslivres.pt/"},{"data":"2025-07-09","texto":"An Environment Agency inspection finds seven beaches in Grândola with access restricted by tourist developments: Tróia-Galé, Galé-Fontaínhas, Camarinhas, Duna Cinzenta, Golfinhos, Garças and Pinheirinho. The Government requires signage and new public accesses.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2025/07/09/governo-obriga-proprietarios-entre-troia-e-melides-a-colocar-sinalizacao-e-garantir-acesso-a-praia/"},{"data":"2025-10-27","texto":"The Environment Minister admits that the solutions for Grândola's beaches may not be ready before the bathing season.","fonte":"https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/soluo-para-praias-fechadas-em-grndola-pode-no-estar-pronta-antes-do-vero-admite-ministra"},{"data":"2026-06-08","texto":"Quercus asks the Environment Minister whether the irregularities found by the Environment Agency have been corrected and whether fines were issued.","fonte":"https://osetubalense.com/local/grandola/quercus-questiona-governo-sobre-reposicao-do-acesso-livre-as-praias-de-grandola"},{"data":"2026-08-10","texto":"With no reply, Quercus accuses the Minister and the Environment Agency of \"throwing sand in the eyes of the Portuguese\": physical barriers remain at Galé-Fontainhas and Aberta Nova beaches.","fonte":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/10/quercus-exige-explicacoes-a-ministra-do-ambiente-e-ao-presidente-da-cm-de-grandola-sobre-barreiras-e-controlo-de-acessos-em-praias-de-melides/"},{"data":"2026-09","texto":"Developer Coporgest threatens an injunction against the Environment Agency to stop the revision of the Espichel-Odeceixe Coastal Programme and 250 parking spaces next to the only public access to Camarinhas and Duna Cinzenta beaches.","fonte":"https://osetubalense.com/local/grandola/quercus-pede-firmeza-a-apa-perante-contestacao-aos-acessos-as-praias-de-grandola/"},{"data":"2026-09-17","texto":"Quercus condemns the developer's \"intimidation strategies\" and asks the Environment Agency to go ahead with the revision and with fines.","fonte":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/09/17/quercus-apela-a-apa-para-nao-se-deixar-intimidar-por-ameacas-de-promotor-imobiliario-sobre-as-praias-de-grandola/"}],"contexto":"Between Tróia and Melides, in Grândola, the Costa Terra luxury resort occupies an estate of about 850 hectares on the coast, developed by Discovery Land Company. Private security, fences and identity checks restrict access to public beaches in the area."},"descontaminacao-ilha-terceira":{"corpo":"<p>Over nearly seven decades, the US military presence at Lajes Base, on Terceira Island, left dozens of contaminated sites, documented by the Portuguese Air Force and the National Civil Engineering Laboratory (LNEC). Between 2020 and 2022, the United States carried out no remediation work, holding that the soil and aquifer contamination was not harmful to health.</p>\n<p>The decontamination process is stuck in a diplomatic deadlock, with neither Portugal nor the United States taking on concrete responsibility. An active public petition calls for effective environmental decontamination of the island's soils and aquifers.</p>\n<p>The Azores Parliament approved, with support from several parties, the creation of an Independent Technical Committee to oversee, monitor and evaluate the process. The Azores branch of the Socialist Party and the Left Bloc have asked the national Government for updated information and political priority on the issue.</p>","fontes":[["Green Savers","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/pela-descontaminacao-ambiental-dos-solos-e-aquiferos-da-ilha-terceira-ha-peticao-publica-online/"],["Observador: independent committee","https://observador.pt/2026/07/10/acores-criam-comissao-independente-para-fiscalizar-descontaminacao-dos-solos-na-ilha-terceira-junto-a-base-das-lajes/"],["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/portugal/detalhe/acores-solicitam-documentacao-sobre-descontaminacao-de-solos-e-aquiferos-ao-governo-da-republica"]],"stat":"Nearly 7 decades of contamination","link":"https://greensavers.sapo.pt/pela-descontaminacao-ambiental-dos-solos-e-aquiferos-da-ilha-terceira-ha-peticao-publica-online/","linkL":"Read on greensavers.sapo.pt"},"litoral-greenpeace":{"corpo":"<p>The report \"Destruição a Toda a Costa: Retrato de um litoral português em risco\" (\"Destruction All Along the Coast\"), published by Greenpeace Portugal on 23 July 2026, finds that 25% of mainland Portugal's coastline is eroding and that more than 100,000 people live in at-risk coastal areas, as sea level rises 3.7 mm a year, faster than the global average.</p><p>The organisation singles out the municipalities of Sesimbra and Grândola, in Setúbal district, as examples of outdated municipal master plans that keep licensing large tourism developments in protected areas: in Sesimbra, projects such as Pinhal da Prata, Pinhal do Atlântico and Étosoto occupy more than 260 hectares of protected land, moving forward without adequate environmental assessment.</p><p>Greenpeace estimates that by 2100 up to 50% of Alentejo's beaches and around 40% of the Algarve's beaches could disappear, and is calling on the government for a moratorium on construction in flood- or erosion-risk areas until 2050.</p>","fontes":[["Greenpeace Portugal: Comunicado do relatório \"Destruição a Toda a Costa\"","https://www.greenpeace.pt/meios-de-comunicacao/comunicados/greenpeace-portugal-alerta-um-quarto-da-costa-continental-portuguesa-esta-em-recuo-e-pressao-urbanistica-agrava-risco-no-litoral/"],["Jornal Económico: 25% da costa portuguesa está a recuar e mais de 100 mil pessoas vivem em risco","https://jornaleconomico.sapo.pt/noticias/25-da-costa-portuguesa-esta-a-recuar-e-mais-de-100-mil-pessoas-vivem-em-risco/"],["Barlavento: Greenpeace Portugal pede travão à construção nas zonas de risco do litoral algarvio","https://www.barlavento.pt/greenpeace-construcao-zonas-risco-litoral-algarvio/"],["Executive Digest: Mar avança sobre o litoral português e 40% das praias podem desaparecer até ao fim do século","https://executivedigest.sapo.pt/mar-avanca-sobre-o-litoral-portugues-e-40-das-praias-podem-desaparecer-ate-ao-fim-do-seculo/"]],"stat":"25% of the mainland coast eroding; 100,000+ people at risk","link":"https://www.greenpeace.pt/como-ajudar/peticoes/litoral/","linkL":"See Greenpeace's petition →"},"marao":{"corpo":"<p>The project plans to install around 25,000 photovoltaic panels next to the existing Penedo Ruivo Wind Farm, in Serra do Marão, between 1,120 and 1,220 metres of altitude.</p>\n<p>FAPAS warned of erosion and habitat loss risks in one of the highest-altitude areas of the North region, with direct impact on birds of prey and high-altitude vegetation cover.</p>\n<p>The public petition filed against the project asks for the environmental impact assessment to be reviewed before any final licensing decision.</p>","fontes":[["FAPAS","https://www.fapas.pt/a-fapas-pronuncia-se-contra-a-hibridizacao-fotovoltaica-no-parque-eolico-de-penedo-ruivo-no-marao/"],["Petição Pública","https://peticaopublica.com/mobile/pview.aspx?pi=PT130242"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2026/04/30/azul/noticia/baiao-parecer-desfavoravel-central-fotovoltaica-marao-2173160"],["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/clima/detalhe/associacao-alerta-para-riscos-de-central-fotovoltaica-no-marao"],["Câmara Municipal de Baião","https://cm-baiao.pt/municipio-de-baiao-emitiu-parecer-sobre-o-projeto-fotovoltaico-de-penedo-ruivo/"]],"stat":"1,120-1,220m altitude","link":"https://www.fapas.pt","linkL":"Learn more at fapas.pt"},"hyperion-abrantes":{"corpo":"<p>Hyperion II Renewables Services wants to build the second large-scale data center next to the Pego power plant, in Abrantes, already holding National Interest Project (PIN) status. The project envisages a 200 MVA connection capacity on over 1 million square metres of land, of which 15 hectares are earmarked for construction, with a planned start in 2029.</p>\n<p>Abrantes Municipal Council unanimously approved the project's preliminary request in May 2026. The Portuguese Environment Agency made its approval conditional on the submission of a complete environmental impact study, but only at the next licensing stage: in other words, the process moved forward before a full environmental assessment of the project existed.</p>\n<p>PIN status speeds up licensing and gives the developer a single point of contact within the State. It is the same regime used for other data centers, mines and energy projects in Portugal, some already documented by Causas de Raiz.</p>\n<p>On 22 September 2026, the Movimento pelo Tejo (proTEJO) demanded that licensing of the two Abrantes projects, Hyperion, in Alvega, and EDC One, next to Pego, be preceded by a cumulative Environmental Impact Assessment, warning that the Tagus basin \"no longer has room to be the cooling tower of European artificial intelligence\". According to the movement's estimates, the two data centers could consume, combined and at full capacity, between 3.6 and 22.2 million litres of water per day, depending on the cooling technology chosen, information the developers have not yet disclosed; on the energy side, the estimated maximum combined consumption is 4,380 GWh per year, nearly 29 times the municipality's annual electricity use. proTEJO also calls for public information sessions in Alvega and Concavada, binding maximum limits on water and energy efficiency, public disclosure of each data center's performance data, and a reassessment of the Pego Technology Free Zone.</p>","fontes":[["Correio do Ribatejo","https://correiodoribatejo.pt/abrantes-aprova-pedido-previo-para-segundo-centro-de-dados-junto-a-central-do-pego/"],["ECO: how the Government plans to attract more data centers","https://eco.sapo.pt/descodificador/como-o-governo-planeia-atrair-mais-data-centers-para-portugal/"],["Observador/Lusa news agency: proTEJO demands limits on data centers' water and energy use in Abrantes (22 Sep 2026, in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2026/09/22/protejo-exige-limites-ao-consumo-de-agua-e-energia-de-centros-de-dados-em-abrantes/"],["Quercus: two mega data centers in Abrantes could exceed the municipality's annual energy consumption by nearly 30 times (26 Aug 2026, in Portuguese)","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/26/centros-de-dados-abrantes/"]],"stat":"200 MVA connection capacity","link":"https://correiodoribatejo.pt/abrantes-aprova-pedido-previo-para-segundo-centro-de-dados-junto-a-central-do-pego/","linkL":"Read on Correio do Ribatejo"},"incineradora-algarve":{"corpo":"<p>Environment and Energy Minister Maria da Graça Carvalho announced on 8 August 2026 that the Portuguese Environment Agency will move ahead with an energy-from-waste incineration unit in the Algarve, with investment of up to 300 million euros and operation expected to begin in 2034. The plan responds to the looming exhaustion of the Portimão and Loulé landfills, expected around 2027, in a region that produces 400,000 tonnes of urban waste a year, 85% of which goes to landfill.</p><p>Environmental group Zero called the proposal \"harmful management\" of the public interest and requested an urgent meeting with the minister to clarify the region's waste strategy. Quercus considers incineration \"completely anachronistic\", incompatible with PERSU 2030 targets and Portugal's climate commitments, arguing the technology emits more CO₂ per kWh than fossil fuels.</p><p>On 3 September, Quercus announced it will lead a White Paper on Waste in Portugal, with input from universities, municipalities and other bodies, to propose alternatives to incineration. The Environment Agency plans to launch a tender on 15 October to study the technology and final location of the unit.</p><p>On 6 October 2026, according to Lusa, ZERO met the Environment Minister and again rejected incineration, proposing mechanical-biological treatment \"by improving and expanding\" Algar's two plants. Ecologist Rui Berkemeier warned that the separation of household waste from waste from economic activities \"is partly not being complied with in the Algarve\", which is filling the landfills faster. See also the Sotavento Landfill case, in Loulé.</p>","fontes":[["Observador: Ambientalistas consideram incineradora \"gestão danosa\"","https://observador.pt/2026/08/10/ambientalistas-consideram-incineradora-no-algarve-gestao-danosa-do-interesse-publico/"],["TSF: Governo anuncia construção de incineradora no Algarve","https://www.tsf.pt/sociedade/artigo/governo-anuncia-construcao-de-incineradora-no-algarve/18114431"],["Barlavento: ZERO chama gestão danosa à eventual incineradora","https://www.barlavento.pt/zero-chama-gestao-danosa-a-eventual-incineradora-no-algarve/"],["Quercus: Queimar lixo não","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/09/03/queimar-lixo-nao-quercus-critica-incineradora-no-algarve-e-vai-dinamizar-livro-branco-dos-residuos-em-portugal/"],["Sul Informação: Quercus rejeita incineradora e exige respostas à ministra","https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2026/09/quercus-rejeita-incineradora-no-algarve-e-exige-respostas-a-ministra/"],["Jornal do Algarve/Lusa: Association backs mechanical-biological waste treatment and rejects incineration (6 Oct. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://jornaldoalgarve.pt/associacao-defende-tratamento-mecanico-e-biologico-dos-residuos-e-rejeita-incineracao/"]],"stat":"400,000 tonnes of waste/year in the Algarve, 85% landfilled","link":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/09/03/queimar-lixo-nao-quercus-critica-incineradora-no-algarve-e-vai-dinamizar-livro-branco-dos-residuos-em-portugal/","linkL":"See Quercus's position →"},"matosinhos-ribeira-leca":{"corpo":"<p>Discharges of polluting waste from the site of Galp's former refinery in Leça da Palmeira left a \"nauseating smell\" affecting Matosinhos in April 2026. Galp confirmed the occurrence at a decommissioned part of the old refinery, saying it was \"under mitigation\" and posed no risk to public health; the Portuguese Environment Agency is now processing a fine against the company.</p><p>The problem runs deeper: Matosinhos City Council has detected around 900 illegal connections discharging wastewater directly into the Riguinha and Carcavelos streams, which flow out near Matosinhos beach. Episodes of microbiological contamination have already led to temporary bathing bans (the beach was closed 18 times in the last bathing season) and it risks losing its official \"Bathing Water\" status.</p><p>In August 2026, PSD and Chega councillors demanded the council draw up an integrated stream-recovery plan, inspect illegal connections and set up public real-time water-quality monitoring. The municipality has already corrected around 200 of the illegal connections found.</p>","fontes":[["JN: Descargas nas ribeiras deixam \"cheiro nauseabundo\" em Matosinhos","https://www.jn.pt/jn-direto/artigo/descargas-nas-ribeiras-deixam-cheiro-nauseabundo-em-matosinhos/18069284"],["Observador: Galp confirma descarga de antiga refinaria em Matosinhos \"em mitigação\"","https://observador.pt/2026/05/06/galp-confirma-descarga-de-antiga-refinaria-em-matosinhos-que-esta-em-mitigacao/"],["ECO: Galp confirma descarga de antiga refinaria em Matosinhos","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/05/06/galp-confirma-descarga-de-antiga-refinaria-em-matosinhos-que-esta-em-mitigacao/"],["JN: Matosinhos deteta 900 ligações ilegais nas ribeiras urbanas","https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/matosinhos-deteta-900-ligacoes-ilegais-nas-ribeiras-urbanas/17853601"],["Público: Praia de Matosinhos em risco de não ser zona balnear","https://www.publico.pt/2026/01/25/azul/noticia/praia-matosinhos-risco-nao-zona-balnear-2162430"],["JN: Centenas de ligações ilegais ajudam a explicar contaminação na praia de Matosinhos","https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/centenas-de-ligacoes-ilegais-ajudam-a-explicar-contaminacao-na-praia-de-matosinhos-/17858641"]],"stat":"~900 illegal connections found in Matosinhos's streams","link":"https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/matosinhos-deteta-900-ligacoes-ilegais-nas-ribeiras-urbanas/17853601","linkL":"See JN report →"},"meia-praia-lagos":{"corpo":"<p>Around 50 people protested outside Lagos City Council against the construction of two hotels and a block of tourist apartments on 11,000 m² of Meia Praia, under a 1988 building permit revised in 2008. The protest was organised by the civic movement \"Salvar a Meia Praia\" (Save Meia Praia), made up mostly of foreign residents in the area.</p><p>The movement argues the land should be turned into public green space rather than a tourist development that includes a five-star hotel. It is also calling for a new environmental impact assessment, particularly of the lagoon basin on the site.</p><p>Lagos's mayor said he was not in favour of building on the first line of coast, but acknowledged the council cannot block the project if the developer meets all applicable laws and regulations; he confirmed licensing is conditional on rehabilitating the lagoon basin.</p>","fontes":[["Postal: Protesto em Lagos pede suspensão de projeto turístico na Meia Praia","https://postal.pt/algarve/protesto-em-lagos-pede-suspensao-de-projeto-turistico-na-meia-praia/"],["Jornal do Algarve: Cidadãos mostram-se contra a construção de unidades hoteleiras na Meia Praia, em Lagos","https://jornaldoalgarve.pt/cidadaos-mostram-se-contra-a-construcao-de-unidades-hoteleiras-na-meia-praia-em-lagos/"],["The Portugal News: Citizens gather at Câmara Municipal de Lagos to Save Meia Praia","https://www.theportugalnews.com/news/2026-08-28/citizens-gather-at-camara-municipal-de-lagos-to-save-meia-praia/1075492"],["Algarve Marafado: O caos urbanístico da Meia Praia","https://www.algarvemarafado.com/2026/04/30/o-caos-urbanistico-da-meia-praia/"]],"stat":"Two hotels and tourist apartments on 11,000 m² of Meia Praia","link":"https://postal.pt/algarve/protesto-em-lagos-pede-suspensao-de-projeto-turistico-na-meia-praia/","linkL":"See report on the protest →"},"lagoa-salgada":{"corpo":"<p>The Lagoa Salgada mining project, between Grândola and Alcácer do Sal, plans a €196 million investment to mine a polymetallic deposit of copper, lead and zinc near the Alentejo coast.</p>\n<p>The Portuguese Environment Agency has already issued an unfavourable Environmental Impact Statement, citing risks to underground water resources and coastal ecosystems in the region.</p>\n<p>The public petition calls for the definitive cancellation of the licensing process, even in the face of possible appeals from the promoting company.</p>","fontes":[["Petição Pública","https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT125518"],["JN","https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/protecao-da-agua-justifica-chumbo-da-agencia-portuguesa-do-ambiente-a-mina-da-lagoa-salgada/18043930"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/01/23/mina-de-cobre-e-zinco-da-lagoa-salgada-volta-a-ter-chumbo-ambiental/"],["Alentejo Ilustrado","https://alentejoilustrado.pt/alcacer-do-sal-muito-feliz-com-chumbo-da-mina-da-lagoa-salgada/"]],"stat":"€196 million","link":"https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT125518","linkL":"View the petition"},"mina-adagoi":{"corpo":"<p>The C-192 Adagoi mining concession, located in the parishes of Capeludos and Bragado, in Vila Pouca de Aguiar, plans to mine quartz, feldspar and lithium through the company MCS, which describes the project as \"relatively small-scale and low-impact\".</p>\n<p>Citizens concerned with protecting the environment, public health and sustainable development are asking for clarification on the impacts on water resources, soils, biodiversity and the local landscape, as well as on the financial guarantees planned for environmental recovery.</p>\n<p>The project adds to other concessions in the same Barroso region, where mining pressure on farming communities has already been a source of resistance for several years.</p>","fontes":[["A Voz de Trás-os-Montes","https://www.avozdetrasosmontes.pt/projeto-de-exploracao-mineira-da-origem-a-peticao/"],["Jornal de Chaves","https://jornaldechaves.pt/noticia?id=11310"],["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/02/23/mcs-quer-explorar-feldspato-em-vila-pouca-de-aguiar-mas-enfrenta-oposicao/"]],"stat":"","link":"https://www.avozdetrasosmontes.pt/projeto-de-exploracao-mineira-da-origem-a-peticao/","linkL":"Read on A Voz de Trás-os-Montes"},"mina-gudina":{"corpo":"<p>In Pentes, in the municipality of A Gudiña (Ourense, Galicia), Tungsten San Juan, a subsidiary of Swedish Eurobattery Minerals, is preparing an open-pit tungsten mine about 100 metres from the Ribeira de Pente, which flows into the river Rabaçal in Vinhais, inside the Montesinho Natural Park, and supplies water to fourteen Portuguese villages.</p>","fontes":[["Mensageiro de Bragança: European Commission wants rigorous assessment of the tungsten mine's impacts (6 Jul 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.mdb.pt/index.php/noticia/comissao-europeia-quer-avaliacao-rigorosa-aos-impactos-da-mina-de-volframio-dois"],["Diário de Trás-os-Montes","https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/ecologistas-e-autarcas-protestam-em-a-gudina-contra-mina-junto-a-fronteira-com-portugal"],["Mensageiro de Bragança","https://www.mdb.pt/noticia/ambientalistas-portugueses-e-galegos-protestam-contra-mina-junto-fronteira-de-vinhais"],["Jornal Nordeste","https://jornalnordeste.com/2026/06/19/uivo-acusa-espanha-de-violar-acordos-bilaterais-e-admite-recorrer-aos-tribunais-para-travar-exploracao-junto-a-fronteira-portuguesa/"],["Ambiente Online","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/movimento-alerta-para-mina-espanhola-junto-a-vinhais-que-pode-ameacar-o-rio-rabacal-e-o-parque-natural-de-montesinho"],["ICNF: Montesinho Natural Park, description (in Portuguese, accessed 27 Sep 2026)","https://resources.natural.pt/uploads/additional-information/2019/06/12/08/Msm1aTmOfwIWzjc2.pdf"],["Galiciapress, 24 Sep 2026: A Gudiña council orders immediate halt to Eurobattery Minerals mine (in Spanish)","https://www.galiciapress.es/articulo/empresas/2026-09-24/6026945-gobierno-gudina-ordena-paralizar-inmediatamente-actividad-mina-eurobattery-minerals"],["Galiciapress, 28 Sep 2026: A Gudiña mining company announces temporary suspension of mining activities (in Spanish)","https://www.galiciapress.es/articulo/economia/2026-09-28/6031702-empresa-mina-gudina-ourense-comunica-suspension-temporal-actividade-mineras"],["Notícias ao Minuto / Lusa, 26 Sep 2026: Mining works in A Gudiña suspended after company director's conviction (in Portuguese)","https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/3057782/trabalhos-mineiros-na-a-gudina-suspensos-apos-condenacao-do-diretor-da-empresa-responsavel"],["Mensageiro de Bragança, 28 Sep 2026: Uivo Movement calls for definitive revocation of tungsten mine near the Portuguese border (in Portuguese)","https://www.mdb.pt/noticia/movimento-uivo-apela-revogacao-definitiva-da-mina-de-volframio-junto-fronteira-portuguesa"]],"stat":"14 villages rely on the Rabaçal river","link":"https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/ecologistas-e-autarcas-protestam-em-a-gudina-contra-mina-junto-a-fronteira-com-portugal","linkL":"Read in Diário de Trás-os-Montes","cronologia":[{"data":"2026-06-19","texto":"Movimento UIVO accuses Spain of ignoring the transboundary impact assessment required by the Espoo Convention and considers going to court.","fonte":"https://jornalnordeste.com/2026/06/19/uivo-acusa-espanha-de-violar-acordos-bilaterais-e-admite-recorrer-aos-tribunais-para-travar-exploracao-junto-a-fronteira-portuguesa/"},{"data":"2026-07-06","texto":"Answering MEPs Catarina Martins and Ana Miranda, the European Commission reiterates the obligation to rigorously assess the mine's transboundary environmental impacts.","fonte":"https://www.mdb.pt/index.php/noticia/comissao-europeia-quer-avaliacao-rigorosa-aos-impactos-da-mina-de-volframio-dois"},{"data":"2026-07-23","texto":"About 40 Portuguese and Galician environmentalists and local officials gather in A Gudiña and hand the mayor a letter demanding the transboundary study.","fonte":"https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/ecologistas-e-autarcas-protestam-em-a-gudina-contra-mina-junto-a-fronteira-com-portugal"},{"data":"2026-09-24","texto":"The A Gudiña council orders the immediate halt of mining activity until the company submits the required documents.","fonte":"https://www.galiciapress.es/articulo/empresas/2026-09-24/6026945-gobierno-gudina-ordena-paralizar-inmediatamente-actividad-mina-eurobattery-minerals"},{"data":"2026-09-26","texto":"Lusa reports that the Spanish courts have upheld the conviction of the head of Eurobattery Minerals to a two-year suspended sentence for fraud in a Sierra Leone gold mining scheme.","fonte":"https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/3057782/trabalhos-mineiros-na-a-gudina-suspensos-apos-condenacao-do-diretor-da-empresa-responsavel"},{"data":"2026-09-28","texto":"Tungsten San Juan, a subsidiary of Eurobattery Minerals, starts the procedure to temporarily suspend mining.","fonte":"https://www.galiciapress.es/articulo/economia/2026-09-28/6031702-empresa-mina-gudina-ourense-comunica-suspension-temporal-actividade-mineras"},{"data":"2026-09-28","texto":"Movimento UIVO calls for the mine to be permanently revoked.","fonte":"https://www.mdb.pt/noticia/movimento-uivo-apela-revogacao-definitiva-da-mina-de-volframio-junto-fronteira-portuguesa"}],"contexto":"In Pentes, in the municipality of A Gudiña (Ourense, Galicia), Tungsten San Juan, a subsidiary of Swedish Eurobattery Minerals, is preparing an open-pit tungsten mine about 100 metres from the Ribeira de Pente, which flows into the river Rabaçal in Vinhais, inside the Montesinho Natural Park, and supplies water to fourteen Portuguese villages."},"mina-panasqueira":{"corpo":"<p>The Panasqueira Mines, operating for over a century across the municipalities of Covilhã and Fundão, are among Europe's oldest and most productive tin and tungsten mines, currently run by Beralt Tin and Wolfram Portugal. In January 2026, heavy rain caused another collapse in the mine's tailings structure, sweeping toxic inert waste into the Cebola stream, a tributary of the Zêzere River.</p>\n<p>Quercus warned of highly toxic heavy metals, including lead and arsenic, also detected along the banks of the Zêzere itself. The incident led to the suspension of water intake at a local supply point and forced Covilhã's municipal council to step up water quality testing.</p>\n<p>The association notes that the Castelo do Bode Dam, on the Zêzere, supplies water to the Greater Lisbon area, and is calling on the Portuguese Environment Agency, the water regulator ERSAR and the Inspectorate-General of Agriculture, Sea, Environment and Land Use Planning for stronger oversight, while demanding that Beralt remediate the tailings, expand wastewater treatment capacity and carry out regular maintenance of the pipes carrying toxic effluent.</p>","fontes":[["Quercus","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/03/24/alerta-para-risco-de-contaminacao-do-rio-zezere/"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2026/03/24/azul/noticia/minas-panasqueira-quercus-denuncia-risco-contaminacao-toxica-rio-zezere-2163617"],["JN","https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/quercus-pede-fiscalizacao-a-agua-do-zezere-por-receio-de-contaminacao-com-residuos-da-panasqueira/18065748"],["Portugal Resident","https://www.portugalresident.com/concerns-for-lisbon-drinking-water-following-repeated-mining-waste-collapse/"]],"stat":"Lead and arsenic in the Zêzere","link":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/03/24/alerta-para-risco-de-contaminacao-do-rio-zezere/","linkL":"Read Quercus' statement"},"rio-corgo-vila-real":{"corpo":"<p>The Portuguese Environment Agency (APA) is investigating the death of dozens of fish recorded in the Corgo River, in Vila Real municipality, in an action carried out together with the GNR's Nature and Environment Protection Service (SEPNA). Water samples and dead fish specimens were collected for laboratory analysis.</p>\n<p>The authorities' preliminary assessment points to a probable abnormal wastewater discharge, whose source is still being determined, that entered the watercourse through the stormwater drainage network. The pollution event appears to have been a one-off, between 15 and 16 August 2026, days with thunderstorms and rain in the region; combined with high temperatures and the low summer flow typical of the season, this likely triggered the fish kill.</p>\n<p>APA continues to monitor the situation on the ground and is awaiting laboratory reports to determine the exact extent of the ecological damage and the source of the discharge.</p>","fontes":[["Diário de Notícias","https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/apa-investiga-causas-da-morte-de-peixes-no-rio-corgo-em-vila-real"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/08/19/descarga-de-aguas-residuais-podera-ter-causado-morte-de-peixes-em-rio-de-vila-real/"]],"stat":"One-off discharge on 15-16 August 2026","link":"https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/apa-investiga-causas-da-morte-de-peixes-no-rio-corgo-em-vila-real","linkL":"Read on Diário de Notícias"},"trilhos-madeira":{"corpo":"<p>The Regional Government of Madeira decided to hand over management of access to hiking trails to private entities, contracting the security company Strong Charon for 320,000 euros, from April to December, to control access to sites such as Pico do Areeiro, Ribeiro Frio, Achada do Teixeira, Queimadas and Ponta de São Lourenço.</p>\n<p>Citizens concerned with preserving the Autonomous Region's natural, cultural and social heritage are speaking out against any privatisation, concession or abusive restriction of public access to the trails. The LIVRE party also publicly spoke out against the measure, calling it \"an attack on public natural heritage\".</p>\n<p>Critics point above all to the lack of public consultation, transparency or democratic debate before the Regional Government's decision.</p>","fontes":[["Jornal da Madeira","https://www.jm-madeira.pt/regiao/livre-continua-a-opor-se-a-privatizacao-dos-percursos-pedestres-e-apela-a-intervencao-da-sociedade-civil-DN18407422"],["Funchal Notícias","https://funchalnoticias.net/2025/06/24/livre-madeira-mantem-oposicao-a-privatizacao-dos-percursos-pedestres/"],["Petição Pública","https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT125916"]],"stat":"","link":"https://www.jm-madeira.pt/regiao/livre-continua-a-opor-se-a-privatizacao-dos-percursos-pedestres-e-apela-a-intervencao-da-sociedade-civil-DN18407422","linkL":"Read on Jornal da Madeira"},"costa-caparica-arvores":{"corpo":"<p>A beach-access upgrade project in Costa da Caparica (phase 2), costing around €3 million, led Almada municipal council to announce the felling of 47 trees in Praça Padre Manuel Bernardes and Torre das Argolas.</p>\n<p>Residents, however, count 103 trees already cut or marked for felling, including at least 23 in June 2026 alone, and question the council's criteria. The council has pledged to plant 120 new trees in compensation.</p>\n<p>A public petition, now past 2,600 signatures, calls for an immediate halt to the felling of the 34 trees still marked, for the demolition of Praça dos Navegantes to stop, and for more transparency and dialogue with residents before the works proceed.</p>","fontes":[["Almadense (in Portuguese)","https://almadense.sapo.pt/ambiente/abate-de-arvores-na-costa-da-caparica-indigna-moradores-nao-percebemos-qual-o-criterio/"],["Almada Municipal Council (in Portuguese)","https://www.cm-almada.pt/empreitada-acessibilidade-a-costa-da-caparica-acesso-alternativo-as-praias-fase-2-rua-padre-manuel-bernardes"]],"stat":"103 trees counted vs. 47 announced","link":"https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=PT132029","linkL":"See the petition"},"campismo-gale":{"corpo":"<p>The Galé campsite in Melides (Grândola municipality) closed in October 2021, after being bought for around €25 million by Discovery Land Company, the developer behind the Costa Terra Golf &amp; Ocean Club luxury resort. Widely regarded as the country's best public campsite, it has never reopened.</p><p>The Reabrir a Galé civic movement, born from a group of regular campsite users, launched a petition for the campsite's continued operation, discussed at a parliamentary hearing in October 2022 with the participation of the Dunas Livres Association. The group also alleges environmental irregularities linked to the resort, such as dune destruction to build a golf course roughly 500 metres from the sea. Grândola's municipal council has stated it cannot intervene since it is private investment. The same resort (and the same stretch of coast between Tróia and Melides) is also linked to recurring complaints about restricted public beach access, documented in official inspections and denounced by Quercus.</p>","fontes":[["Rádio Campanário (parliamentary hearing)","https://www.radiocampanario.com/reabertura-do-parque-de-campismo-da-gale-em-audicao-na-assembleia-da-republica-dia-13/"],["The Portugal News (profile of the Reabrir a Galé movement)","https://www.theportugalnews.com/news/2022-08-06/reabrir-a-gale-fighting-for-answers/69191"],["Portugal Resident (barriers to beach access in Melides)","https://www.portugalresident.com/all-portuguese-beaches-are-public-says-government-but-not-so-in-melides/"]],"stat":"","link":"https://www.facebook.com/ReabrirAGale/","linkL":"See the Reabrir a Galé movement's page →"},"aranha-cavernicola-arrabida":{"corpo":"<p>Anapistula ataecina, known as the Frade cave spider, is Europe's smallest spider, measuring under half a millimetre. It lives only in the karst system of Frade, in Sesimbra, inside the Arrábida Natural Park; males of the species have never been observed, as reproduction is parthenogenetic.</p>\n<p>The International Union for Conservation of Nature classifies the species as Critically Endangered, the highest threat level. With such a restricted range, the presence of quarries within its distribution area, and the risk of their expansion, is identified as the main threat to the species' survival.</p>\n<p>The petition, addressed to Parliament and to ICNF, calls for concrete measures to protect the species' cave habitat, in a natural park where we already document other causes linked to quarrying activity.</p>","fontes":[["Naturdata","https://naturdata.com/aranha-endemica-de-portugal-classificada-pela-iucn-como-criticamente-em-perigo-de-extincao/"],["GreenSavers","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/sabia-que-a-aranha-mais-pequena-da-europa-vive-em-portugal/"],["Esquerda.net","https://www.esquerda.net/artigo/pelo-menos-mais-de-200-especies-de-invertebrados-em-risco-de-extincao-em-portugal/87085"]],"stat":"","link":"https://naturdata.com/aranha-endemica-de-portugal-classificada-pela-iucn-como-criticamente-em-perigo-de-extincao/","linkL":"Read on Naturdata"},"fortes-ferreira-alentejo":{"corpo":"<p>The AZPO – Azeites de Portugal plant, which extracts olive-pomace oil about 300 metres from the village of Fortes in Ferreira do Alentejo, has been accused for over a decade of polluting the region's air and water; the Portuguese Environment Agency has already confirmed unlicensed wastewater discharges.</p>\n<p>A criminal case against the company was archived by the Public Prosecutor's Office for lack of evidence. Tired of waiting for a response from the authorities, the Amigos das Fortes Environmental Association bought its own air-quality monitoring equipment.</p>\n<p>Between 24 and 29 July 2026, the equipment recorded over 30 hours of volatile organic compound concentrations above acceptable limits. The association will hand the results over to the environment agency and has launched a petition for the right to breathe clean air.</p>","fontes":[["Diário de Notícias (in Portuguese)","https://www.dn.pt/portugal/queixas-no-ministerio-publico-contra-fabrica-acusada-de-poluir-aldeia-no-alentejo-9345952.html"],["Observador (in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2026/07/24/cansados-de-esperar-moradores-compram-equipamento-para-medir-poluicao-de-fabrica-junto-a-sua-aldeia-no-alentejo/"],["Plataforma Media (in Portuguese)","https://www.plataformamedia.com/2026/08/03/qualidade-do-ar-preocupa-moradores-de-aldeia-portuguesa-apos-testes-revelarem-valores-acima-do-permitido/"]],"stat":"30+ hours above VOC limits","link":"https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=PT131002","linkL":"See the petition"},"pedreira-lajedo-santo-tirso":{"corpo":"<p>The Lajedo quarry, in Monte Córdova, Santo Tirso, sat inactive for over ten years until it was reactivated in 2024, with an illegal expansion into an ecological reserve zone. For decades, residents complained of blasts that cracked walls and threw stones onto roofs, on top of noise and pressure on soils and water resources.</p>\n<p>A group of citizens launched a public petition demanding the permanent closure of the quarry, arguing that the operation undermines the well-being and quality of life of the local population. In March 2026, the company operating the quarry went as far as threatening to cut off a public road that had been in use for 30 years.</p>\n<p>The dispute between the company and residents remains unresolved, with Santo Tirso City Council also involved in the process.</p>","fontes":[["Jornal de Notícias","https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/moradores-criaram-peticao-para-exigir-fim-de-pedreira-em-santo-tirso/17855057"],["Diário de Santo Tirso","https://www.diariodesantotirso.pt/peticao-publica-pelo-encerramento-da-pedreira-do-lajedo-ja-tem-de-350-assinaturas/"],["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/03/04/empresa-ameaca-cortar-estrada-publica-em-santo-tirso-para-operar-em-pedreira/"],["Jornal do Ave","https://jornaldoave.sapo.pt/cidadaos-lancam-peticao-contra-reativacao-da-pedreira-de-lajedo-em-monte-cordova/"]],"stat":"","link":"https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/moradores-criaram-peticao-para-exigir-fim-de-pedreira-em-santo-tirso/17855057","linkL":"Read on Jornal de Notícias"},"predios-madeira":{"corpo":"<p>Madeira's Regional Government president, Miguel Albuquerque, defended revising Funchal's Municipal Master Plan (PDM) to allow residential buildings up to 20 storeys, as a response to the shortage of available land for housing. Funchal City Council came out in support of the proposal.</p>\n<p>In response, more than 1,700 citizens signed the petition \"Pela Salvaguarda do Modelo Urbano da Madeira\" (\"For the Safeguard of Madeira's Urban Model\"), asking parties represented in the regional parliament to recommend that the Government not approve legislative, regulatory or territorial planning changes that would, as a general rule, allow buildings over ten storeys in the region. The petitioners instead call for urban rehabilitation policies, reuse of vacant buildings and regeneration of already built-up areas.</p>\n<p>According to the petition, defining Madeira's urban model \"is a generational decision, whose effects will last for decades,\" and should be preceded by a broad public debate involving universities, professional associations, local authorities and experts in urban planning, architecture and the environment. Miguel Albuquerque downplayed the opposition, saying the proposal would only allow high-rise construction \"in areas with no landscape impact.\"</p>","fontes":[["Espaço de Arquitetura","https://espacodearquitetura.com/noticias/peticao-contra-o-aumento-da-construcao-em-altura-na-madeira/"],["DNOTICIAS","https://www.dnoticias.pt/2026/7/24/500243-peticao-contra-construcao-em-altura-a-caminho-da-assembleia/"],["Observador: Albuquerque defende revisão do PDM","https://observador.pt/2026/07/15/albuquerque-defende-revisao-do-pdm-para-permitir-predios-de-habitacao-em-altura-no-funchal/"],["Observador: Câmara do Funchal apoia","https://observador.pt/2026/07/16/camara-do-funchal-apoia-construcao-de-predios-de-habitacao-em-altura-no-concelho/"],["JM Madeira","https://www.jm-madeira.pt/not%C3%ADcias/regi-o/30002568/mais-de-1-700-peticionarios-contra-o-aumento-da-construcao-em-altura-na-madeira.html"],["SAPO Notícias","https://sapo.pt/artigo/peticao-contra-edificios-em-altura-na-madeira-atinge-mil-assinaturas-6a5cb85ec3fc30cdb0f69f0b"]],"stat":"","link":"https://espacodearquitetura.com/noticias/peticao-contra-o-aumento-da-construcao-em-altura-na-madeira/","linkL":"Read on Espaço de Arquitetura"},"nordeste-vivo-mogadouro":{"corpo":"<p>At the first public information session on renewable energy megaprojects in Northeast Trás-os-Montes, held in Mogadouro with around 50 people present, Plataforma Nordeste Vivo confirmed that most residents did not know the real scale of the projects already built or approved. According to José Jambas, one of the movement's founders, the continuous stretch of solar panels already exceeds 1,500 hectares across the Planalto Mirandês.</p>\n<p>In Miranda do Douro, the hybridization project promoted by Engie plans to install 35 wind turbines 200 metres tall, more than half the height of the Eiffel Tower. The developers' own environmental impact studies show that hundreds of hectares of farmland, including dryland crops, will go uncultivated for the 30-year lifespan of the projects.</p>\n<p>Plataforma Nordeste Vivo said it would move forward with legal injunctions and new complaints to the Public Prosecutor's Office. The movement is not opposed to renewable energy itself, but argues that rooftops, industrial zones, parking lots and other existing infrastructure should be used first, before farmland and forest land.</p>","fontes":[["Jornal Nordeste","https://jornalnordeste.com/noticias/nordeste-vivo-prepara-novas-acoes-apos-primeira-sessao-de-esclarecimento-sobre-megaprojetos-energeticos"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2026/05/12/azul/noticia/engie-avanca-hibridizacao-hidroelectricas-transmontanas-energia-fotovoltaica-2174366"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/15/plataforma-nordeste-vivo-exige-suspensao-do-programa-de-renovaveis-e-acusa-governo-de-conduzir-processo-na-sombra/"],["Mensageiro de Bragança","https://www.mdb.pt/index.php/noticia/plataforma-nordeste-vivo-exige-suspensao-do-pszaer-pedindo-responsabilidade-politica-0"],["Jornal Nordeste: council opposition","https://jornalnordeste.com/noticias/presidente-da-camara-de-mogadouro-reforca-oposicao-a-novos-parques-renovaveis"],["Petição Pública: Travanca","https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT131073"]],"stat":"1,500+ hectares already covered","link":"https://jornalnordeste.com/noticias/nordeste-vivo-prepara-novas-acoes-apos-primeira-sessao-de-esclarecimento-sobre-megaprojetos-energeticos","linkL":"Read on Jornal Nordeste"},"sao-luis-odemira":{"corpo":"<p>The Juntos por São Luís movement is raising the alarm over a mega photovoltaic plant planned for the Poldreiros do Meio and Lameiros area, in the parish of São Luís, municipality of Odemira, covering between 100 and 150 hectares inside the Natura 2000 network, in National Ecological Reserve areas.</p>\n<p>Juntos por São Luís is part of the Movimento Energia Justa e Sustentável (MEJS), a national platform created by nine civic movements and associations against the spread of solar and wind megaprojects \"with unacceptable location and scale\", defending a just energy transition.</p>\n<p>The petition calls for the project's site to be reviewed and for already artificial land, such as rooftops and industrial zones, to be prioritised before farmland and forest land.</p>","fontes":[["RTP","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/economia/movimentos-civicos-criam-plataforma-nacional-contra-megaprojetos-solares-e-eolicos_n1745481"],["Sul Informação","https://alentejo.sulinformacao.pt/2026/06/movimentos-civicos-criam-plataforma-nacional-contra-megaprojetos-solares-e-eolicos"],["Jornal Económico","https://jornaleconomico.sapo.pt/noticias/movimentos-civicos-criam-plataforma-nacional-contra-megaprojetos-solares-e-eolicos/"]],"stat":"","link":"https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/economia/movimentos-civicos-criam-plataforma-nacional-contra-megaprojetos-solares-e-eolicos_n1745481","linkL":"Read on RTP"},"eolico-penamacor-2":{"corpo":"<p>The government authorised, through Order (Despacho) no. 775/2026 of 23 January, the felling of 451 cork oaks (383 young, 68 mature) and 304 holm oaks (284 young, 20 mature), 755 protected trees in total, across 6.76 hectares in the Serra de Santo André, in the Meimoa and Penamacor parishes, Castelo Branco district.</p><p>The felling is for the Penamacor 2 Wind Farm repowering project: developer Lestenergia will replace the seven existing turbines with four more powerful ones, nearly quadrupling annual output from 23.48 GWh to 88.44 GWh. The Portuguese Environment Agency exempted the project from its own environmental impact assessment, under the regime applicable to repowering already-licensed wind farms.</p><p>The authorisation is conditional on an environmental compensation plan requiring the company to plant trees across 12.7 hectares, almost double the affected area. A public petition is calling for the felling authorisation to be revoked entirely, for alternative, lower-impact sites to be assessed, and for the principle of avoiding and minimising harm before compensating for it to be reinforced.</p><p>The case fits a wider pattern: according to Executive Digest, the Government authorised the felling of over 9,000 protected trees in just two months, across several wind repowering projects nationwide.</p>","fontes":[["Público: Government authorises felling of cork and holm oaks in Penamacor wind park (in Portuguese)","https://www.publico.pt/2026/01/27/azul/noticia/governo-autoriza-abate-sobreiros-azinheiras-parque-eolico-penamacor-2162560"],["Executive Digest: Government authorises felling of over 9,000 protected trees in just two months (in Portuguese)","https://executivedigest.sapo.pt/governo-autoriza-abate-de-mais-de-9000-arvores-protegidas-em-apenas-dois-meses/"],["Diário Digital Castelo Branco: Penamacor: Government authorises felling of cork and holm oaks in wind park (in Portuguese)","https://www.diariodigitalcastelobranco.pt/noticia/70664/penamacor-governo-autoriza-abate-de-sobreiros-e-azinheiras-em-parque-eolico"],["Despacho n.º 775/2026, of 23 January: Diário da República (in Portuguese)","https://dre.tretas.org/dre/6421708/despacho-775-2026-de-23-de-janeiro"],["Public petition (in Portuguese)","https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=PT129537"]],"stat":"755 protected trees authorised for felling (451 cork oaks, 304 holm oaks)","link":"https://www.publico.pt/2026/01/27/azul/noticia/governo-autoriza-abate-sobreiros-azinheiras-parque-eolico-penamacor-2162560","linkL":"See the public petition →"},"sophia-beira":{"corpo":"<p>Lightsource bp planned two mega solar plants in Beira Baixa: Sophia (867 MWp), in Fundão, Penamacor and Idanha-a-Nova, and Beira (266 MW, 425,600 modules on about 524 hectares), in Castelo Branco and Idanha-a-Nova, in areas of cork oak woodland and protected habitats.</p>","fontes":[["Mais Beiras: Sophia project breaks record for public submissions (21 Nov 2025) (in Portuguese)","https://maisbeiras.sapo.pt/beira-baixa-projeto-sophia-bateu-recorde-participacoes-publicas-contra-o-projeto"],["Diário de Viseu/Lusa: Developer abandons the Beira solar plant (14 Sep 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.diarioviseu.pt/2026/09/14/promotor-abandona-projeto-da-central-solar-beira-em-castelo-branco-e-idanha-a-nova/"],["SAPO: Environment Agency publishes consultation reports on Beira and Sophia (19 May 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://sapo.pt/artigo/apa-torna-publico-relatorio-das-consultas-publicas-das-mega-centrais-solares-beira-e-sophia-6a0c778291dd71e123e2e2b7"],["Green Savers: Deadline to reformulate the Sophia project ends on 2 October (9 Sep 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/prazo-para-reformulacao-do-projeto-da-central-solar-sophia-termina-em-02-de-outubro/"],["ECO: Lightsource bp abandons the Beira solar plant (14 Sep 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/09/14/lightsource-bp-desiste-de-central-solar-da-beira-por-falta-de-viabilidade-financeira/"],["SAPO: Revised project cuts Sophia's capacity by 34% (14 Sep 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://sapo.pt/artigo/projeto-alterado-reduz-em-34-capacidade-da-central-solar-sophia-apos-diagnostico-de-impacto-negativo-6aa7a97dd98f4c2b510a241f"],["Participação Parlamento","https://participacao.parlamento.pt/initiatives/5569"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2026/01/30/azul/noticia/beira-baixa-entrega-peticao-parlamento-traz-lisboa-oposicao-centrais-solares-2162812"],["SÁBADO","https://www.sabado.pt/portugal/detalhe/de-beira-baixa-a-lisboa-contra-megaprojetos-solares-planeados-para-a-regiao"],["Diário Digital Castelo Branco","https://www.diariodigitalcastelobranco.pt/noticia/70468/plataforma-contra-mega-centrais-solares-na-beira-baixa-entrega-peticao-no-parlamento"],["RTP","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/economia/plataforma-contra-mega-centrais-solares-na-beira-baixa-entrega-peticao-no-parlamento_n1707993"],["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/especiais/megacentral-sophia-encolhe-mais-de-um-terco-para-caber-nas-exigencias-do-territorio-conheca-o-novo-desenho/"],["O Interior: Lightsource BP redesigns Sophia Solar Plant projects (23 Sep 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.ointerior.pt/regiao/lightsource-bp-reformula-projetos-para-central-solar-sophia/"],["Lightsource bp (press release, via SAPO): Lightsource bp steps up dialogue with communities on the Sophia Solar Park (25 Sep 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://sapo.pt/artigo/lightsource-bp-reforca-dialogo-com-as-comunidades-sobre-o-parque-solar-sophia-6ab6416f9a39cd87ad9a3e69"]],"stat":"1,158+ ha of montado","link":"https://participacao.parlamento.pt/initiatives/5569","linkL":"View the initiative in Parliament","cronologia":[{"data":"2025-11","texto":"The public consultation on the Sophia project exceeds ten thousand submissions, a record for environmental assessment procedures in Portugal.","fonte":"https://maisbeiras.sapo.pt/beira-baixa-projeto-sophia-bateu-recorde-participacoes-publicas-contra-o-projeto"},{"data":"2025-12","texto":"The assessment committee finds that the Beira project, as submitted, cannot be approved, due to significant negative impacts on ecological systems and land use.","fonte":"https://www.diarioviseu.pt/2026/09/14/promotor-abandona-projeto-da-central-solar-beira-em-castelo-branco-e-idanha-a-nova/"},{"data":"2025-12-30","texto":"The Platform against Mega Solar Plants in Beira Baixa delivers to Parliament a petition calling for a halt to mega solar plans in natural areas and fragile ecosystems.","fonte":"https://www.diariodigitalcastelobranco.pt/noticia/70468/plataforma-contra-mega-centrais-solares-na-beira-baixa-entrega-peticao-no-parlamento"},{"data":"2026-05-19","texto":"After a complaint to the Administrative Documents Access Commission, the Environment Agency publishes the consultation reports: they point to permanent and irreversible impacts and, for Sophia, with 12,693 submissions, the need for a very significant reduction of the project.","fonte":"https://sapo.pt/artigo/apa-torna-publico-relatorio-das-consultas-publicas-das-mega-centrais-solares-beira-e-sophia-6a0c778291dd71e123e2e2b7"},{"data":"2026-09-09","texto":"The Environment Agency sets 2 October as the deadline for Lightsource bp to submit the reformulated Sophia project; a new 10-working-day public consultation follows.","fonte":"https://greensavers.sapo.pt/prazo-para-reformulacao-do-projeto-da-central-solar-sophia-termina-em-02-de-outubro/"},{"data":"2026-09-14","texto":"Lightsource bp abandons the Beira project, citing the lack of financial viability of the reformulated solution.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/09/14/lightsource-bp-desiste-de-central-solar-da-beira-por-falta-de-viabilidade-financeira/"},{"data":"2026-09-14","texto":"Lightsource bp announces a 34% reduction of Sophia, from 867 to about 573 MWp, and its withdrawal from areas with irrigation potential.","fonte":"https://sapo.pt/artigo/projeto-alterado-reduz-em-34-capacidade-da-central-solar-sophia-apos-diagnostico-de-impacto-negativo-6aa7a97dd98f4c2b510a241f"},{"data":"2026-09-21","texto":"The developer presents the reformulated project at public sessions in Penamacor, Idanha-a-Nova and Fundão.","fonte":"https://www.ointerior.pt/regiao/lightsource-bp-reformula-projetos-para-central-solar-sophia/","dataFim":"2026-09-23"}],"contexto":"Lightsource bp planned two mega solar plants in Beira Baixa: Sophia (867 MWp), in Fundão, Penamacor and Idanha-a-Nova, and Beira (266 MW, 425,600 modules on about 524 hectares), in Castelo Branco and Idanha-a-Nova, in areas of cork oak woodland and protected habitats."},"citrinos-alcacer-do-sal":{"corpo":"<p>The Aquaterra group, linked to a North American investment fund, received a conditional Environmental Impact Statement on 3 August 2026 for an intensive tangerine farming project across roughly 295 hectares at the Murta and Monte Novo estates, in Alcácer do Sal. It is the fourth version of the project: the previous three, which proposed 722 hectares of avocado, were all rejected.</p>\n<p>The site lies within the Natura 2000 network, in the Comporta/Galé Special Conservation Area, over an aquifer already in critical condition, with land subsidence and rising piezometric pressure. The project still depends on groundwater abstraction through 12 deep boreholes. Alentejo's regional environmental authority approved the statement despite an unfavourable opinion from Quercus and despite 99.2% of public consultation submissions rejecting the project; ZERO called the decision a \"gross error\".</p>\n<p>Quercus will file a formal complaint with the European Commission for breach of EU law, calling for the protection of the Comporta-Galé conservation area and the region's aquifers, and is considering an injunction at Portugal's administrative courts to suspend the statement. The association is also demanding an independent opinion from the National Laboratory of Energy and Geology on the aquifer and the resumption of the National Water Council, which hasn't met in three years.</p><p>Before the decision, on 15 June 2026, during the public consultation on the revised project (open until 19 June), the civic movement Alcácer P'lo Ambiente warned of a \"devastating\" environmental impact and called for the proposal to be rejected: according to the movement, the project involves clearing 352 hectares, felling 40,984 stone pines and 442 maritime pines, and using about 1.74 billion litres of water a year, with risks of soil erosion and desertification in a region already vulnerable to drought.</p>","fontes":[["Wilder","https://wilder.pt/historias/quercus-apresenta-queixa-a-comissao-europeia-sobre-projeto-de-citrinos-em-alcacer-do-sal"],["Quercus","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/14/projeto-citrinos-alcacer-do-sal/"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/08/13/luz-verde-dada-a-projeto-de-tangerinas-que-substitui-abacates-em-alcacer-do-sal-e-erro-grosseiro-diz-a-zero/"],["GreenSavers","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/zero-considera-erro-grosseiro-luz-verde-a-projeto-de-tangerinas-em-alcacer-do-sal/"],["Diário do Distrito (SAPO): Movement warns of felling of more than 41,000 pine trees in Alcácer do Sal (15 Jun. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://sapo.pt/artigo/movimento-alerta-para-abate-de-mais-de-41-mil-pinheiros-em-alcacer-do-sal-6a2fed46272fc55d31f3ac4e"]],"stat":"99.2% of public consultation against the project","link":"https://wilder.pt/historias/quercus-apresenta-queixa-a-comissao-europeia-sobre-projeto-de-citrinos-em-alcacer-do-sal","linkL":"Read on Wilder"},"eolico-mira-odemira":{"corpo":"<p>Galp proposes the \"Mira Wind Project\", a hybrid wind-solar park with about 22 turbines and about 158 megawatts between Odemira and Ourique, near the parishes of Relíquias, São Martinho das Amoreiras, Luzianes-Gare and Santa Clara-a-Velha.</p>","fontes":[["Rádio Pax: Galp wind farm on the Alentejo coast will not go ahead (27 May 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.radiopax.com/parque-eolico-da-galp-no-litoral-alentejano-nao-vai-avancar-camara-de-odemira/"],["Sul Informação: \"Mira Wind Project\": Galp plans new hybrid wind-solar project in Odemira and Ourique municipalities (in Portuguese)","https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2026/07/projeto-eolico-do-mira-galp-planeia-novo-projeto-hibrido-eolico-solar-nos-concelhos-de-odemira-e-ourique/"],["ECO: Galp studies wind project with around 22 turbines between Ourique and Odemira (in Portuguese)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/07/22/galp-estuda-projeto-eolico-com-cerca-de-22-aerogeradores-entre-ourique-e-odemira/"],["Public Petition (in Portuguese)","https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT131724"],["Jornal PT Green: Mira Wind Project sits less than 9km from three protected areas (in Portuguese)","https://jornalptgreen.pt/noticia/projeto-eolico-do-mira-instala-se/"],["Participa (Portuguese Environment Agency): Mira Wind Farm, Hybridisation of the Ourique Solar Plant, PDA283 (in Portuguese)","https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/parque-eolico-de-mira-hibridizacao-da-central-fotovoltaica-de-ourique-pda283"],["Quercus, 25 Sep 2026: Quercus warns of potential ecological impacts of new wind farm in Odemira and Ourique (in Portuguese)","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/09/25/quercus-alerta-para-potenciais-impactes-ecologicos-de-novo-parque-eolico-em-odemira-e-ourique/"],["Green Savers: Quercus calls for review of the Mira Wind Farm project in Alentejo (in Portuguese)","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/quercus-defende-revisao-do-projeto-do-parque-eolico-do-mira-no-alentejo/"]],"stat":"22 turbines · 158 MW · 476 public consultation submissions","link":"https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2026/07/projeto-eolico-do-mira-galp-planeia-novo-projeto-hibrido-eolico-solar-nos-concelhos-de-odemira-e-ourique/","linkL":"Read on Sul Informação","cronologia":[{"data":"2026-01","texto":"Galp's previous project in the area, the Cachenas wind farm (19 turbines between Vila Nova de Milfontes and Porto Covo), is under public consultation; a petition calls for its suspension.","fonte":"https://www.radiopax.com/parque-eolico-da-galp-no-litoral-alentejano-nao-vai-avancar-camara-de-odemira/"},{"data":"2026-05-27","texto":"Odemira Council announces that Galp has dropped the Cachenas wind farm.","fonte":"https://www.radiopax.com/parque-eolico-da-galp-no-litoral-alentejano-nao-vai-avancar-camara-de-odemira/"},{"data":"2026-07-22","texto":"Galp studies a new project, the \"Mira Wind Project\", with about 22 turbines and a solar component between Odemira and Ourique.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/07/22/galp-estuda-projeto-eolico-com-cerca-de-22-aerogeradores-entre-ourique-e-odemira/"},{"data":"2026-09-04","texto":"Public consultation on the scoping proposal for the environmental impact study, with 476 submissions.","fonte":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/parque-eolico-de-mira-hibridizacao-da-central-fotovoltaica-de-ourique-pda283","dataFim":"2026-09-24"},{"data":"2026-09-25","texto":"Quercus issues an unfavourable opinion: impacts on birds and sensitive habitats are underestimated, and the turbines, up to 200 metres tall, would stand about 5 km from protected areas.","fonte":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/09/25/quercus-alerta-para-potenciais-impactes-ecologicos-de-novo-parque-eolico-em-odemira-e-ourique/"}],"contexto":"Galp proposes the \"Mira Wind Project\", a hybrid wind-solar park with about 22 turbines and about 158 megawatts between Odemira and Ourique, near the parishes of Relíquias, São Martinho das Amoreiras, Luzianes-Gare and Santa Clara-a-Velha."},"incendios":{"corpo":"<p>By 19 August 2026, Portugal had recorded 6,666 rural fires and 63,347 hectares of burned area, according to the Integrated Rural Fire Management System (SGIFR), run by AGIF. It is the fifth worst year for burned area in the decade, behind 2017, 2025, 2016 and 2022, and the sixth worst year for number of fires, reversing the downward trend seen since 2022.</p>\n<p>The fire that broke out in Tourelhe, Vouzela, on 2 July officially became Europe's largest wildfire of 2026, alone accounting for around 70% of all area burned in Portugal this year, with the destruction nearly quadrupling compared to the equivalent 2025 fire. According to Diário de Notícias, this is already the worst cumulative record since the tragic year of 2017 and the Pedrógão Grande fire.</p>\n<p>Since 15 August, several significant fires have broken out daily, mostly in the north, most notably in Torre de Moncorvo, Bragança district, the longest-running and still active. The municipalities with the most burned area in 2026 are Valpaços, Mirandela, Águeda and Vouzela. In July, a firefighter was injured while fighting the Santo Tirso fire and was taken to Hospital do Médio Ave.</p>\n<p>Agricultural burning was the leading cause of fires recorded up to 15 August, responsible for 37% of incidents. By region, the North has the most burned area (34,929 ha), followed by the Centre (20,452 ha) and the Alentejo (3,335 ha).</p>","fontes":[["Diário de Notícias: European record","https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/vouzela-atira-portugal-para-recorde-da-europa-de-rea-ardida-em-2026"],["ECO: burned area four times smaller, but more fires","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/08/18/area-ardida-quatro-vezes-menor-este-ano-mas-numero-de-fogos-aumenta/"],["CNN Portugal: agricultural burning behind most fires","https://cnnportugal.iol.pt/incendios/fogos/incendios-queimas-e-queimadas-na-origem-da-maior-parte-dos-fogos-ate-15-de-agosto/20260819/6a858fa0d34ed0733ba8089b"],["Diário de Coimbra","https://www.diariocoimbra.pt/2026/08/19/queimas-sao-principal-causa-dos-incendios-em-portugal-ate-15-de-agosto/"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/06/area-ardida-duplicou-em-cinco-dias-e-ja-e-a-maior-desde-2017-mais-de-15-000-hectares-queimados-entre-1-e-5-de-julho/"]],"stat":"63,347 hectares burned · Vouzela fire is Europe's largest of 2026","link":"https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/vouzela-atira-portugal-para-recorde-da-europa-de-rea-ardida-em-2026","linkL":"Read on Diário de Notícias"},"barragem-foupana":{"corpo":"<p>Portugal's Environment Agency (APA) opened, on 31 August 2026, public consultation on the Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA) for the new Foupana dam in eastern Algarve, running until 12 October via the Participa portal. The project, promoted by the Eastern Algarve Irrigation Beneficiaries Association (ABPRSA), includes the dam itself, a connecting tunnel to the Odeleite-Beliche system and access roads, with an overall estimated cost between 150 and 200 million euros.</p><p>Environmental group Almargem has opposed the project since 2023, calling the Foupana stream &quot;the Algarve's last great free-flowing stream&quot; and one of the region's best-preserved watercourses, with no protection status at all. The group argues the Foupana should be included in the Natura 2000 network, warns of the impact on the saramugo, a critically endangered endemic fish, and notes that the Algarve's six existing dams (Odelouca, Arade, Funcho, Bravura, Beliche and Odeleite) already frequently run below capacity, questioning the cost-benefit of a seventh. Castro Marim's municipal council has separately warned about the lack of protected status for the area, compounded by a mining prospecting request overlapping the future dam's site.</p>","fontes":[["Jornal do Algarve / Lusa (opening of public consultation)","https://jornaldoalgarve.pt/apa-avanca-com-avaliacao-de-impacte-ambiental-para-barragem-na-foupana/"],["Algarve Marafado (estimated project cost)","https://www.algarvemarafado.com/2026/08/29/nova-barragem-a-vista-para-o-algarve-custo-ronda-os-200-milhoes-de-euros/"],["Jornal do Algarve (Almargem's position)","https://jornaldoalgarve.pt/almargem-manifesta-se-contra-construcao-da-barragem-da-foupana/"],["Barlavento (Castro Marim council on the area's vulnerability)","https://www.barlavento.pt/barragem-da-foupana-castro-marim-alerta-para-vunerabilidade-da-zona/"]],"stat":"Estimated cost between 150 and 200 million euros","link":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/barragem-da-foupana","linkL":"See public consultation on Participa →"},"biometano-abrigada-alenquer":{"corpo":"<p>Gás da Terra wants to build a 20.5 million euro biomethane plant in Marés, about 500 metres from homes in Abrigada, in the municipality of Alenquer, to process about 84,000 tonnes of farm waste a year.</p>","fontes":[["O Mirante (in Portuguese)","https://omirante.pt/sociedade/2026-08-15-abrigada-rejeita-unidade-de-biometano-a-500-metros-das-casas-6d2e6bf7"],["Valor Local (in Portuguese)","https://valorlocal.pt/projeto-biometano-mares-alenquer-preocupa-populacao/"],["Quercus, 15 Sep 2026: unfavourable opinion on the Abrigada plant (in Portuguese)","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/09/15/biometano-nao-pode-por-em-risco-agua-e-solos-quercus-emite-parecer-desfavoravel-a-unidade-de-abrigada-em-alenquer/"],["Lusa/RTVON, 15 Sep 2026: About a hundred people protest against biomethane plant in Alenquer (in Portuguese)","https://www.rtvon.pt/2026/09/15/uma-centena-pessoas-em-protesto-contra-central-de-biometano-em-alenquer/"],["O Mirante, 19 Aug 2026: project enters public consultation (in Portuguese)","https://omirante.pt/sociedade/2026-08-19-projecto-de-unidade-de-biometano-em-abrigada-entrou-em-consulta-publica-e6bbd143"],["Voz de Alenquer, 4 Sep 2026: residents form committee against project (in Portuguese)","https://vozdealenquer.pt/central-de-biometano-moradores-criam-comissao-contra-projeto/"],["Participa: EIA public consultation, 19 Aug to 29 Sep 2026 (in Portuguese)","https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/uab-abrigada--unidade-de-producao-de-biometano-de-origem-renovavel-de-abrigada"],["SAPO / Lusa, 25 Sep 2026: Alenquer Municipal Assembly speaks out against biomethane plant (in Portuguese)","https://sapo.pt/artigo/assembleia-municipal-de-alenquer-manifesta-se-contra-instalacao-de-central-de-biometano-6ab6ab0bc5a3f84d7f57a258"],["Ambiente Online / Lusa, 28 Sep 2026: Location of biomethane plant contested by Alenquer Municipal Assembly (in Portuguese)","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/localizacao-de-central-de-biometano-contestada-pela-assembleia-municipal-de-alenquer"],["Voz de Alenquer: Planned biomethane plant in Marés presented amid local protest (7 Aug 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://vozdealenquer.pt/futura-central-de-biometano-nas-mares-apresentada-com-contestacao-de-populares/"]],"stat":"€20.5 million · 500m from homes","link":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/uab-abrigada--unidade-de-producao-de-biometano-de-origem-renovavel-de-abrigada","linkL":"View the public consultation →","cronologia":[{"data":"2026-08-06","texto":"At an information session held by Gás da Terra at the Abrigada philharmonic society, residents repeatedly interrupt the presentation, worried about the plant's proximity to homes.","fonte":"https://vozdealenquer.pt/futura-central-de-biometano-nas-mares-apresentada-com-contestacao-de-populares/"},{"data":"2026-08-19","texto":"Public consultation on the Environmental Impact Assessment on the Participa portal, which receives 417 submissions.","fonte":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/uab-abrigada--unidade-de-producao-de-biometano-de-origem-renovavel-de-abrigada","dataFim":"2026-09-29"},{"data":"2026-08","texto":"Alenquer Council issues an unfavourable opinion: there is no evidence that the plant will not produce odours, and there are concerns about access and the EN1/IC2 road.","fonte":"https://www.rtvon.pt/2026/09/15/uma-centena-pessoas-em-protesto-contra-central-de-biometano-em-alenquer/"},{"data":"2026-09-03","texto":"At a session held by the parish union of Abrigada and Cabanas de Torres, with about 150 people, the parish presents an unfavourable opinion on the location and a residents' committee against the project is announced.","fonte":"https://vozdealenquer.pt/central-de-biometano-moradores-criam-comissao-contra-projeto/"},{"data":"2026-09-15","texto":"Quercus issues an unfavourable opinion, citing impacts on a watercourse, use of public mains water and the spreading of digestate on farmland without identified plots.","fonte":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/09/15/biometano-nao-pode-por-em-risco-agua-e-solos-quercus-emite-parecer-desfavoravel-a-unidade-de-abrigada-em-alenquer/"},{"data":"2026-09-15","texto":"About a hundred people protest in Marés, joined by the Mayor of Alenquer; the developer expects the Environmental Impact Statement by mid-2027.","fonte":"https://www.rtvon.pt/2026/09/15/uma-centena-pessoas-em-protesto-contra-central-de-biometano-em-alenquer/"},{"data":"2026-09","texto":"Alenquer Municipal Assembly unanimously approves a proposal declaring the plant of no municipal interest.","fonte":"https://sapo.pt/artigo/assembleia-municipal-de-alenquer-manifesta-se-contra-instalacao-de-central-de-biometano-6ab6ab0bc5a3f84d7f57a258"}],"contexto":"Gás da Terra wants to build a 20.5 million euro biomethane plant in Marés, about 500 metres from homes in Abrigada, in the municipality of Alenquer, to process about 84,000 tonnes of farm waste a year."},"almaraz":{"corpo":"<p>Spain's Ministry for Ecological Transition renewed the operating licence for Units I and II of the Almaraz Nuclear Power Plant, in Cáceres, in the Tagus river basin, about 100 kilometres from the Portuguese border, until June 2030. The decision follows a formal request for the extension made in October 2025 by the plant's three owners, Iberdrola, Endesa and Naturgy.</p>\n<p>The gradual shutdown of the two reactors, operating since the early 1980s, had been scheduled for November 2027 (Unit I) and October 2028 (Unit II), under a protocol already agreed between the companies and the Spanish state. The movement \"Alargar as Nucleares, Não Obrigado\" (\"Extend Nuclear Plants, No Thanks\"), which brings together Adenex, Ecologistas en Acción and Greenpeace, calls the extension \"illegal\" for breaking that agreement.</p>\n<p>The Iberian Energy Observatory, which brings together Portuguese and Spanish associations, announced it will go to court \"as soon as possible\" against the decision, with the case to be filed in Spain by Adenex. The associations warn that extending Almaraz could also jeopardise the shutdown schedule for Spain's other nuclear plants.</p>","fontes":[["O Mirante","https://omirante.pt/nacional/2026-08-14-associacoes-avancam-para-tribunal-contra-prolongamento-do-funcionamento-da-central-de-almaraz-3acf4579"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/08/14/associacoes-avancam-para-tribunal-contra-prolongamento-do-funcionamento-da-central-nuclear-de-almaraz/"],["DN","https://www.dn.pt/internacional/associaes-avanam-para-tribunal-contra-prolongamento-do-funcionamento-da-central-de-almaraz"],["Infobae (Spain)","https://www.infobae.com/espana/agencias/2026/08/16/ecologistas-extremadura-recurre-la-orden-de-prorroga-de-la-central-nuclear-de-almaraz/"]],"stat":"Licence extended to 2030","link":"https://omirante.pt/nacional/2026-08-14-associacoes-avancam-para-tribunal-contra-prolongamento-do-funcionamento-da-central-de-almaraz-3acf4579","linkL":"Read on O Mirante"},"talude-militar-loures":{"corpo":"<p>Talude Militar was born in the 1980s, when Cape Verdean and São Tomean families working in construction around Lisbon began self-building homes on land in Loures, with no access to formal housing. More than 40 years on, the neighbourhood was never integrated or resolved by successive municipal governments.</p>\n<p>On July 14, 2025, Loures City Council launched a large-scale demolition operation targeting 64 structures where 161 people lived. 55 homes were demolished in two days; displaced families spent the night in tents and a church. On the third day, a court injunction filed by 14 residents led the Lisbon Administrative Court to suspend the operation.</p>\n<p>A year later, in July 2026, the deadlock remains: the council has demolished 88 homes since the operation began, but 23 are still protected by collective injunctions, and the Public Prosecutor's Office has opened an inquiry into the demolitions. None of the proceedings has reached a final outcome. Loures City Council has contested the court suspension.</p>\n<p>In the same municipality, the Santa Iria da Azóia neighbourhood, also mostly São Tomean, faced a 48-hour demolition notice in December 2024, later suspended at Social Security's request. The Portuguese press treats these cases as a housing crisis. But the pattern, decades of basic infrastructure denied and eviction without a housing alternative for racialized communities of African origin, is also environmental racism: a term rarely used in Portugal to describe a well-documented reality.</p>","fontes":[["Público (40-year-old neighbourhood)","https://www.publico.pt/2025/07/23/local/noticia/talude-militar-bairro-loures-nasceu-clandestino-ha-40-anos-resolveu-2141394"],["Observador (deadlock, Jul. 2026)","https://observador.pt/2026/07/14/vida-justa-faz-acusacoes-ao-presidente-da-camara-impasse-judicial-mantem-dezenas-de-barracas-em-pe-no-talude-militar-em-loures/"],["RTP (families in tents)","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/pais/bairro-do-talude-familias-desalojadas-passam-noite-em-tendas-e-igreja_n1669173"],["Renascença (court suspends)","https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2025/07/15/tribunal-impede-camara-de-loures-de-demolir-habitacoes-no-bairro-do-talude/432785/"],["Lisboa Para Pessoas (Santa Iria da Azóia)","https://lisboaparapessoas.pt/2024/12/16/despejo-em-loures-cerca-de-100-pessoas-sem-alternativa-habitacional/"],["AbrilAbril (Santa Iria da Azóia, follow-up)","https://www.abrilabril.pt/local/despejo-em-loures-continua-suspenso-mas-moradores-temem-janeiro"]],"stat":"88 homes demolished since July 2025 · 23 under court injunction · a year of legal deadlock","link":"https://www.publico.pt/2025/07/23/local/noticia/talude-militar-bairro-loures-nasceu-clandestino-ha-40-anos-resolveu-2141394","linkL":"Read on Público"},"barragem-pisao":{"corpo":"<p>The Pisão Dam, in the municipality of Crato (Alto Alentejo), budgeted at about 222 million euros, would submerge the village of Pisão and requires felling tens of thousands of holm and cork oaks.</p>","fontes":[["Público: Obras da Barragem do Pisão voltam a ficar suspensas","https://www.publico.pt/2026/05/18/local/noticia/obras-barragem-pisao-voltam-ficar-suspensas-2175113"],["Público: Autarcas dizem que tribunal levantou suspensão das obras da Barragem do Pisão","https://www.publico.pt/2026/01/31/azul/noticia/autarcas-tribunal-levantou-suspensao-obras-barragem-pisao-2162956"],["Renascença: Ambientalistas requerem em tribunal paragem das obras na Barragem do Pisão","https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2026/03/20/ambientalistas-requerem-em-tribunal-paragem-das-obras-na-barragem-do-pisao/463818/"],["Agroportal: Questão processual implica nova suspensão das obras da Barragem do Pisão","https://www.agroportal.pt/questao-processual-implica-nova-suspensao-das-obras-da-barragem-do-pisao/"],["SPEA / C7 coalition: Pisão dam is not in the public interest, say 7 national environmental organisations (31 Oct 2024) (in Portuguese)","https://spea.pt/imprensa/12819/"],["Rádio Campanário: Environmental NGOs against the Pisão dam (31 Oct 2024) (in Portuguese)","https://www.radiocampanario.com/organizacoes-nao-governamentais-de-ambiente-contra-barragem-do-pisao-nao-tem-interesse-publico/"],["GEOTA, 23 Sep 2026: Environment Ministry's statements in Parliament on the Pisão dam call the democratic rule of law into question (in Portuguese)","https://www.geota.pt/blogs/declaracoes-do-ministerio-do-ambiente-e-energia-no-parlamento-sobre-barragem-do-pisao-poem-em-causa-o-estado-de-direito-democratico"],["Linhas de Elvas / Lusa, 25 Sep 2026: Environmentalists accuse Environment Minister of trying to influence the courts over Pisão (in Portuguese)","https://linhasdeelvas.pt/2026/09/25/ambientalistas-acusam-ministra-do-ambiente-de-querer-influenciar-tribunais-sobre-pisao/"],["Rádio Portalegre, 24 Sep 2026: NGOs warn of the impact of the minister's statements on the Pisão dam case (in Portuguese)","https://radioportalegre.pt/onga-alertam-para-impacto-das-declaracoes-da-ministra-no-processo-da-barragem-do-pisao/"]],"stat":"Over 220 million euros; only 1% of volume for public supply","link":"https://www.publico.pt/2026/05/18/local/noticia/obras-barragem-pisao-voltam-ficar-suspensas-2175113","linkL":"See Público report →","cronologia":[{"data":"2024-10-31","texto":"Seven environmental organisations (ANP|WWF, FAPAS, GEOTA, LPN, Quercus, SPEA and ZERO) state that the dam is not in the public interest, citing the felling of more than 40,000 holm and cork oaks and changes to the flow of the Seda stream.","fonte":"https://spea.pt/imprensa/12819/"},{"data":"2025","texto":"The Castelo Branco Administrative and Tax Court annuls the Environmental Impact Statement for the main works; the ruling is appealed to the Central Administrative Court of the South.","fonte":"https://linhasdeelvas.pt/2026/09/25/ambientalistas-acusam-ministra-do-ambiente-de-querer-influenciar-tribunais-sobre-pisao/"},{"data":"2025-09","texto":"The Environmental Impact Statement is suspended following the environmental associations' legal action.","fonte":"https://www.agroportal.pt/questao-processual-implica-nova-suspensao-das-obras-da-barragem-do-pisao/"},{"data":"2026-01","texto":"The Castelo Branco court lifts the suspension and works may resume.","fonte":"https://www.publico.pt/2026/01/31/azul/noticia/autarcas-tribunal-levantou-suspensao-obras-barragem-pisao-2162956"},{"data":"2026-03-20","texto":"The environmental associations ask the court to halt the works.","fonte":"https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2026/03/20/ambientalistas-requerem-em-tribunal-paragem-das-obras-na-barragem-do-pisao/463818/"},{"data":"2026-05-08","texto":"The Central Administrative Court of the South overturns the January decision over a procedural error and reinstates the suspension; works stop again.","fonte":"https://www.agroportal.pt/questao-processual-implica-nova-suspensao-das-obras-da-barragem-do-pisao/"},{"data":"2026-09-09","texto":"At a parliamentary hearing, the Minister of Environment and Energy says she may \"ask Parliament for help\" on the dam.","fonte":"https://linhasdeelvas.pt/2026/09/25/ambientalistas-acusam-ministra-do-ambiente-de-querer-influenciar-tribunais-sobre-pisao/"},{"data":"2026-09-23","texto":"Seventeen environmental organisations say those statements undermine the democratic rule of law by suggesting a legislative way around the courts.","fonte":"https://www.geota.pt/blogs/declaracoes-do-ministerio-do-ambiente-e-energia-no-parlamento-sobre-barragem-do-pisao-poem-em-causa-o-estado-de-direito-democratico"}],"contexto":"The Pisão Dam, in the municipality of Crato (Alto Alentejo), budgeted at about 222 million euros, would submerge the village of Pisão and requires felling tens of thousands of holm and cork oaks."},"fernando-pessoa":{"corpo":"<p>The Fernando Pessoa solar plant, by Iberdrola with Prosolia, was presented as Europe's largest solar plant: 1,200 megawatts on about a thousand hectares in São Domingos, Santiago do Cacém, near Sines, requiring the felling of about 1.5 million trees, mostly eucalyptus.</p>","fontes":[["ECO: Association seeks annulment of mega solar plant (6 Dec 2023) (in Portuguese)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2023/12/06/associacao-pede-impugnacao-de-megacentral-solar-junto-ao-centro-da-start-campus/"],["ECO: Environment Agency will contest Public Prosecutor's action against solar plant (26 Mar 2024) (in Portuguese)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2024/03/26/apa-vai-contestar-acao-do-ministerio-publico-contra-central-solar-em-santiago-do-cacem/"],["Observador: Construction of Portugal's largest solar plant stuck in court for over two years (10 Jul 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2026/07/10/construcao-da-maior-central-solar-em-portugal-encravada-ha-mais-de-dois-anos-na-justica-apesar-de-aprovada/"],["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2024/03/24/maior-central-solar-da-europa-travada-pela-justica/"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2024/03/25/sociedade/noticia/associacao-protegealentejo-satisfeita-accao-mp-central-solar-santiago-cacem-2084850"],["Portugal Resident","https://www.portugalresident.com/solar-park-projects-pushed-through-without-transparency/"]],"stat":"1,200 MW · Europe's largest solar plant","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/07/10/construcao-da-maior-central-solar-em-portugal-encravada-ha-mais-de-dois-anos-na-justica-apesar-de-aprovada/","linkL":"Read on Observador","cronologia":[{"data":"2023-01","texto":"The Environment Agency approves the Environmental Impact Statement for the Fernando Pessoa plant, by Iberdrola and Prosolia.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2024/03/24/maior-central-solar-da-europa-travada-pela-justica/"},{"data":"2023-12-04","texto":"ProtegeAlentejo files an action at the Beja Administrative and Tax Court to annul the Environmental Impact Statement, pointing to unfavourable opinions from ICNF, LNEG and the head of the Environment Agency's impact assessment department.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2023/12/06/associacao-pede-impugnacao-de-megacentral-solar-junto-ao-centro-da-start-campus/"},{"data":"2024-01","texto":"The Public Prosecutor brings an action at the Beja Administrative and Tax Court against the environmental licence, for non-compliance with land-use and natural resource protection instruments.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2024/03/24/maior-central-solar-da-europa-travada-pela-justica/"},{"data":"2024-03-26","texto":"The Environment Agency announces it will contest the action and says it has no suspensive effect.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2024/03/26/apa-vai-contestar-acao-do-ministerio-publico-contra-central-solar-em-santiago-do-cacem/"},{"data":"2024-06","texto":"The court rules that the Environmental Impact Statement's effects are suspended, which halts the subsequent permits. The Environment Agency appeals.","fonte":"https://observador.pt/2026/07/10/construcao-da-maior-central-solar-em-portugal-encravada-ha-mais-de-dois-anos-na-justica-apesar-de-aprovada/"},{"data":"2026-07","texto":"According to the Environment Agency, the case is still awaiting a first-instance ruling; construction has not started.","fonte":"https://observador.pt/2026/07/10/construcao-da-maior-central-solar-em-portugal-encravada-ha-mais-de-dois-anos-na-justica-apesar-de-aprovada/"}],"contexto":"The Fernando Pessoa solar plant, by Iberdrola with Prosolia, was presented as Europe's largest solar plant: 1,200 megawatts on about a thousand hectares in São Domingos, Santiago do Cacém, near Sines, requiring the felling of about 1.5 million trees, mostly eucalyptus."},"praias-arrabida":{"corpo":"<p>Since July 2025, a lawsuit (case 4833/25.7T8STB) has been running in the Judicial Court of Setúbal, filed by Palácio da Comenda, S.A., current holder of the Quinta Herdade da Comenda estate, against the Portuguese State and the Portuguese Environment Agency. The company claims private ownership of five beaches, a municipal road and the Comenda picnic park: the beaches of Rasca, Comenda, Rainha, Maria Esguelha and Albarquel.</p>\n<p>The \"Deslarrrguem a Arrábida!\" movement brought together hundreds of people for a march between Setúbal and the Comenda Recreation Park, in protest against the attempted private appropriation and against restrictions on public access to the area.</p>\n<p>The petition delivered to Parliament has gathered enough signatures to be debated in Parliament. The Government and Setúbal City Council have publicly reaffirmed that the beaches are public, trusting the courts to stop the process.</p>","fontes":[["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/19/centenas-de-pessoas-marcham-em-setubal-contra-privatizacao-de-praias-e-acessos-da-arrabida/"],["Esquerda.net","https://www.esquerda.net/artigo/uma-multidao-juntou-se-na-caminhada-para-gritar-deslarrrguem-arrabida/98408"],["SAPO Notícias","https://sapo.pt/artigo/arrabida-governo-reafirma-que-praias-sao-publicas-e-camara-de-setubal-confia-na-justica-para-travar-privatizacao-6a592bb5bbff543e35398909"],["Portugal Resident","https://www.portugalresident.com/pt/Centenas-protestam-contra-a-privatiza%C3%A7%C3%A3o-das-praias-de-Arr%C3%A1bida--enquanto-a-pol%C3%AAmica-sobre-o-acesso-p%C3%BAblico-se-intensifica./"],["ADN Agência de Notícias","https://www.adn-agenciadenoticias.com/2026/06/herdade-da-comenda-reclama-cinco-praias.html"],["Postal","https://postal.pt/nacional/centenas-marcham-em-defesa-de-cinco-praias-e-dos-acessos-da-arrabida/"],["Público: parliamentary debate","https://publico.pt/2026/06/26/local/noticia/peticao-vai-conseguir-privatizacao-praias-arrabida-debatida-parlamento-2179605"],["PT Green: 12,500 signatures","https://jornalptgreen.pt/noticia/peticao-com-mais-de-12-500-assinaturas-pede-debate-parlamentar-sobre-alegada-privatizacao-de-cinco-praias-de-setubal/"]],"stat":"","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/07/19/centenas-de-pessoas-marcham-em-setubal-contra-privatizacao-de-praias-e-acessos-da-arrabida/","linkL":"Read on Observador"},"dessalinizadora-albufeira":{"corpo":"<p>The Algarve Seawater Desalination Plant, under construction next to Praia da Rocha Baixinha in Albufeira, represents an investment of over €100 million, financed through the Recovery and Resilience Plan. The Águas do Algarve project aims to convert an initial 16 million cubic metres of seawater into drinking water per year, potentially rising to 24 million.</p>\n<p>The project has already faced two court injunctions. In 2025, associations linked to the Sustainable Water Platform, including Almargem and A Rocha Portugal, unsuccessfully challenged the length of the public consultation on the Execution Project's Environmental Compliance Report. In April 2026, with construction already under way, Seacliff, the former owner of the expropriated land where the plant is being built, filed a new injunction at the Administrative and Fiscal Court of Loulé, with immediate suspensive effect on construction.</p>\n<p>Fishermen from Albufeira and Quarteira, together with Albufeira's mayor, joined a protest at Praia da Rocha Baixinha, calling for a fuller assessment of the impacts on the sea and local fishing. Despite the opposition, the Environment Minister insists the project will proceed, and Águas do Algarve expects to complete the plant within about two years.</p>","fontes":[["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/05/04/dessalinizadora-no-algarve-alvo-de-mais-uma-providencia-cautelar/"],["Sul Informação","https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2026/07/dessalinizadora-do-algarve-esta-a-avancar-e-devera-estar-concluida-em-dois-anos/"],["The Portugal News","https://www.theportugalnews.com/news/2026-05-04/construction-of-desalination-plant-in-the-algarve-has-been-suspended/1016802"],["Postal","https://postal.pt/algarve/seacliff-denuncia-continuacao-de-obras-na-dessalinizadora-mas-aguas-do-algarve-nega/"]],"stat":"€100+ million","link":"https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2026/07/dessalinizadora-do-algarve-esta-a-avancar-e-devera-estar-concluida-em-dois-anos/","linkL":"Read on Sul Informação"},"mina-borralha":{"corpo":"<p>Minerália wants to reopen the Borralha mines, in Salto (Montalegre), with 15 years of underground mining of tungsten, copper and tin and a new 12-hectare waste heap. The mine lies in Barroso, a FAO Globally Important Agricultural Heritage System, inside the Gerês-Xurés Transboundary Biosphere Reserve and about 2 km from the Venda Nova reservoir, which supplies water to thousands of people in the North, including Braga.</p>","fontes":[["O Minho: Association files lawsuit against environmental assessment of Montalegre mine (9 Jun 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://ominho.pt/associacao-interpoe-acao-judicial-contra-avaliacao-ambiental-da-mina-em-montalegre/"],["RTP: APA gives conditional approval to the Borralha mine (in Portuguese)","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/economia/apa-da-parecer-favoravel-condicionado-a-mina-da-borralha-em-montalegre_n1709827"],["Rádio Regional: Gaps and contradictions in the environmental impact study (in Portuguese)","https://radioregional.pt/lacunas-e-contradicoes-movimento-nao-as-minas-chumba-estudo-de-impacte-ambiental-da-borralha/"],["Diário de Trás-os-Montes: Movement challenges the monitoring committee (in Portuguese)","https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/movimento-nao-as-minas-contesta-criacao-de-comissao-de-acompanhamento-na-borralha"],["Jornal Mapa: The return of the Borralha mines' ghost (in Portuguese)","https://www.jornalmapa.pt/2021/03/30/o-regresso-do-fantasma-das-minas-da-borralha/"],["O Minho: Mine could contaminate the Cávado river (in Portuguese)","https://ominho.pt/camara-de-braga-esta-alerta-e-atenta-a-mina-em-tras-os-montes-que-pode-contaminar-rio-cavado/"],["Povo e Natureza do Barroso Association (in Portuguese)","https://assopnb.wordpress.com/"]],"stat":"653 public consultation submissions","link":"","linkL":"","cronologia":[{"data":"1986","texto":"The Borralha mines close. Since 1902 they had been one of the country's main tungsten centres, employing up to about 2,000 people; waste heaps and contaminated soil and water remain.","fonte":"https://www.jornalmapa.pt/2021/03/30/o-regresso-do-fantasma-das-minas-da-borralha/"},{"data":"2025-10-07","texto":"Public consultation on the environmental impact study for Minerália's project, which receives 653 submissions.","fonte":"https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/economia/apa-da-parecer-favoravel-condicionado-a-mina-da-borralha-em-montalegre_n1709827","dataFim":"2025-11-17"},{"data":"2025-11-10","texto":"The Movimento Não às Minas Montalegre points to gaps in the study: missing data on radioactive metals, weaknesses on the stability of old galleries and a new 12-hectare waste heap.","fonte":"https://radioregional.pt/lacunas-e-contradicoes-movimento-nao-as-minas-chumba-estudo-de-impacte-ambiental-da-borralha/"},{"data":"2026-01-08","texto":"The Environment Agency issues a conditionally favourable opinion on the project, with conditions including the rehousing of residents affected by noise and vibration.","fonte":"https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/economia/apa-da-parecer-favoravel-condicionado-a-mina-da-borralha-em-montalegre_n1709827"},{"data":"2026-04","texto":"The Povo e Natureza do Barroso Association files a lawsuit against the Environmental Impact Statement, on behalf of the Movimento Não às Minas Montalegre, the commons of Caniçó, Linharelhos and Campos and the Iris and APIFC associations.","fonte":"https://ominho.pt/associacao-interpoe-acao-judicial-contra-avaliacao-ambiental-da-mina-em-montalegre/"},{"data":"2026-06-07","texto":"The Movimento Não às Minas contests the monitoring commission set up by Minerália, arguing that this is a State competence.","fonte":"https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/movimento-nao-as-minas-contesta-criacao-de-comissao-de-acompanhamento-na-borralha"}],"contexto":"Minerália wants to reopen the Borralha mines, in Salto (Montalegre), with 15 years of underground mining of tungsten, copper and tin and a new 12-hectare waste heap. The mine lies in Barroso, a FAO Globally Important Agricultural Heritage System, inside the Gerês-Xurés Transboundary Biosphere Reserve and about 2 km from the Venda Nova reservoir, which supplies water to thousands of people in the North, including Braga."},"barroso":{"corpo":"<p>Savannah Resources wants to open an open-pit lithium mine in Covas do Barroso (Boticas), in a farming area classified as a Globally Important Agricultural Heritage System by the FAO. The planned concession covers 593 hectares, with an estimated lifetime of 17 years.</p>","fontes":[["Unidos em Defesa de Covas do Barroso: The threat (in Portuguese)","https://udcb.pt/a-ameaca"],["Unidos em Defesa de Covas do Barroso: statement on the Aarhus Convention (3 Sep 2025) (in Portuguese)","https://udcb.pt/comunicados/portugal-viola-convencao-de-aarhus-na-mina-do-barroso"],["Unidos em Defesa de Covas do Barroso: European Commission sued (5 Feb 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://udcb.pt/comunicados/comissao-europeia-processada-por-decisao-sobre-a-mina-do-barroso"],["Unidos em Defesa de Covas do Barroso: second administrative easement (6 May 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://udcb.pt/comunicados/udcb-repudia-imposicao-de-uma-segunda-servidao-administrativa"],["Unidos em Defesa de Covas do Barroso: breach of the EIS (26 May 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://udcb.pt/comunicados/udcb-denuncia-incumprimento-da-dia-em-covas-do-barroso"],["Ambiente Online: Brussels approves 47 strategic raw materials projects (25 Mar 2025) (in Portuguese)","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/destaques/bruxelas-aprova-47-projetos-de-materias-primas-estrategicas-organizacoes-ambientais-vao-contestar-decisao"],["Diário de Trás-os-Montes: Savannah complies with injunction and suspends works (10 Jun 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/savannah-acata-providencia-cautelar-e-suspende-trabalhos-na-mina-do-barroso"],["ECO: Injunction again suspends works at the Barroso lithium mine (9 Jun 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/06/09/providencia-cautelar-volta-a-suspender-trabalhos-na-mina-de-litio-do-barroso/"],["ECO: Savannah may resume work in Boticas after 20-day suspension (29 Jun 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/06/29/litio-savannah-pode-retomar-trabalhos-em-boticas-apos-suspensao-de-20-dias/"],["Diário de Trás-os-Montes: Covas do Barroso commons concerned about resumption of works (30 Jun 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/baldios-de-covas-do-barroso-preocupados-com-retoma-dos-trabalhos-em-boticas"],["IMVF: Barroso, five days of debate and defence of the territory (13 Aug 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.imvf.org/2026/08/13/barroso-cinco-dias-de-debate-e-defesa-do-territorio/"],["Diário de Trás-os-Montes: Covas do Barroso commons say agreements do not mean social consent (14 Aug 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/baldios-de-covas-do-barroso-dizem-que-acordos-nao-significam-consentimento-social"],["Unidos em Defesa de Covas do Barroso","https://www.facebook.com/udcovasdobarroso/"],["ClientEarth: EU Commission sued by NGOs and communities over Barroso lithium mine decision (5 Feb 2026)","https://www.clientearth.org/latest/press-office/press-releases/eu-commission-sued-by-ngos-and-communities-over-barroso-lithium-mine-decision/"],["Jornal Mapa","https://www.jornalmapa.pt"],["Ambiente Online: Environment Agency issues conditionally favourable EIS for the Barroso lithium mine (31 May 2023) (in Portuguese)","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/apa-emite-declaracao-de-impacte-ambiental-favoravel-condicionada-a-mina-de-litio-do-barroso"],["ECO/Lusa: Barroso lithium project receives favourable Environmental Impact Statement (31 May 2023) (in Portuguese)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2023/05/31/projeto-de-litio-do-barroso-recebe-declaracao-de-impacte-ambiental-favoravel/"],["Jornal Económico: Environmental organisations take action against the European Commission over the Barroso mine (5 Feb 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://jornaleconomico.sapo.pt/noticias/organizacoes-ambientais-movem-acao-contra-comissao-europeia-por-causa-da-mina-do-barroso/"],["ECO: Owner of the Barroso lithium mine completes 31.3 million euro capital increase (23 Sep 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/09/23/dona-da-mina-de-litio-do-barroso-conclui-aumento-de-capital-de-313-milhoes-de-euros/"],["Investing.com: Savannah Resources advances fieldwork at Barroso lithium project (17 Sep 2026)","https://www.investing.com/news/company-news/savannah-resources-advances-fieldwork-at-barroso-lithium-project-93CH-4904846"]],"stat":"8 years of resistance","link":"https://barrososemminas.org","linkL":"Learn more at barrososemminas.org","cronologia":[{"data":"2006","texto":"The Directorate-General for Energy and Geology grants Saibrais the right to mine quartz and feldspar on 120 hectares.","fonte":"https://udcb.pt/a-ameaca"},{"data":"2008","texto":"Saibrais transfers the concession to Imerys Ceramics Portugal, without having carried out any extraction.","fonte":"https://udcb.pt/a-ameaca"},{"data":"2010","texto":"Imerys applies to enlarge the concession from 120 to 542 hectares and to add lithium to the minerals to be mined.","fonte":"https://udcb.pt/a-ameaca"},{"data":"2016","texto":"The enlargement is granted, without prior notice to local institutions.","fonte":"https://udcb.pt/a-ameaca"},{"data":"2017","texto":"The contract passes to Slipstream Resources Portugal, a subsidiary of Savannah Resources.","fonte":"https://udcb.pt/a-ameaca"},{"data":"2018","texto":"The concession holder is renamed Savannah Lithium and starts prospecting; local people halt the works on learning of the extraction project.","fonte":"https://udcb.pt/a-ameaca"},{"data":"2020","texto":"Savannah starts the Environmental Impact Assessment procedure with the Portuguese Environment Agency.","fonte":"https://udcb.pt/a-ameaca"},{"data":"2022-06","texto":"The assessment committee issues an unfavourable opinion, citing \"very significant negative impacts\".","fonte":"https://udcb.pt/a-ameaca"},{"data":"2023-05-31","texto":"The Environment Agency issues a conditionally favourable Environmental Impact Statement: it bans water abstraction from the river Covas and requires compensation for the oak woodland and the red-billed chough and a breeding centre for the freshwater pearl mussel on the river Beça.","fonte":"https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/apa-emite-declaracao-de-impacte-ambiental-favoravel-condicionada-a-mina-de-litio-do-barroso"},{"data":"2024","texto":"At the end of the year, an administrative easement for new prospecting is granted, despite opposition from private owners and the commons.","fonte":"https://udcb.pt/a-ameaca"},{"data":"2025-03-25","texto":"The European Commission includes the Barroso mine among the 47 strategic projects under the Critical Raw Materials Act.","fonte":"https://www.ambienteonline.pt/destaques/bruxelas-aprova-47-projetos-de-materias-primas-estrategicas-organizacoes-ambientais-vao-contestar-decisao"},{"data":"2025-09-03","texto":"UDCB publicises the findings of the Aarhus Convention Compliance Committee (case ACCC/C/2021/186): the Environment Agency, DGEG and CCDR-N withheld information needed for public participation.","fonte":"https://udcb.pt/comunicados/portugal-viola-convencao-de-aarhus-na-mina-do-barroso"},{"data":"2026-02-05","texto":"UDCB and ClientEarth bring an action before the Court of Justice of the European Union against the mine's classification as a \"strategic project\".","fonte":"https://udcb.pt/comunicados/comissao-europeia-processada-por-decisao-sobre-a-mina-do-barroso"},{"data":"2026-05-06","texto":"UDCB rejects the order by the Secretary of State for Energy imposing a second administrative easement on about 228 hectares of private and common land in Covas do Barroso and Romaínho.","fonte":"https://udcb.pt/comunicados/udcb-repudia-imposicao-de-uma-segunda-servidao-administrativa"},{"data":"2026-05-26","texto":"UDCB reports vegetation clearing in early May, outside the period allowed by the Environmental Impact Statement (1 September to 15 March).","fonte":"https://udcb.pt/comunicados/udcb-denuncia-incumprimento-da-dia-em-covas-do-barroso"},{"data":"2026-05-29","texto":"The Mirandela Administrative and Tax Court admits the injunction filed by the Covas do Barroso commons against the Ministry of Environment and Energy and suspends the easement.","fonte":"https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/savannah-acata-providencia-cautelar-e-suspende-trabalhos-na-mina-do-barroso"},{"data":"2026-06-09","texto":"Savannah is notified of the suspension and halts the geotechnical works; according to the company, it is the third injunction against the project.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/06/09/providencia-cautelar-volta-a-suspender-trabalhos-na-mina-de-litio-do-barroso/"},{"data":"2026-06-29","texto":"After 20 days, the Secretary of State for Energy signs a reasoned resolution invoking the public interest and allowing the works to resume.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/06/29/litio-savannah-pode-retomar-trabalhos-em-boticas-apos-suspensao-de-20-dias/"},{"data":"2026-06-30","texto":"The Covas do Barroso commons say the resolution sets \"a deeply worrying precedent\" and point to clearing outside the authorised period.","fonte":"https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/baldios-de-covas-do-barroso-preocupados-com-retoma-dos-trabalhos-em-boticas"},{"data":"2026-08-06","texto":"Sixth Camp in Defence of Barroso, organised by UDCB, with more than 700 participants.","fonte":"https://www.imvf.org/2026/08/13/barroso-cinco-dias-de-debate-e-defesa-do-territorio/","dataFim":"2026-08-10"},{"data":"2026-08-14","texto":"After Savannah announces agreements with other commons, the Covas do Barroso commons state that \"financial compensation, protocols or community benefits do not turn those agreements into social consent\".","fonte":"https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/baldios-de-covas-do-barroso-dizem-que-acordos-nao-significam-consentimento-social"},{"data":"2026-09-17","texto":"Savannah reports having dug 189 geotechnical test pits on site.","fonte":"https://www.investing.com/news/company-news/savannah-resources-advances-fieldwork-at-barroso-lithium-project-93CH-4904846"},{"data":"2026-09-23","texto":"Savannah completes a 31.3 million euro capital increase; according to the company, construction is due to start in the first half of 2027.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/09/23/dona-da-mina-de-litio-do-barroso-conclui-aumento-de-capital-de-313-milhoes-de-euros/"}],"contexto":"Savannah Resources wants to open an open-pit lithium mine in Covas do Barroso (Boticas), in a farming area classified as a Globally Important Agricultural Heritage System by the FAO. The planned concession covers 593 hectares, with an estimated lifetime of 17 years."},"pego-transicao-justa":{"corpo":"<p>Endesa is moving forward with a €700 million project combining solar power, wind power and storage on the site of the former Pego coal-fired power plant, presented as part of the region's \"just transition\". The project already holds National Interest Project (PIN) status.</p>\n<p>Gavião Municipal Council unanimously rejected the project's PIN status. The council says the municipality already has about 2% of its territory covered by renewable energy projects and argues it is becoming a \"sacrifice zone\" serving the energy transition of other regions.</p>\n<p>In July 2026, the site of the former Pego power plant also became one of the locations eligible for a national 300 MVA renewables-plus-storage tender, part of the National Energy Storage Strategy, which also includes Rio Maior, Sines and Santo André. This tender is separate from Endesa's PIN project: of the roughly 600 MW of grid capacity available at the site, about 280 MW are already allocated to Endesa's project, leaving between 300 and 320 MW available for new developers. Tender applications opened on 14 September 2026; the mayor of Abrantes voiced support for the initiative.</p>\n<p>The case adds to other energy and digital projects concentrated in the same area, next to the Pego power plant, including a second large-scale data center already reported (see the Hyperion II case, also documented by Causas de Raiz).</p>","fontes":[["Jornal de Abrantes","https://jornaldeabrantes.sapo.pt/economia/gaviao-contra-estatuto-de-potencial-interesse-nacional-de-transicao-justa-da-central-do-pego"],["Observador/Agência Lusa: Pego power plant site joins national 300 MVA renewables-and-storage tender (3 Jul 2026)","https://observador.pt/2026/07/03/central-do-pego-integra-leilao-nacional-de-300-mva-para-renovaveis-com-armazenamento/"]],"stat":"€700 million investment","link":"https://jornaldeabrantes.sapo.pt/economia/gaviao-contra-estatuto-de-potencial-interesse-nacional-de-transicao-justa-da-central-do-pego","linkL":"Read on Jornal de Abrantes"},"ia-sines":{"corpo":"<p>The announcement of an artificial intelligence gigafactory in Sines is presented as a milestone of \"technological sovereignty\" for the country, but the project carries energy and water needs that are rarely discussed in public.</p>\n<p>Water supply is planned through desalinated seawater, a process that has already triggered a legal dispute over the terms of the concession. The data centre's energy consumption will require building Europe's largest solar plant in the region, involving forest felling in areas that are currently classified.</p>\n<p>Local organizations from the Alentejo coast, including TAMLA, question the real environmental cost of a project presented mainly in economic and geopolitical terms.</p>","fontes":[["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2026/06/17/azul/noticia/edp-guerra-juridica-estado-garantir-agua-mar-sines-2178488"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/especiais/edp-abre-batalha-juridica-com-o-estado-pelo-fornecimento-da-agua-do-mar-em-sines/"],["Jornal de Negócios","https://www.jornaldenegocios.pt/economia/ambiente/detalhe/aguas-de-portugal-da-primeiro-passo-para-a-dessalinizadora-de-sines-prevista-para-2031"],["Sul Informação","https://alentejo.sulinformacao.pt/2023/10/movimentos-protestam-em-sines-e-pedem-travao-na-destruicao-do-litoral-alentejano/"]],"stat":"Europe's largest solar plant","link":"","linkL":""},"montijo-alcochete":{"corpo":"<p>After the Montijo airport project was stopped on environmental grounds, the Government chose the Alcochete firing range as the new site for Lisbon's future airport.</p>\n<p>The new location carries even greater environmental risks: construction threatens over 250,000 cork oaks and overlaps with the Tejo-Sado aquifer, the country's largest underground freshwater reserve.</p>\n<p>Environmental organizations and local associations are calling for a full strategic environmental assessment before any final decision, warning that the impacts may be even more severe than those of the original Montijo project.</p>","fontes":[["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2024/05/14/azul/noticia/alcochete-opcao-problematica-novo-aeroporto-ambientalistas-2090439"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/24/aeroporto-ambientalistas-avisam-que-ha-riscos-para-o-aquifero-e-para-abastecimento-de-agua-a-setubal/"],["O Setubalense","https://osetubalense.com/ultimas/quercus-diz-que-futuro-aeroporto-poe-em-risco-aquifero-e-abastecimento-de-agua"],["Portugal Resident","https://www.portugalresident.com/new-lisbon-airport-will-need-to-divert-water-courses/"]],"stat":"250,000+ cork oaks threatened","link":"","linkL":""},"castelo-bode":{"corpo":"<p>The Amara Village development plans a 50-hectare tourist resort on the shores of the Castelo de Bode reservoir, in Tomar, the country's second-largest freshwater reserve.</p>\n<p>The licensing process moved forward with no Environmental Impact Assessment, despite the scale of the project and its location next to one of the main water supply reserves for the Centre region.</p>\n<p>Local environmental associations and Quercus question the legality of the process, asking for it to be suspended until a full environmental assessment is carried out.</p>\n<p>On 7 July 2026, Quercus expressed \"great concern\" about the effects of Amara Village on the water resources and ecosystems of the Castelo de Bode reservoir: the project covers 50 hectares, 30 of them for construction, with 193 properties, a wastewater treatment plant, access roads and a boat pier, and involves works on sloping ground, tree removal and more boat noise on the water.</p>","fontes":[["Quercus: tourism project at Castelo de Bode reservoir advancing without Environmental Impact Assessment is scandalous (7 Jul 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/07/07/quercus-considera-escandaloso-avanco-de-projeto-turistico-na-albufeira-de-castelo-de-bode-sem-avaliacao-de-impacte-ambiental/"],["Observador/Lusa: Quercus contests luxury tourist village in Tomar advancing without environmental assessment (7 Jul 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2026/07/07/quercus-contesta-avanco-de-aldeamento-turistico-de-luxo-em-tomar-sem-avaliacao-ambiental/"],["Médio Tejo","https://mediotejo.net/quercus-contesta-avanco-de-aldeamento-turistico-de-luxo-em-tomar-sem-avaliacao-ambiental/"],["O Mirante","https://omirante.pt/sociedade/2026-07-18-turismo-de-luxo-na-albufeira-de-castelo-de-bode-levanta-preocupacoes-880d34a9"]],"stat":"50 hectares","link":"","linkL":""},"rio-almansor":{"corpo":"<p>The Almansor River rises near Arraiolos and runs 97 kilometres before flowing into the Sorraia, passing through Montemor-o-Novo, Vendas Novas, Canha and Santo Estêvão. For decades it has received pollutant loads well above the regional average, from urban sewage, intensive agriculture and pig farming, leading Portugal's water authority to rate its quality as \"Below Good\", with no significant change for years.</p>\n<p>In 2024, after a sewage system failure in Montemor-o-Novo, residents along the riverbank organized and founded AMORA, an association run through horizontal, deliberative democracy. That same year, the first ever Water Management Plan for the Almansor was approved in Portugal, and the municipality created its first ever municipal environmental council. AGDA, the sanitation utility, was fined €130,000 for negligence, a decision it has appealed.</p>\n<p>Water tests carried out by residents along the river found high levels of fecal coliforms, excess nutrients and microplastics. AMORA maps pollution sources, takes part in public consultations and mobilizes the community to clean and regenerate the river, aiming to make it swimmable again within five years.</p>","fontes":[["AMORA - The Almansor","https://amoralmansor.pt/o-almansor/"],["Montemor-o-Novo Municipal Council","https://www.cm-montemornovo.pt/comunicado-valorizacao-do-rio-almansor-e-garantia-da-qualidade-da-agua-no-concelho/"],["Spring Prize","https://springprize.org/shortlisted/associacao-de-moradores-do-rio-almansor-amora/"]],"stat":"€130,000 fine against AGDA (under appeal)","link":"https://amoralmansor.pt","linkL":"Learn more at amoralmansor.pt"},"rio-eiriz-meixomil":{"corpo":"<p>A polluting discharge recorded in the early hours of a Sunday in August 2026 in the Eiriz River, next to Meixomil's Urban Park, killed dozens of fish. The Meixomil Parish Council announced it would file a complaint with the competent authorities to determine the source of the contamination.</p>\n<p>The subsequent investigation identified the cause: a malfunction in a clogged sewage collector on Rua da Agra, in the parish of Eiriz, which caused effluent to accidentally overflow into the watercourse. The possibility of intentional or deliberate pollution was ruled out.</p>\n<p>The utility Águas de Paços de Ferreira unblocked the collector and is carrying out a river clean-up operation, including removal of sludge and waste from the discharge.</p>","fontes":[["Imediato (discharge)","https://www.imediato.pt/descarga-poluente-no-rio-eiriz-provoca-morte-de-dezenas-de-peixes-em-meixomil/"],["Imediato (cause)","https://www.imediato.pt/avaria-em-coletor-de-saneamento-na-origem-da-mortalidade-de-peixes-no-rio-eiriz/"],["Novum Canal","https://novumcanal.pt/2026/08/avaria-em-coletor-esteve-na-origem-da-descarga-poluente-no-rio-eiriz-que-provocou-a-morte-a-dezenas-de-peixes/"]],"stat":"Dozens of dead fish · malfunction confirmed, no sign of intentional discharge","link":"https://www.imediato.pt/descarga-poluente-no-rio-eiriz-provoca-morte-de-dezenas-de-peixes-em-meixomil/","linkL":"Read on Imediato"},"sobreiros-tortosendo":{"corpo":"<p>Quercus denounced, in a statement sent to newsrooms on 1 September 2026, Covilhã City Council's intention to fell around 1,400 cork oaks (dozens of them centuries old) to allow the expansion of the Tortosendo Industrial Park, as part of the revision of the Municipal Master Plan (PDM). The environmental group points to two watercourses, three ponds and several springs in the planned area, plus 10 primary residences whose occupants could face expropriation. The denunciation comes days before the end of the PDM revision's public discussion period, which closes on 4 September 2026.</p><p>Quercus questions the need for more industrial land, arguing the current industrial zone \"has half its plots empty or abandoned\", and calls the expansion a \"false pretext\". The group argues that, since it involves a legally protected species, the council must prove the expansion into the cork oak stand is \"the only viable alternative to serve the public interest\" before authorising its removal. Mayor Hélio Fazendeiro confirms this third phase of the industrial park was already planned around 30 years ago, acknowledges the environmental and family concerns, and says the expansion will comply with the law, including replanting trees as happened in earlier phases of the same park.</p>","fontes":[["Observador (Quercus denunciation, in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2026/09/01/quercus-denuncia-abate-de-1-400-sobreiros-para-expansao-de-parque-industrial-na-covilha/"],["Rádio Clube da Covilhã (mayor's response, in Portuguese)","https://radio-covilha.pt/2026/09/noticias/quercus-denuncia-possivel-abate-de-sobreiros-no-tortosendo-camara-garante-cumprimento-da-lei/"],["Greensavers / SAPO Ambiente (in Portuguese)","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/quercus-denuncia-abate-de-1-400-sobreiros-para-expansao-de-parque-industrial-na-covilha/"],["Ambiente Magazine (in Portuguese)","https://www.ambientemagazine.com/quercus-denuncia-abate-de-1-400-sobreiros-para-expansao-do-parque-industrial-do-tortosendo/"]],"stat":"Master plan would fell around 1,400 cork oaks, dozens centuries old","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/09/01/quercus-denuncia-abate-de-1-400-sobreiros-para-expansao-de-parque-industrial-na-covilha/","linkL":"Read the article (in Portuguese) →"},"central-eolica-fronteira":{"corpo":"<p>The Fronteira Wind Farm plans to install 35 wind turbines, with 157.5 MW of installed capacity, in a 5,893-hectare study area across the municipalities of Vimioso and Miranda do Douro. The project is designed as a hybrid with the Picote Hydroelectric Plant, sharing its grid connection point.</p>\n<p>The study area overlaps the Douro Internacional Natural Park and three Natura 2000 Special Conservation Areas. The proposal that was in consultation defined the scope of the future environmental impact study, in other words, what will (or will not) be assessed in depth before licensing.</p>\n<p>Miranda do Douro Municipal Council made the consultation public; it ran on the Participa portal until August 17, 2026. The final scope of the environmental impact study follows next.</p>","fontes":[["Miranda do Douro Municipal Council","https://www.cm-mdouro.pt/municipio/comunicacao/noticias/noticia/consulta-publica-projeto-da-central-eolica-da-fronteira"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/28/central-eolica-da-fronteira-em-vimioso-com-5-893-hectares-em-area-de-estudo/"],["Diário de Trás-os-Montes","https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/central-eolica-da-fronteira-em-vimioso-com-5893-hectares-de-area-de-estudo"]],"stat":"5,893 hectares in the study area","link":"https://www.cm-mdouro.pt/municipio/comunicacao/noticias/noticia/consulta-publica-projeto-da-central-eolica-da-fronteira","linkL":"Read on the Miranda do Douro Council website"},"sobreira":{"corpo":"<p>EDP is preparing, in Pedrógão, in the municipality of Vidigueira, its largest photovoltaic plant in Europe, with construction planned to start in November 2026.</p>\n<p>The project's environmental impact study classifies the impacts on Bonelli's eagle, a threatened species with confirmed presence in the region, and on several protected bat species, as \"very significant\".</p>\n<p>Environmental organizations are asking for the project layout to be revised to preserve flight corridors and hunting areas essential to these species' survival in the region.</p>\n<p>September 2026 update: the project, promoted by Empresa Hidroelétrica do Guadiana (EHG) in partnership with EDP Renováveis, was planned with an installed capacity of 292.6 MVA and estimated annual output of 418 GWh, with marginal effect on Portel municipality. After an initial public consultation, the Portuguese Environment Agency and the Assessment Commission confirmed, in an opinion, very significant negative impacts on Bonelli's eagle and on bats associated with the nationally important Alqueva shelter. In response, the developer reformulated the project under article 16 of Decree-Law 151-B/2013, reducing the direct footprint to 96 hectares, within an 836-hectare property. The reformulated version, dated September 2025, was resubmitted for a new public consultation in 2026.</p>","fontes":[["LPN","https://www.lpn.pt/pt/noticias/estudo-de-impacte-ambiental-da-central-fotovoltaica-da-sobreira-de-baixo-"],["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2024/11/25/vai-nascer-no-alentejo-a-maior-central-fotovoltaica-da-edp-na-europa/"],["Jornal Económico","https://leitor.jornaleconomico.pt/noticia/edp-com-projeto-para-instalar-a-sua-maior-central-solar-europeia-no-alentejo"],["Câmara Municipal de Vidigueira","https://cm-vidigueira.pt/31331/consulta-publica--central-fotovoltaica-da-sobreira-de-baixo"],["SAPO: EDP's solar plant in Vidigueira and Portel reformulated and back in public consultation (in Portuguese)","https://sapo.pt/artigo/central-solar-da-edp-em-vidigueira-e-portel-reformulada-e-novamente-em-consulta-publica-68e53df72061e0b556e91a8c"],["Sul Informação: Vidigueira holds information session on Sobreira de Baixo photovoltaic plant (in Portuguese)","https://alentejo.sulinformacao.pt/2024/12/vidigueira-promove-sessao-de-esclarecimento-sobre-central-fotovoltaica-da-sobreira-de-baixo/"]],"stat":"292.6 MVA · 96 ha direct footprint · impacts on Bonelli's eagle and bats","link":"https://sapo.pt/artigo/central-solar-da-edp-em-vidigueira-e-portel-reformulada-e-novamente-em-consulta-publica-68e53df72061e0b556e91a8c","linkL":"Read on SAPO"},"hidrogenio-sines":{"corpo":"<p>Sines concentrates several National Interest Project (PIN) status projects tied to hydrogen, ammonia and synthetic fuels: Madoqua H2, GreenH2Atlantic, Green Amonia Express, Navigator Green Fuels and MDQ Synfuels. They are part of the 13 projects in the \"chemical and petrochemical\" sector that, according to a 2024 business-press survey, represent the largest share of PIN projects granted in Portugal, alongside tourism.</p>\n<p>There is no public, official and complete list of all PIN projects in Portugal: sector figures come from AICEP statements to the press, not from an open registry. This cluster adds to two other cases already documented by Causas de Raiz in the same area, the AI gigafactory in Sines and the Southwest Wind Farm, both linked to the same pressure on water, energy and land on the Alentejo coast.</p>\n<p>As of this research, we did not identify a citizen organisation specifically monitoring this hydrogen cluster. It is recorded here as an alert, for ongoing monitoring.</p>","fontes":[["ECO: 55 National Interest Projects","https://eco.sapo.pt/2024/08/13/portugal-acompanha-55-projetos-de-potencial-interesse-nacional-maioria-e-de-capital-estrangeiro/"],["ECO: how the Government plans to attract more data centers","https://eco.sapo.pt/descodificador/como-o-governo-planeia-atrair-mais-data-centers-para-portugal/"]],"stat":"5 PIN projects in Sines","link":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2024/08/13/portugal-acompanha-55-projetos-de-potencial-interesse-nacional-maioria-e-de-capital-estrangeiro/","linkL":"Read on ECO"},"biometano-tougues-vila-do-conde":{"corpo":"<p>Capwatt, a Sonae group company, plans to build a biomethane production unit in the parish of Tougues, in the municipality of Vila do Conde. The project has already been recognised by the Government as a Project of National Interest (PIN) and is at the stage of technical assessments and studies.</p><p>The application reached Vila do Conde City Council in December 2025 and, in May 2026, the council issued a favourable decision on the Prior Information Request. The council told the Lusa news agency that this decision concerns only the planning viability of the land and not the licensing of the activity, which depends on opinions and authorisations from the Directorate-General for Energy and Geology (DGEG) and the Portuguese Environment Agency (APA); according to JN, as cited by Viva Porto, also from the Northern Regional Coordination Commission (CCDR Norte).</p><p>According to Jornal de Notícias, as cited by Viva Porto, the unit would stand about 20 metres from some homes and from a care home where 16 elderly people live, some with respiratory problems. Residents fear bad smells, gases, flies, noise, heavy lorry traffic, soil contamination and falling property values, and point to National Agricultural Reserve land nearby. Many say they do not oppose biomethane production as such, but its location so close to homes.</p><p>A public information session with the company, organised by Tougues Parish Council, was scheduled for 28 September 2026 and was postponed with no new date; the parish council cited a lack of logistical conditions, and its president told JN that it was the company that decided to postpone. That same evening, around two hundred residents gathered outside Tougues Church in protest, and they are considering further actions at the City Council and at Sonae.</p>","fontes":[["O Minho / Lusa, 25 Sep 2026: Company wants to produce biomethane in Vila do Conde (in Portuguese)","https://ominho.pt/empresa-quer-produzir-biometano-em-vila-do-conde/"],["Mais/Semanário, 28 Sep 2026: Tougues parish council postpones information session on biomethane plant (in Portuguese)","https://maissemanario.pt/junta-tougues-adia-sessao-de-esclarecimento-sobre-central-de-biometano/"],["Mais/Semanário, 28 Sep 2026: Residents protest in Tougues against biomethane plant (in Portuguese)","https://maissemanario.pt/populares-manifestam-se-em-tougues-contra-instalacao-de-central-de-biometano/"],["Viva Porto, 29 Sep 2026: Around 200 residents protest against biomethane plant in Vila do Conde (in Portuguese)","https://viva-porto.pt/cerca-de-200-moradores-protestam-contra-central-de-biometano-em-vila-do-conde/"]],"stat":"About 20 m from the nearest homes (according to JN) · around 200 protesters","link":"https://viva-porto.pt/cerca-de-200-moradores-protestam-contra-central-de-biometano-em-vila-do-conde/","linkL":"Read on Viva Porto"},"azambuja-dc":{"corpo":"<p>French company Neoen requested National Interest Project (PIN) status from AICEP for a data center valued at €2 billion, to be built in Alcoentre, a parish within Azambuja municipality.</p>\n<p>In July 2026, Azambuja Municipal Council gave an unfavourable opinion on the request, citing missing environmental, noise and landscape impact studies. The council's opinion is not binding: the final decision on PIN status is made at the national level, by AICEP, and the process remains open.</p>\n<p>The case illustrates a structural tension in the PIN regime: it speeds up licensing from Lisbon, even when the municipality where the project would be built objects for lack of environmental information.</p>","fontes":[["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/07/31/camara-de-azambuja-trava-estatuto-pin-para-data-center-de-2-mil-milhoes-de-euros/"]],"stat":"€2 billion investment","link":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/07/31/camara-de-azambuja-trava-estatuto-pin-para-data-center-de-2-mil-milhoes-de-euros/","linkL":"Read on ECO"},"lagoas-acores":{"corpo":"<p>Lagoa das Furnas and Lagoa das Sete Cidades, two of São Miguel Island's landscape landmarks, face a growing eutrophication process, linked to the intensification of dairy production in the surrounding watersheds.</p>\n<p>Excess fertilizer and animal waste run off into the lakes, feeding algae blooms that reduce the oxygen available in the water and threaten local aquatic ecosystems.</p>\n<p>The problem is structural: it requires changes in farming practices across the whole watershed, not just isolated measures at the lakes themselves, and involves balancing an economic activity central to the Azores with the preservation of two of its most emblematic landscapes.</p>","fontes":[["Açoriano Oriental","https://www.acorianooriental.pt/noticia/regiao-destaca-esforco-no-combate-a-eutrofizacao-nas-lagoas-294433"],["Diário de Notícias","https://www.dn.pt/lusa/governo-dos-acores-destaca-esforco-no-combate-a-eutrofizacao-nas-lagoas-10179507.html"]],"stat":"Two lakes affected","link":"","linkL":""},"monte-rei":{"corpo":"<p>The Monte Rei resort, in Vila Nova de Cacela, wants to build a second 56-hectare golf course, in an Algarve region that has faced critical water scarcity for several consecutive years.</p>\n<p>ZERO called the project \"incompatible with the water emergency\" the region faces, questioning the priority given to water use for recreational purposes over the water supply needs of local residents.</p>\n<p>The licensing process received an unfavourable opinion, but the developer keeps the project under review, with the possibility of appealing the decision.</p>\n<p>On 15 March 2024, the Algarve Regional Coordination and Development Commission (CCDR Algarve) decided that the detailed design of the new golf course \"does not comply\" with the Environmental Impact Statement. Among the grounds is the failure to meet the condition requiring a declaration of essential public interest for felling cork oak and holm oak stands: the project foresees cutting down 264 cork and holm oaks. The decision also notes that two protected plant species were identified on site, Picris willkommii, listed as \"endangered\", and Ruscus aculeatus, and that the flora survey submitted does not ensure the detection of all natural values of interest potentially present.</p>","fontes":[["Sul Informação","https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2024/02/novo-campo-de-golfe-no-algarve-e-projeto-incompativel-com-a-emergencia-hidrica-que-se-vive/"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2024/02/01/local/noticia/seca-campo-golfe-algarve-apa-impoe-rega-aguas-residuais-2078793"],["Postal","https://postal.pt/nacional/novo-campo-de-golfe-em-vila-real-de-santo-antonio-so-avanca-se-rega-for-com-agua-tratada/"],["CCDR Algarve: Decision on the environmental compliance of the detailed design, Monte Rei golf course expansion (non-compliant, 15 Mar 2024) (in Portuguese)","https://www.ccdr-alg.pt/site/sites/default/files/inline-files/20240704_MteReidcape-anexos.pdf"],["Assessment Committee (CCDR Algarve, Environment Agency, ICNF, Cultural Heritage, VRSA Council): opinion on the environmental compliance of the Monte Rei detailed design (in Portuguese)","https://siaia.apambiente.pt/AIADOC/RECAPE549/parecer%20da%20ca%20%20recape%20monte%20rei202431512254.pdf"]],"stat":"56 hectares","link":"","linkL":""},"linha-atalaia-cruzeiro-concavada":{"corpo":"<p>The Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA no. 3736) of the Atalaia-Torre das Vargens power line and the Cruzeiro-Concavada line branch, promoted by Endesa Generación Portugal, was in public consultation until August 18, 2026. These lines are part of the so-called Pego Cluster, the set of four groups of solar, wind and storage projects with which Endesa occupies the former Pego coal-fired power plant site, across the municipalities of Abrantes, Gavião and Ponte de Sor.</p>\n<p>CHIRO, a Portuguese bat conservation association, objected to a reformulation of the related Atalaia-Concavada solar project, asking for monitoring of bat populations before, during and after construction, and for the preservation of the main feeding areas and shelters identified.</p>\n<p>The case adds to two others already documented by Causas de Raiz in the same area, next to the Pego power plant: the Hyperion II data center and the \"Just Transition\" project contested by Gavião Council.</p>","fontes":[["Gavião Municipal Council","https://cm-gaviao.pt/apa-consulta-publica-projeto-solar-de-atalaia-concavada-e-linhas-eletricas-de-interligacao-220kv-via-se-comenda-e-cruzeiro/"],["Public Consultation Report, EIA no. 3736 (APA)","https://siaia.apambiente.pt/AIADOC/AIA3736/rel_cp202615102631.pdf"]],"stat":"EIA no. 3736","link":"https://cm-gaviao.pt/apa-consulta-publica-projeto-solar-de-atalaia-concavada-e-linhas-eletricas-de-interligacao-220kv-via-se-comenda-e-cruzeiro/","linkL":"Read on the Gavião Council website"},"movimento-meco-livre":{"corpo":"<p>Four tourist developments (Etosoto, Idiluz, Pinhal da Prata and Turimeco's Pinhal do Atlântico aparthotel, with 411 units and 1,168 beds) plan more than 3,000 beds next to the villages of Meco and Azóia, in Sesimbra, all within the Arrábida/Espichel Natura 2000 Special Area of Conservation and one inside the Arrábida Natural Park.</p>","fontes":[["Petição Pública: Extreme water scarcity demands revocation of large tourist developments (18 Jul 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=aguaemsesimbra"],["RTP: Meco Livre Movement denounces stone pine felling","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/pais/movimento-meco-livre-denuncia-abate-de-pinheiro-manso_v1726496"],["Diário do Distrito: Meco Livre Movement raises alarm over 'one of the biggest environmental attacks in Sesimbra'","https://diariodistrito.sapo.pt/movimento-meco-livre-lanca-alerta-sobre-um-dos-maiores-atentados-ambientais-em-sesimbra/"],["Diário do Distrito: Sesimbra council clarifies population on Meco developments","https://diariodistrito.sapo.pt/sesimbra-municipio-esclarece-populacao-sobre-empreendimentos-no-meco/"],["Public Petition: SOS Meco: No to mega projects! (closed)","https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT125714"],["Facebook: O Meco Livre","https://www.facebook.com/omecolivre/"],["Instagram: @mecolivre","https://www.instagram.com/mecolivre/"],["Diário de Notícias: Meco residents oppose 1,832 more beds in tourism units (in Portuguese)","https://www.dn.pt/local/turismo-populacao-do-meco-contra-mais-1832-camas-na-aldeia-em-unidades-turisticas-13751017.html"],["MAGG: Aldeia do Meco launches petition against hotel projects (in Portuguese)","https://magg.sapo.pt/atualidade/atualidade-nacional/artigos/aldeia-meco-lanca-peticao-projetos-hoteleiros"],["Notícias ao Minuto: new petition against large hotel projects in Aldeia do Meco (in Portuguese)","https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/casa/1752440/ha-uma-nova-peticao-nao-a-grandes-projetos-hoteleiros-aldeia-do-meco"]],"stat":"14,683 signatures on the SOS Meco petition · new active petition against salinization risk","link":"https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=aguaemsesimbra","linkL":"See the water petition","cronologia":[{"data":"1998","texto":"The Meco tourist developments are included in Sesimbra's Municipal Master Plan.","fonte":"https://diariodistrito.sapo.pt/sesimbra-municipio-esclarece-populacao-sobre-empreendimentos-no-meco/"},{"data":"2021-04","texto":"Residents launch the petition \"No to Large Hotel Projects in Meco Village\", against four Turimeco projects with 1,832 beds, conditionally approved by regional authorities.","fonte":"https://www.dn.pt/local/turismo-populacao-do-meco-contra-mais-1832-camas-na-aldeia-em-unidades-turisticas-13751017.html"},{"data":"2025-05-11","texto":"Sesimbra Council states that the developments comply with the master plan and have favourable environmental impact assessments from CCDR-LVT, ICNF and the Environment Agency.","fonte":"https://diariodistrito.sapo.pt/sesimbra-municipio-esclarece-populacao-sobre-empreendimentos-no-meco/"},{"data":"2025-06","texto":"Movimento Meco Livre launches the \"SOS Meco\" petition: the four projects (Etosoto, Idiluz, Pinhal da Prata and Pinhal do Atlântico), with over 3,000 beds, are going ahead without a cumulative environmental impact assessment.","fonte":"https://diariodistrito.sapo.pt/movimento-meco-livre-lanca-alerta-sobre-um-dos-maiores-atentados-ambientais-em-sesimbra/"},{"data":"2026-02-24","texto":"The \"SOS Meco\" petition is delivered to Parliament with 14,683 signatures.","fonte":"https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT125714"},{"data":"2026-03","texto":"The movement reports the felling of stone pines at Herdade do Cabeço da Flauta; ICNF replies that no authorisation was needed as it is private land outside protected areas.","fonte":"https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/pais/movimento-meco-livre-denuncia-abate-de-pinheiro-manso_v1726496"},{"data":"2026-07-18","texto":"A new petition calls for the embargo and revocation of the licences of Sesimbra's large tourist developments, citing Environment Agency data on extreme water scarcity and the risk of salinisation.","fonte":"https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=aguaemsesimbra"}],"contexto":"Four tourist developments (Etosoto, Idiluz, Pinhal da Prata and Turimeco's Pinhal do Atlântico aparthotel, with 411 units and 1,168 beds) plan more than 3,000 beds next to the villages of Meco and Azóia, in Sesimbra, all within the Arrábida/Espichel Natura 2000 Special Area of Conservation and one inside the Arrábida Natural Park."},"royal-china-clay-serra-del-rei":{"corpo":"<p>Mining concession C-185 \"Royal China Clay\", awarded to Motamineral – Minerais Industriais, S.A., aims to extract around 101 hectares of kaolinitic sand and clay across three sites near Serra d'El-Rei, in the municipality of Peniche, with an on-site washing plant. The extracted material is destined for the ceramic-paste factory of MCS – Mota Ceramic Solutions. Projected annual output is around 569,100 tonnes (31,800 tonnes of kaolin, 270,000 of washed sand and 267,300 of common clay), under a two-decade state concession.</p><p>The public consultation on the environmental impact study ran from 22 July to 1 September 2026. According to Quercus, the concession would affect 471 of the 662 cork oaks in the area, with compensation planned for just 300 new specimens (which the group calls \"derisory\") as well as nine vulnerable animal species, a wet-heathland habitat and the native plant Drosophyllum lusitanicum.</p><p>The Óbidos and Peniche municipal councils, the Atouguia da Baleia, Peniche and Serra d'El-Rei parish councils, Quercus and the Portuguese Association of Landscape Architects all issued unfavourable opinions on the project. The Left Bloc questioned the government about the process on 3 September.</p><p>On 11 September 2026, the council of the Oeste Intermunicipal Community (OesteCIM), grouping 12 municipalities in the region, decided to formally oppose the project and asked the Portuguese Environment Agency for an unfavourable Environmental Impact Declaration, calling it \"incompatible with the environmental and territorial support capacity of the surrounding area\". OesteCIM points to errors in the impact study regarding distances to nearby homes (the study states 4 km, when houses actually stand 20, 150 and 450 metres from the site), and warns of risk to 24 groundwater catchments and the São Domingos reservoir, near which a sand-washing plant is planned. The council also estimates the mine would create only 12 direct jobs, against the environmental and traffic costs (11 trucks per hour projected) for the region. Peniche's mayor announced he would request meetings with the Environment Minister and APA.</p>","fontes":[["DN: Óbidos e Peniche contestam exploração mineira de caulino e argila a céu aberto","https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/bidos-e-peniche-contra-explorao-mineira-de-caulino-e-argila-a-cu-aberto"],["Quercus: Quercus insta a CIM Oeste a posicionar-se contra exploração mineira em Peniche","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/28/exploracao-mineira-peniche/"],["Observador: Bloco de Esquerda questiona Governo sobre projeto de mina de caulino para Peniche","https://observador.pt/2026/09/03/bloco-de-esquerda-questiona-governo-sobre-projeto-de-mina-de-caulino-para-peniche/"],["Região de Leiria: Câmaras de Peniche e Óbidos contestam exploração mineira em Serra d'El-Rei","https://www.regiaodeleiria.pt/2026/08/camaras-de-peniche-e-obidos-contestam-exploracao-mineira-em-serra-del-rei/"],["Observador: Arquitetos paisagistas chumbam mina de caulino em Peniche","https://observador.pt/2026/09/01/arquitetos-paisagistas-chumbam-mina-de-caulino-em-peniche-abate-de-sobreiros-sem-compensacao-e-lacuna-mais-consequente/"],["Observador/Lusa news agency: Municípios do Oeste pedem declaração ambiental desfavorável para mina de caulino (11 Sep 2026, in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2026/09/11/municipios-do-oeste-pedem-declaracao-ambiental-desfavoravel-para-mina-de-caulino/"]],"stat":"471 of 662 cork oaks affected, compensation of only 300 new trees","link":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/28/exploracao-mineira-peniche/","linkL":"See Quercus's position →"},"mina-gaviao-aljustrel":{"corpo":"<p>The Gavião mine project represents a total investment of around 250 million euros by Almina – Minas do Alentejo, involving the construction of a new underground mine next to the existing Aljustrel mine, reusing the current processing plant and other facilities. The company plans to extract around 1.5 million tonnes of ore per year, mostly copper, but also zinc, plus smaller quantities of sulphur, iron, lead, silver and gold. If it goes ahead, the investment is expected to create around 150 direct and indirect jobs and extend operations at the Aljustrel mines until 2050.</p><p>Once local processing is complete, the project plans to export around 85,000 tonnes of copper and zinc concentrates a year by truck, through the ports of Setúbal and Huelva, in Spain, despite a rail branch line that historically served Aljustrel's ore transport, currently deactivated.</p><p>The environmental association ZERO issued an unfavourable opinion on the project during the public consultation, which closed on 31 August 2026, calling for the process to be rejected. Among the reasons cited: the environmental impact study does not properly assess a rail transport alternative for the ore, even though that was the historical solution for Aljustrel for decades; and the project does not present a defined destination for the millions of tonnes of waste (tailings and processing rejects) that will be produced from 2031 onward, once the capacity of existing waste piles runs out.</p>","fontes":[["Observador (special report): 250-million-euro project extends the life of the Aljustrel Mines, but with the rail branch deactivated the ore leaves by truck (in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/especiais/projeto-de-250-milhoes-estica-vida-das-minas-de-aljustrel-mas-com-ramal-ferroviario-desativado-minerio-sai-de-camiao/"],["Observador: ZERO calls for rejection of Almina's project for the Gavião mine in Aljustrel (in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2026/09/02/zero-defende-chumbo-do-projeto-da-almina-para-mina-do-gaviao-em-aljustrel/"],["Ambiente Magazine: New Aljustrel mine does not meet conditions for approval, says ZERO (in Portuguese)","https://www.ambientemagazine.com/nova-mina-de-aljustrel-nao-reune-condicoes-para-aprovacao-considera-zero/"],["Notícias ao Minuto: Investment puts Aljustrel mine \"at the forefront of mining\" (in Portuguese)","https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/3006072/investimento-coloca-mina-de-aljustrel-na-linha-da-frente-da-mineracao"]],"stat":"250 million euros · 1.5 million tonnes of ore/year · around 150 jobs expected","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/09/02/zero-defende-chumbo-do-projeto-da-almina-para-mina-do-gaviao-em-aljustrel/","linkL":"Read on Observador"},"cais-carga-sines":{"corpo":"<p>The Environmental Impact Study for the new General Cargo Dock at the Port of Sines, a €90 million investment promoted by the Administration of the Ports of Sines and the Algarve, sets out \"dual\" civil and military use requirements for the infrastructure.</p>\n<p>The Left Bloc questioned the government about the terms, scale and timeline of any military use, and whether the new dock is part of a wider strategy linking it to NATO's logistics network. The port authority denies a permanent military installation.</p>\n<p>Iniciativa Cidadã, a Sines residents' group led by Eugénia Santa Bárbara and Bruno Candeias, organised a public meeting on 4 September 2026 at the Sines Fire Station, arguing there had not been enough public information before the Environmental Impact Assessment's public consultation.</p>\n<p>According to the non-technical summary of the Environmental Impact Study, in public consultation on the Participa portal until 9 September 2026, the project's most significant impact on ecological systems occurs during construction, \"with the destruction of marine habitats and disturbance of benthic species\", and during operation there will be a risk of exotic marine species spreading with increased shipping traffic; the study considers these effects negative but controllable with appropriate measures. On 24 September 2026, according to Lusa, ZERO warned that the formal separation between procedures must not lead to underestimating cumulative impacts on marine habitats.</p>","fontes":[["Diário de Notícias (in Portuguese)","https://www.dn.pt/pol%C3%ADtica/be-questiona-governo-se-novo-cais-de-sines-far-parte-da-rede-logstica-da-nato"],["Sul Informação (in Portuguese)","https://alentejo.sulinformacao.pt/2026/09/possivel-utilizacao-militar-do-novo-cais-do-porto-de-sines-preocupa-cidadaos"],["Esquerda.net (in Portuguese)","https://www.esquerda.net/artigo/bloco-contra-cais-militar-em-sines/98744"],["Participa.pt (public consultation)","https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/novo-cais-de-carga-geral-do-porto-de-sines"],["Environmental Impact Study of the new general cargo pier at the Port of Sines: non-technical summary (EIA 3931) (in Portuguese)","https://siaia.apambiente.pt/AIADOC/AIA3931/t24003_eia_novo_cais_carga_sines_v00_rnt202672715911.pdf"],["SAPO/Lusa: ZERO wants offshore wind to be the priority for the new Sines pier (24 Sep 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://sapo.pt/artigo/zero-quer-eolica-offshore-como-prioridade-no-novo-cais-de-sines-6ab535571c8a1615618914d4"]],"stat":"€90 million · \"dual\" use","link":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/novo-cais-de-carga-geral-do-porto-de-sines","linkL":"🗳 View the public consultation (closed) →"},"eolico-sudoeste-sines":{"corpo":"<p>Hyperion Renewables Sines wants to build the Southwest Wind Farm between Santiago do Cacém and Cercal do Alentejo: 23 to 31 turbines, 138 MW and a battery system, over a study area of 1,098.4 hectares, to supply the Sines data centre.</p>","fontes":[["Quercus","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/08/megaprojeto-eolico-em-santiago-do-cacem-ao-servico-da-ia-quercus-alerta-para-impactos-ambientais-subavaliados/"],["Executive Digest","https://executivedigest.sapo.pt/parque-eolico-com-23-aerogeradores-em-santiago-do-cacem-em-consulta-publica/"],["Rádio Campanário: RENOVAR Santiago do Cacém","https://www.radiocampanario.com/renovar-santiago-do-cacem-critica-projeto-do-parque-eolico-do-sudoeste-e-exige-maior-envolvimento-das-populacoes/"],["Rádio Campanário: underassessed impacts","https://www.radiocampanario.com/associacao-ambientalista-alerta-para-subavaliacao-de-impactos-ambientais-de-parque-eolico/"]],"stat":"1,098 hectares · up to 31 turbines","link":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/08/megaprojeto-eolico-em-santiago-do-cacem-ao-servico-da-ia-quercus-alerta-para-impactos-ambientais-subavaliados/","linkL":"","cronologia":[{"data":"2026-08-08","texto":"Quercus warns that the consultation document labels as \"insignificant\" impacts such as the destruction of cork oak woodland and heath, bird and bat deaths and effects on agricultural and ecological reserves.","fonte":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/08/megaprojeto-eolico-em-santiago-do-cacem-ao-servico-da-ia-quercus-alerta-para-impactos-ambientais-subavaliados/"},{"data":"2026-08","texto":"The RENOVAR Santiago do Cacém movement contests the project, criticises holding the consultation during the holidays and calls for a study of the cumulative impacts of the region's energy megaprojects.","fonte":"https://www.radiocampanario.com/renovar-santiago-do-cacem-critica-projeto-do-parque-eolico-do-sudoeste-e-exige-maior-envolvimento-das-populacoes/"},{"data":"2026-08-18","texto":"The public consultation on the scoping proposal for the environmental impact study closes.","fonte":"https://executivedigest.sapo.pt/parque-eolico-com-23-aerogeradores-em-santiago-do-cacem-em-consulta-publica/"}],"contexto":"Hyperion Renewables Sines wants to build the Southwest Wind Farm between Santiago do Cacém and Cercal do Alentejo: 23 to 31 turbines, 138 MW and a battery system, over a study area of 1,098.4 hectares, to supply the Sines data centre."},"parque-natural-arrabida":{"corpo":"<p>The Arrábida Natural Park protects 12,328 hectares of limestone hills by the sea, between Setúbal, Palmela and Sesimbra. Quarries now cover 323 hectares, double the 1976 area, and built-up land inside the park has grown by about 500% since the 1960s. Quarrying, building and tourism press on the same territory; some of these conflicts have their own case file, such as Meco Livre and the Outão Fort.</p>","fontes":[["Arrábida - Natureza e Comunidade: \"A Arrábida e o Progresso\"","https://www.arrabida.org/a-arrabida-e-o-progresso/"],["Resolution Bill No. 694/XV/1st, PCP: Portuguese Parliament","https://www.pcp.pt/salvaguarda-dos-valores-naturais-do-parque-natural-da-arrabida"],["ZERO: Secil quarry expansion","https://zero.ong/noticias/zero-considera-que-expansao-da-pedreiras-da-secil-na-arrabida-e-impossivel-e-inadmissivel/"],["LPN: Secil quarries deactivation plan","https://www.lpn.pt/pt/noticias/lpn-pede-plano-de-desativacao-das-pedreiras-da-secil-no-parque-natural-da-arrabida"],["TSF: environmentalists ask Secil for a deactivation plan for quarries in Arrábida (in Portuguese)","https://www.tsf.pt/portugal/sociedade/ambientalistas-pedem-secil-plano-de-desativacao-de-pedreiras-da-secil-na-arrabida-16729282.html"],["GreenSavers: environmentalists demand the definitive end of Secil's quarries in Arrábida (in Portuguese)","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/ambientalistas-exigem-o-fim-definitivo-das-pedreiras-da-secil-na-arrabida/"],["Setúbal Mais: CCDR rejects expansion of Secil's quarry in Arrábida (in Portuguese)","https://setubalmais.pt/ccdr-chumba-ampliacao-da-pedreira-da-secil-na-arrabida/"],["RTP: Meco Livre Movement denounces stone pine felling","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/pais/movimento-meco-livre-denuncia-abate-de-pinheiro-manso_v1726496"],["Diário do Distrito: Meco Livre Movement raises alarm","https://diariodistrito.sapo.pt/movimento-meco-livre-lanca-alerta-sobre-um-dos-maiores-atentados-ambientais-em-sesimbra/"],["Public Petition: SOS Meco","https://peticaopublica.com/?pi=PT125714"],["Facebook: O Meco Livre","https://www.facebook.com/omecolivre/"],["Instagram: @mecolivre","https://www.instagram.com/mecolivre/"]],"stat":"323 ha of quarries inside the park · 4,000+ planned tourist beds with no cumulative EIA","link":"https://www.arrabida.org/a-arrabida-e-o-progresso/","linkL":"Read more at arrabida.org","cronologia":[{"data":"1976","texto":"The Arrábida Natural Park is created, after decades of campaigning by naturalists and local people.","fonte":"https://www.arrabida.org/a-arrabida-e-o-progresso/"},{"data":"2020-09-24","texto":"ZERO calls the expansion of Secil's quarries \"impossible and inadmissible\", recalling that the Park's management plan prohibits enlarging existing quarries.","fonte":"https://zero.ong/noticias/zero-considera-que-expansao-da-pedreiras-da-secil-na-arrabida-e-impossivel-e-inadmissivel/"},{"data":"2023-05-12","texto":"A draft resolution in Parliament asks the Government to reject the Secil quarry expansion and revise the Park's management plan; it is rejected.","fonte":"https://www.pcp.pt/salvaguarda-dos-valores-naturais-do-parque-natural-da-arrabida"},{"data":"2023-07-21","texto":"Seven environmental organisations (ANP|WWF, FAPAS, GEOTA, LPN, Quercus, SPEA and ZERO) ask Secil for a plan to decommission its quarries in the Park and close the Outão plant.","fonte":"https://www.lpn.pt/pt/noticias/lpn-pede-plano-de-desativacao-das-pedreiras-da-secil-no-parque-natural-da-arrabida"},{"data":"2023-08","texto":"CCDR-LVT rejects the Secil quarry expansion due to significant, non-mitigable negative impacts on ecological systems; of 812 public consultation submissions, 794 were against.","fonte":"https://setubalmais.pt/ccdr-chumba-ampliacao-da-pedreira-da-secil-na-arrabida/"}],"contexto":"The Arrábida Natural Park protects 12,328 hectares of limestone hills by the sea, between Setúbal, Palmela and Sesimbra. Quarries now cover 323 hectares, double the 1976 area, and built-up land inside the park has grown by about 500% since the 1960s. Quarrying, building and tourism press on the same territory; some of these conflicts have their own case file, such as Meco Livre and the Outão Fort."},"aterro-abrunheira-mafra":{"corpo":"<p>The Abrunheira landfill, at the Abrunheira Ecopark in the parish of São Miguel de Alcainça, Mafra, takes the waste of the municipalities of Cascais, Mafra, Oeiras and Sintra and is run by Tratolixo, an inter-municipal company owned by those four municipalities. According to Diário de Notícias, the landfill passed 91% of its capacity in April 2026 and was due to close in 2027.</p><p>On 18 August 2026, Tratolixo asked Mafra City Council to recognise the public interest of extending the landfill by three years, which would add one million tonnes of capacity until 2030. The council approved the request on 21 August, with the three PSD councillors voting against and stating that the landfill \"is harmful to the interests of the populations of the Municipality of Mafra\".</p><p>On 24 September 2026, Mafra Municipal Assembly rejected the proposal, with 23 votes against and 6 abstentions. At the session, residents delivered a petition against the extension; according to Lusa, the petitioners' representative, Jorge Silva, said it was unacceptable to extend operation to 2030 given the effects the population feels every day, and resident Carla Inverno described a \"nauseating smell\" that makes it impossible to air homes, especially on hot days. The president of the Malveira and São Miguel de Alcainça Parish Union, Carla Galrão, asked for studies justifying keeping the landfill open and for a new waste disposal site to be identified.</p><p>The mayor of Mafra, Hugo Moreira Luís, defended the proposal, recalling that Tratolixo had already decided in 2022 to extend the landfill's life for lack of an alternative. According to Diário de Notícias, an independent study identified nine possible sites for a new landfill, five in the municipality of Sintra and four in Mafra, and the mayor will ask Tratolixo to hold an information session for the population.</p>","fontes":[["Diário de Notícias, 24 Sep 2026: Controversy in Mafra: landfill \"public interest\" at risk of rejection, also affecting Cascais, Sintra and Oeiras (in Portuguese)","https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/polmica-em-mafra-interesse-pblico-do-aterro-em-risco-de-chumbar-e-afetar-ainda-cascais-sintra-e-oeiras"],["Diário de Notícias, 25 Sep 2026: Mafra: Abrunheira landfill expansion proposal rejected, creating a problem for four municipalities (in Portuguese)","https://www.dn.pt/sociedade/mafra-proposta-de-ampliao-do-aterro-da-abrunheira-foi-chumbada-e-cria-problema-a-quatro-concelhos"],["Ambiente Online / Lusa, 28 Sep 2026: Mafra rejects three-year extension of the Abrunheira landfill (in Portuguese)","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/mafra-rejeita-prolongamento-do-aterro-da-abrunheira-por-mais-tres-anos"]],"stat":"Over 91% of capacity used in April 2026 · 23 votes against the extension","link":"https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/mafra-rejeita-prolongamento-do-aterro-da-abrunheira-por-mais-tres-anos","linkL":"Read on Ambiente Online"},"borba":{"corpo":"<p>The Borba and Vila Viçosa region has 232 registered marble quarries, one of the highest densities of mining activity in the country.</p>\n<p>Independent surveys point out that over half of these quarries operate with no valid environmental recovery plan, in breach of legislation on landscape recovery of mined areas.</p>\n<p>The lack of regular inspection has been identified as the main obstacle to correcting this situation, leaving degraded areas without a recovery plan even after mining has ended.</p>","fontes":[["SÁBADO","https://www.sabado.pt/portugal/detalhe/borba-ambientalistas-apontam-centenas-de-pedreiras-abandonadas-sem-salvaguardas-ambientais"],["SAPO 24","https://24.sapo.pt/atualidade/artigos/acidenteborba-ambientalistas-apontam-centenas-de-pedreiras-abandonadas-sem-salvaguardas-ambientais"],["Linhas de Elvas","https://linhasdeelvas.pt/2026/07/15/secretario-de-estado-adjunto-e-da-energia-reuniu-com-municipio-de-vila-vicosa-para-analisar-plano-de-intervencao-nas-pedreiras/"]],"stat":"232 registered quarries","link":"","linkL":""},"restauro-natureza":{"corpo":"<p>The National Nature Restoration Plan was under public consultation until August 19, 2026, through the Participa Portal. The document sets out an investment of €500 million a year until 2030, spread across 407 measures in eight domains, from rivers and wetlands to forests and marine ecosystems.</p>\n<p>It is the national transposition of the European Nature Restoration Regulation, and the public consultation was the formal moment when anyone could propose changes to the plan before its final version, which Portugal must submit to EU authorities by September 2026.</p>\n<p>Organizations such as ZERO and SPEA submitted technical input during the process. Causas de Raiz will keep following the plan's final version.</p>","fontes":[["Portal Participa","https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/projeto-do-plano-nacional-de-restauro-da-natureza-e-respetiva-avaliacao-ambiental-estrategica"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/10/plano-nacional-de-restauro-da-natureza-em-consulta-publica-ate-19-de-agosto-500-milhoes-por-ano-e-400-medidas-para-travar-perda-de-biodiversidade/"],["Renascença","https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2026/06/02/plano-nacional-preve-quinhentos-milhoes-por-ano-ate-2030-para-restaurar-natureza/472996/"],["ZERO","https://jornalptgreen.pt/noticia/zero-quer-revisao-do-plano-nacional-de-restauro-da-natureza-antes-da-entrega-a-bruxelas/"]],"stat":"407 measures · 8 domains","link":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/projeto-do-plano-nacional-de-restauro-da-natureza-e-respetiva-avaliacao-ambiental-estrategica","linkL":"View the plan on the Participa Portal"},"poco-velho-aveiros-albufeira":{"corpo":"<p>Between August and September 2025, the Portuguese Environment Agency inspected 29 licensed beaches in the Algarve in municipalities \"where there were reports of irregularities or a history of incidents\". In Albufeira, the inspection confirmed that the main access to Poço Velho beach is closed by a gate on private land, with no regularized parking nearby. The Agency is now identifying and contacting the landowners, aiming to reopen the gate and coordinate parking and access planning with the municipal council.</p>\n<p>The Poço Velho case is not isolated in the municipality. In 2014, Praia dos Aveiros, in the same area, had its access blocked by a gate after a tourism developer claimed ownership of the access path in court. The Albufeira court eventually ordered the municipal council to restore the public signage, but the dispute left a precedent for how easily a private developer can, in practice, condition access to a legally public beach.</p>\n<p>The 2025 inspection also found other irregularities linked to beach concessions in the Algarve: at Monte Gordo, bathroom facilities closed or restricted to concession clients, despite access to bathrooms being universal by law; and occupation of the sand beyond the licensed area at Armação de Pêra and at Portimão beaches such as Rocha, Alvor and Prainha.</p>\n<p>The Agency's president, José Pimenta Machado, confirmed that around ten violation notices were issued in this inspection and that offenders have been or will be notified.</p>","fontes":[["Postal: APA inspection","https://postal.pt/algarve/fiscalizacao-da-apa-revela-ocupacoes-ilegais-e-falhas-em-concessoes-de-praias-algarvias/"],["Observador: rescue posts used as storage","https://observador.pt/2025/10/27/fiscalizacao-em-praias-do-algarve-encontrou-postos-de-socorro-a-servir-de-armazens-diz-agencia-portuguesa-do-ambiente/"],["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/fiscalizacao-em-praias-do-algarve-encontrou-postos-de-socorro-a-servir-de-armazens"],["The Portugal News","https://www.theportugalnews.com/pt/noticias/2025-10-29/irregularidades-detectadas-nas-praias-algarvias/908678"],["Sul Informação","https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2025/10/fiscalizacao-em-praias-do-algarve-encontrou-postos-de-socorro-a-servir-de-armazens-e-sanitarios-encerrados/"],["Público (2014): Praia dos Aveiros","https://www.publico.pt/2014/06/11/local/noticia/praia-dos-aveiros-em-albufeira-vai-ter-cancela-a-barrar-o-acesso-ao-mar-1639295"],["oturismo.pt (2014): Praia dos Aveiros","https://www.oturismo.pt/oturismo/26181-praia-dos-aveiros-passou-de-publica-a-privada-por-inercia-da-autarquia-de-albufeira.html"]],"stat":"29 beaches inspected · access blocked at Poço Velho since at least 2025, precedent at Aveiros since 2014","link":"https://postal.pt/algarve/fiscalizacao-da-apa-revela-ocupacoes-ilegais-e-falhas-em-concessoes-de-praias-algarvias/","linkL":"Read on Postal"},"quinta-dos-ingleses":{"corpo":"<p>Quinta dos Ingleses is a pine wood planted between 1900 and 1920, covering about 52 hectares next to Carcavelos beach, in Cascais. The Carcavelos Sul detailed plan, approved by the Council, allows about 850 flats, a hotel and a shopping centre, with an urban park of about eight hectares.</p>","fontes":[["Notícias ao Minuto/Lusa: St. Julian's says lawsuit halted works at Quinta dos Ingleses (28 Sep 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/3058604/st-julians-diz-que-acao-judicial-travou-obras-na-quinta-dos-ingleses-mas-tambem-recuperacao-da-escola"],["Notícias ao Minuto/Lusa: Court postpones action against Quinta dos Ingleses development (6 Jul 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/3017268/tribunal-adia-acao-contra-loteamento-da-quinta-dos-ingleses-em-carcavelos"],["Correio da Manhã: Lawyer says positive impacts outweigh negative ones at Quinta dos Ingleses (11 Sep 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/jurista-diz-que-impactos-positivos-superam-negativos-na-urbanizacao-da-quinta-dos-ingleses"],["SÁBADO: Cascais judge who cleared development was a council lawyer (28 May 2025) (in Portuguese)","https://www.sabado.pt/portugal/detalhe/cascais-jurista-e-juiz-em-camara-propria"],["Surf Total: New civic movement halts destruction of Quinta dos Ingleses (9 Jan 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://surftotal.com/noticias/nacionais/item/26706-novo-movimento-civico-trava-destruicao-da-quinta-dos-ingleses-em-cascais"],["ECO: Public Prosecutor seeks suspension of Hilton hotel in Cascais","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/07/19/mp-pede-suspensao-de-hotel-hilton-na-linha-de-cascais/"],["ECO: Cascais Council to appeal Public Prosecutor's decision","https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/07/23/camara-de-cascais-vai-recorrer-de-decisao-do-mp-que-ordena-suspensao-das-obras-do-hilton/"],["JN: Hilton project leads Judicial Police to search Cascais Council","https://www.jn.pt/justica/artigo/projeto-do-hilton-leva-pj-a-realizar-buscas-na-camara-de-cascais/17849549"],["Executive Digest: Public Prosecutor investigates Cascais Council over Hilton deal","https://executivedigest.sapo.pt/mp-investiga-camara-municipal-de-cascais-devido-a-negocio-do-hotel-hilton-autarquia-tera-vendido-terreno-em-zona-ameacada-a-baixo-custo/"],["SOS Quinta dos Ingleses: history of Quinta dos Ingleses","https://en.sosquintadosingleses.com/onossopassado"]],"stat":"52-hectare pine forest · 850 apartments planned","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/09/11/quinta-dos-ingleses-jurista-da-autarquia-diz-que-impactos-positivos-superam-negativos/","linkL":"Read on Observador","cronologia":[{"data":"2021-06-24","texto":"The SOS Quinta dos Ingleses movement becomes an association.","fonte":"https://en.sosquintadosingleses.com/onossopassado"},{"data":"2024-06","texto":"Construction of the development begins.","fonte":"https://surftotal.com/noticias/nacionais/item/26706-novo-movimento-civico-trava-destruicao-da-quinta-dos-ingleses-em-cascais"},{"data":"2024-12","texto":"An injunction by SOS Quinta dos Ingleses is rejected by a judge who had previously been a Cascais Council legal adviser with direct contact with the file.","fonte":"https://www.sabado.pt/portugal/detalhe/cascais-jurista-e-juiz-em-camara-propria"},{"data":"2025-10","texto":"The 66 Pela Quinta movement brings a class action against Cascais Council, with Alves Ribeiro and St. Julian's School as interested parties; the injunction halts the works.","fonte":"https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/3058604/st-julians-diz-que-acao-judicial-travou-obras-na-quinta-dos-ingleses-mas-tambem-recuperacao-da-escola"},{"data":"2026-07-06","texto":"The hearings scheduled for July at the Sintra Administrative and Tax Court are postponed because the judge is on sick leave.","fonte":"https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/3017268/tribunal-adia-acao-contra-loteamento-da-quinta-dos-ingleses-em-carcavelos"},{"data":"2026-07-19","texto":"In a related case, the Public Prosecutor seeks to suspend works on the Hilton development on the Carcavelos seafront, built on a plot sold by the Council.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/07/19/mp-pede-suspensao-de-hotel-hilton-na-linha-de-cascais/"},{"data":"2026-07-23","texto":"Cascais Council announces it will appeal the Public Prosecutor's decision on the Hilton.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2026/07/23/camara-de-cascais-vai-recorrer-de-decisao-do-mp-que-ordena-suspensao-das-obras-do-hilton/"},{"data":"2026-09-11","texto":"In court, a Cascais Council lawyer argues that in the environmental assessment positive impacts outweighed negative ones and that the development stayed below the plan's maximum.","fonte":"https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/jurista-diz-que-impactos-positivos-superam-negativos-na-urbanizacao-da-quinta-dos-ingleses"},{"data":"2026-09-28","texto":"Witness hearings end; the Council, Alves Ribeiro and St. Julian's waive the testimony scheduled for 13 October. There is no date for the judge's decision.","fonte":"https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/3058604/st-julians-diz-que-acao-judicial-travou-obras-na-quinta-dos-ingleses-mas-tambem-recuperacao-da-escola"}],"contexto":"Quinta dos Ingleses is a pine wood planted between 1900 and 1920, covering about 52 hectares next to Carcavelos beach, in Cascais. The Carcavelos Sul detailed plan, approved by the Council, allows about 850 flats, a hotel and a shopping centre, with an urban park of about eight hectares."},"megacentrais-solares-divor-evora":{"corpo":"<p>North and northeast of Évora, in Graça do Divor and partly in Arraiolos, three solar plants are planned, all connected to the Divor substation: Incognitworld 3's (362,076 modules, the only one licensed), Hyperion Renewables' Graça do Divor plant (394,500 panels) and Newcon40's Sol de Évora (800,100 modules).</p>","fontes":[["Diana FM: Platform warns Évora's World Heritage status may be at risk (2 Apr 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.dianafm.com/plataforma-alerta-que-classificacao-de-evora-como-patrimonio-mundial-pode-estar-em-risco/"],["ECO: Movement calls two solar plant projects in Évora indefensible (11 Aug 2025) (in Portuguese)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2025/08/11/movimento-considera-indefensaveis-projetos-de-duas-centrais-solares-em-evora/"],["Rádio Campanário: Organisations contest renewable acceleration zones in Évora (15 Jul 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.radiocampanario.com/organizacoes-contestam-criacao-de-zonas-de-aceleracao-de-renovaveis-em-evora/"],["Diário do Sul, 17 Jun. 2026: Évora Municipal Assembly held public hearing on solar plants (in Portuguese)","https://diariodosul.pt/2026/06/17/assembleia-municipal-de-evora-realizou-audicao-publica-sobre-a-instalacao-de-centrais-fotovoltaicas/"],["ECO, 5 Mar. 2025: Project proposes solar plant with more than 800,000 panels near Évora (in Portuguese)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2025/03/05/projeto-propoe-central-solar-com-mais-de-800-mil-paineis-perto-de-evora/"],["Petição Pública: Juntos pelo Divor, against mega solar plants in Graça do Divor parish (in Portuguese)","https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=PT121352"],["Juntos pelo Divor platform poster, May 2026 (Ephemera archive, in Portuguese)","https://ephemerajpp.com/2026/05/13/juntos-pelo-divor/"]],"stat":"3 plants · more than 1,550,000 panels and 1,700 ha, according to the platform","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/04/01/plataforma-alerta-que-esta-em-risco-selo-de-evora-como-patrimonio-mundial-da-unesco-devido-a-fotovoltaicas/","linkL":"Read on Observador","cronologia":[{"data":"1986","texto":"Évora's historic centre is listed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site; the rural landscape north of the city is one of the elements of its integrity.","fonte":"https://www.dianafm.com/plataforma-alerta-que-classificacao-de-evora-como-patrimonio-mundial-pode-estar-em-risco/"},{"data":"2019","texto":"Newcon40 submits its application for the Sol de Évora plant to the Directorate-General for Energy and Geology.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2025/03/05/projeto-propoe-central-solar-com-mais-de-800-mil-paineis-perto-de-evora/"},{"data":"2024-06-27","texto":"The Juntos pelo Divor platform launches a petition against mega solar plants in the parish of Graça do Divor.","fonte":"https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=PT121352"},{"data":"2025-03","texto":"The scoping proposal for the environmental impact study of the Sol de Évora plant, with 800,100 modules, is open to public consultation until 24 March.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2025/03/05/projeto-propoe-central-solar-com-mais-de-800-mil-paineis-perto-de-evora/"},{"data":"2025-07-08","texto":"The platform meets Hyperion Renewables.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2025/08/11/movimento-considera-indefensaveis-projetos-de-duas-centrais-solares-em-evora/"},{"data":"2025-08","texto":"In a letter to the company, the platform calls the Graça do Divor and Sol de Évora projects \"indefensible\" and says the meeting was conducted as if it were a done deal.","fonte":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2025/08/11/movimento-considera-indefensaveis-projetos-de-duas-centrais-solares-em-evora/"},{"data":"2026-04","texto":"The platform warns that Évora's World Heritage status may be at risk: the three plants add up to more than 1.55 million panels on more than 1,700 contiguous hectares. It reports the case to UNESCO and ICOMOS Portugal.","fonte":"https://www.dianafm.com/plataforma-alerta-que-classificacao-de-evora-como-patrimonio-mundial-pode-estar-em-risco/"},{"data":"2026-05","texto":"The platform releases a poster with the slogan \"This is not energy transition, this is the destruction of our heritage\".","fonte":"https://ephemerajpp.com/2026/05/13/juntos-pelo-divor/"},{"data":"2026-06-12","texto":"Évora Municipal Assembly holds a public hearing on the three plants.","fonte":"https://diariodosul.pt/2026/06/17/assembleia-municipal-de-evora-realizou-audicao-publica-sobre-a-instalacao-de-centrais-fotovoltaicas/"},{"data":"2026-07-15","texto":"Grupo Pro-Évora and the Juntos pelo Divor platform issue unfavourable opinions on the Renewable Energy Acceleration Zones, which would cover the north of the municipality within 10 km of the Divor substation, and call for a heritage impact assessment.","fonte":"https://www.radiocampanario.com/organizacoes-contestam-criacao-de-zonas-de-aceleracao-de-renovaveis-em-evora/"}],"contexto":"North and northeast of Évora, in Graça do Divor and partly in Arraiolos, three solar plants are planned, all connected to the Divor substation: Incognitworld 3's (362,076 modules, the only one licensed), Hyperion Renewables' Graça do Divor plant (394,500 panels) and Newcon40's Sol de Évora (800,100 modules)."},"revive-forte-outao":{"corpo":"<p>Under the Revive programme, which grants private companies concessions to run publicly-owned properties of historical value, the Forte Velho do Outão (also known as the 7th Outão Battery), a former coastal defence battery inside the Arrábida Natural Park, next to the Secil quarries, was granted for 50 years.</p>\n<p>The contract was signed on 25 August 2023 with Real Bolhão, Restaurantes, Unipessoal, Lda., with a minimum annual rent of €130,987.32 and a construction area of 6,909 m². Press reports put the actual contracted rent at close to €201,000 a year. The 2022 tender allowed for a hotel, local accommodation or another tourism project; the concession was initially announced for a restaurant. In February 2025, Setúbal City Council approved a reconversion of the project into a 5-star hotel with around 35 rooms.</p>\n<p>According to the official Revive page, operations are expected to start by September 2027. There is no public confirmation of works having started on site.</p>","fontes":[["Turismo de Portugal (Revive, official tender page)","https://revive.turismodeportugal.pt/pt-pt/node/939"],["ECO (concession and rent)","https://eco.sapo.pt/2023/09/12/7a-bateria-do-outao-na-serra-da-arrabida-vai-ser-transformado-em-restaurante-com-renda-anual-de-200-mil-euros/"],["O Setubalense (2023, restaurant)","https://osetubalense.com/local/setubal/vai-nascer-um-restaurante-na-7-a-bateria-do-outao/"],["Publituris Hotelaria (2025, reconversion into hotel)","https://publiturishotelaria.pt/2025/02/04/camara-de-setubal-aprova-reconversao-da-7-a-bataria-do-outao-em-empreendimento-turistico"],["O Setubalense (2025, hotel approval)","https://osetubalense.com/local/setubal/camara-municipal-aprova-proposta-para-futuro-hotel-na-7-a-bataria-do-outao/"],["Echo Boomer","https://echoboomer.pt/7a-bateria-do-outao-vai-dar-origem-novo-restaurante/"]],"stat":"50-year concession, next to the Secil quarries","link":"https://revive.turismodeportugal.pt/pt-pt/node/939","linkL":"See tender on Revive →"},"serta":{"corpo":"<p>Over 25% of the Sertã municipality's area is identified in the national plan as a solar acceleration zone, one of the highest proportions in the country.</p>\n<p>Sertã City Council, joined by neighbouring municipalities in Beira Baixa, issued an unfavourable opinion on the programme, warning of the cumulative impact on the landscape, agriculture and municipal land-use planning.</p>\n<p>The regional pushback reflects a broader concern about the disproportionate concentration of large-scale energy projects in inland territories, with no equivalent compensation for local communities.</p>","fontes":[["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/07/14/camara-da-serta-da-parecer-desfavoravel-as-zonas-de-aceleracao-de-renovaveis/"],["Notícias de Coimbra","https://www.noticiasdecoimbra.pt/camara-da-serta-da-parecer-desfavoravel-as-zonas-de-aceleracao-de-renovaveis/"],["Médio Tejo","https://mediotejo.net/serta-emite-parecer-negativo-a-zona-de-aceleracao-para-as-energias-renovaveis/"],["Mais Beiras","https://maisbeiras.sapo.pt/serta-municipio-emite-parecer-desfavoravel-a-proposta-do-programa-setorial-das-zonas-de-aceleracao-para-as-energias-renovaveis"]],"stat":"25%+ of the municipality","link":"","linkL":""},"lagoa-salgados-silves":{"corpo":"<p>Lagoa dos Salgados, between Armação de Pêra and Albufeira, is the last stretch of the Algarve coast with no ecological protection status at all. On November 22, 2025, the Institute for Nature Conservation and Forests made public a proposal to classify a 400-hectare Natural Reserve at the site, after more than 20 years of requests from environmental organizations.</p>\n<p>The proposal directly conflicts with the Praia Grande Eco-Resort tourism project, which plans an investment of around €200 million in three hotels, two villages, an 18-hole golf course and over two kilometres of beachfront, totalling 4,000 beds. Silves's new Municipal Master Plan already excludes the resort from the Praia Grande area, next to the lagoon.</p>\n<p>On July 28, 2026, Silves City Council met with the State Secretary for the Environment to reiterate the need to move forward with the classification process. The Movimento Participativo Lagoa dos Salgados brings together nine organizations, Almargem, A Rocha, ANP|WWF, Vita Nativa, LPN, Quercus-ANCN, Sociedade Portuguesa de Botânica, SPEA and ZERO, in a long-running campaign through the \"Save Salgados\" petition, which remains active.</p>","fontes":[["Algarve Marafado","https://www.algarvemarafado.com/2026/07/30/avanca-processo-para-a-criacao-de-nova-reserva-natural-no-algarve/"],["LPN","https://www.lpn.pt/pt/noticias/projeto-ressuscitado-ameaca-futura-reserva-natural-da-lagoa-dos-salgados-"],["SPEA","https://spea.pt/imprensa/projeto-ressuscitado-ameaca-futura-reserva-natural-da-lagoa-dos-salgados/"],["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/novo-plano-diretor-municipal-de-silves-ja-exclui-resort-junto-a-lagoa-dos-salgados"],["Público","https://www.publico.pt/2021/12/04/local/noticia/lagoa-salgados-passa-reserva-natural-poe-causa-4-mil-camas-ali-previstas-1987407"]],"stat":"400 hectares proposed","link":"https://www.algarvemarafado.com/2026/07/30/avanca-processo-para-a-criacao-de-nova-reserva-natural-no-algarve/","linkL":"Read on Algarve Marafado"},"curral-freiras":{"corpo":"<p>The cable car and adventure park project in Curral das Freiras, Câmara de Lobos, was approved despite being located in a known nesting area of Zino's petrel, one of the world's most endangered seabirds, endemic to Madeira.</p>\n<p>Quercus-Madeira formally challenged the decision, warning that the environmental impact study fails to robustly rule out risk to the species, which is critically endangered.</p>\n<p>The Ecologist Party, Os Verdes, with a structure in Madeira, reiterated to the regional ICNF its firm opposition to the project, asking for the licensing decision to be reviewed.</p>","fontes":[["Quercus","https://sapo.pt/artigo/quercus-da-madeira-contra-o-teleferico-do-curral-das-freiras-6a18a717795ed400b3851124"],["Os Verdes","https://osverdes.pt/acao-ecologista/eleicoes/sobre-o-sistema-de-telefericos-do-curral-das-freiras/"],["DNoticias","https://www.dnoticias.pt/2026/5/28/493614-quercus-da-madeira-contra-o-teleferico-do-curral-das-freiras/"],["JM Madeira","https://www.jm-madeira.pt/regiao/ver/167333/Os_Verdes_reiteram_posicao_contra_projeto_de_teleferico_no_Curral_das_Freiras"],["Funchal Notícias","https://funchalnoticias.net/2026/07/02/quercus-madeira-impugna-decisao-de-conformidade-ambiental-do-teleferico-do-curral-das-freiras/"]],"stat":"Critically endangered species","link":"","linkL":""},"transvase-tejo-guadiana":{"corpo":"<p>The Alentejo Regional Coordination and Development Commission (CCDR) and EDIA met on 8 September 2026 to prepare a bid for the Alentejo 2030 Regional Programme to fund a study on the feasibility of transferring water from the Tagus river to the Guadiana basin, under the national \"Água que Une\" (\"Water that Unites\") strategy. According to CCDR Alentejo's president, Ricardo Pinheiro, the scenario under study envisages diverting around 150 cubic hectometres of water, which would allow Alqueva-supported irrigation to expand by more than 50,000 new hectares. The study, not yet funded, is meant to assess both the engineering side of the link and the economic impact of the investment across different sub-regions of the Alentejo.</p>\n<p>The environmental association ZERO warns that continuously expanding irrigated area could exhaust the safety reserve the Alqueva reservoir is meant to guarantee in the long run, and notes that inter-basin transfers tend to generate territorial tensions between donor and recipient regions.</p>\n<p>The Minister of Environment and Energy, Maria da Graça Carvalho, has for now downplayed the Tagus-Guadiana link as a priority, arguing that \"this kind of inter-basin link should always be the last solution, after every other solution has been tried\". According to the minister, the Alentejo's water reserves currently stand at 80% (the national average), and other responses are already under way, including Alqueva, existing dams and a planned desalination plant in Sines; any link would also require agreement between the Portuguese and Spanish governments, since the Tagus and Guadiana are international rivers.</p>\n<p>For now there is no green light for construction: the process is solely aimed at securing funding for a technical and economic assessment.</p>","fontes":[["Tribuna Alentejo: Tagus-Guadiana water transfer studied by CCDR Alentejo to expand irrigation by 50,000 hectares, environmentalists push back (8 Sep 2026)","https://tribunaalentejo.pt/artigos/transvaze-de-agua-do-tejo-para-o-guadiana-estudado-pela-ccdr-alentejo-para-aumentar-regadio-em-50-mil-hectares-ambientalistas-contestam/"],["ODigital.pt: CCDR Alentejo wants to assess the economic impact of the Tagus-Guadiana link (3 Sep 2026)","https://odigital.sapo.pt/ccdr-alentejo-estudo-ligacao-tejo-guadiana/"],["ODigital.pt: Tagus-Guadiana link is not the first priority, says Environment Minister (8 Sep 2026)","https://odigital.sapo.pt/ligacao-tejo-guadiana-prioridade-ministra-ambiente/"]],"stat":"150 cubic hectometres under study","link":"","linkL":""},"verdelago-castro-marim":{"corpo":"<p>Between August and September 2025, the Portuguese Environment Agency inspected 29 licensed beaches in the Algarve in municipalities \"where there were reports of irregularities or a history of incidents\". In Castro Marim, the inspection confirmed that access to Verdelago beach runs through the interior of a tourism development, via a gate with a buzzer and unclear signage about the public route.</p>\n<p>As a corrective measure, the Agency notified the developer to install clear signage indicating the public access route to the beach and to create alternative parking to the west, closer to the sand, removing the dependence on the conditioned entrance through the development.</p>\n<p>The Agency's president, José Pimenta Machado, confirmed that around ten violation notices were issued in this inspection and that offenders have been or will be notified. He noted that concessions \"are licensed to occupy a given space\" and that public beach access must be guaranteed regardless of neighboring tourism developments.</p>\n<p>The Verdelago case is not isolated in the Algarve: in the same inspection, Poço Velho beach, in Albufeira, was found with its main access completely blocked by a gate on private land.</p>","fontes":[["Postal: APA inspection","https://postal.pt/algarve/fiscalizacao-da-apa-revela-ocupacoes-ilegais-e-falhas-em-concessoes-de-praias-algarvias/"],["Observador: rescue posts used as storage","https://observador.pt/2025/10/27/fiscalizacao-em-praias-do-algarve-encontrou-postos-de-socorro-a-servir-de-armazens-diz-agencia-portuguesa-do-ambiente/"],["Correio da Manhã","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/fiscalizacao-em-praias-do-algarve-encontrou-postos-de-socorro-a-servir-de-armazens"],["The Portugal News","https://www.theportugalnews.com/pt/noticias/2025-10-29/irregularidades-detectadas-nas-praias-algarvias/908678"],["Sul Informação","https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2025/10/fiscalizacao-em-praias-do-algarve-encontrou-postos-de-socorro-a-servir-de-armazens-e-sanitarios-encerrados/"]],"stat":"29 beaches inspected · conditioned access confirmed at Verdelago","link":"https://postal.pt/algarve/fiscalizacao-da-apa-revela-ocupacoes-ilegais-e-falhas-em-concessoes-de-praias-algarvias/","linkL":"Read on Postal"},"castanheira-ribatejo":{"corpo":"<p>Vila Franca de Xira City Council approved, on 25 August 2026, moving ahead with a detailed plan that expands the Lisbon-North Logistics Platform in Castanheira do Ribatejo by around 340 hectares, nearly triple the current area of about 100 hectares, occupied since 2008. Around 300 hectares are earmarked for economic activities (logistics, technology and data centres), with the area closest to the Tejo river becoming a riverside urban park. The process was in public consultation until 4 September 2026.</p><p>The CDU (Communist coalition) criticised converting about 295 hectares of farmland and ecologically valuable land, estimating €491 million in land-value gains for owners and developers from the reclassification. PSD and IL called for stronger guarantees on the power grid, needed for the planned data centres, and Chega demanded assurances on infrastructure and firefighting capacity. Mayor Fernando Paulo Ferreira argues the project will create around 5,000 jobs and promises a strategic environmental assessment before proceeding. In an earlier phase of the same project (2021-2022), Quercus and the civic movement XIRADANIA had already issued a negative opinion on the environmental impact study for a roughly 38-hectare subdivision on the same platform, citing insufficient study of alternative locations and downplaying of contamination risk to the country's largest freshwater aquifer.</p>","fontes":[["idealista/news (announcement of the detailed plan)","https://www.idealista.pt/news/imobiliario/empresas/2026/08/31/77390-vila-franca-quer-triplicar-plataforma-logistica-de-lisboa-norte"],["Público (opposition's position on the council)","https://www.publico.pt/2026/08/26/local/noticia/vila-franca-quer-triplicar-plataforma-logistica-lisboanorte-oposicao-coloca-duvidas-2186059"],["Participa.pt (public consultation for the earlier project phase, 2021-2022)","https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/plataforma-logistica-de-castanheira-do-ribatejo"],["Quercus (negative opinion on the earlier project phase, 2021)","https://quercus.pt/2021/03/plataforma-logistica-de-castanheira-do-ribatejo-quercus-da-parecer-negativo/"]],"stat":"340-hectare detailed plan, about 300 for logistics, technology and data centres","link":"https://www.idealista.pt/news/imobiliario/empresas/2026/08/31/77390-vila-franca-quer-triplicar-plataforma-logistica-de-lisboa-norte","linkL":"Read the article →"},"mata-albergaria-volta":{"corpo":"<p>ICNF authorised the 7th stage of the Volta a Portugal cycling race to pass through the Mata da Albergaria, one of the country's few well-preserved native oak forests, inside Portugal's only National Park (Peneda-Gerês). The area includes partial-protection zones and is bordered in part by total-protection zones.</p><p>The authorisation imposed strict conditions: no public access, no sound amplification, no aerial support and support vehicles kept to a minimum. Even so, Quercus challenged the decision, warning that the impacts are not eliminated and that it sets a \"grave precedent\" for future events in protected areas. ZERO said it was satisfied with the \"strong conditions\" imposed.</p><p>The stage went ahead on 13 August 2026 under those conditions; Quercus continues to demand the stretch be excluded from future editions of the race.</p>","fontes":[["Observador: Quercus contesta Volta a Portugal em mata sensível no Gerês e alerta para \"grave precedente\"","https://observador.pt/2026/08/11/quercus-contesta-volta-a-portugal-em-mata-sensivel-no-geres-e-alerta-para-grave-precedente/"],["Quercus: Mata de Albergaria, no Gerês, não é lugar para a passagem da Volta a Portugal em bicicleta","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/11/mata-de-albergaria-no-geres-nao-e-lugar-para-a-passagem-da-volta-a-portugal-em-bicicleta/"],["Renascença: Quercus contesta Volta a Portugal no Gerês, ZERO satisfeita com \"fortes condicionantes\"","https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2026/08/11/quercus-contesta-volta-a-portugal-no-geres-zero-satisfeita-com-fortes-condicionantes/481484/"],["A Bola: Quercus contesta Volta a Portugal no Gerês e pede suspensão da etapa","https://www.abola.pt/noticias/quercus-contesta-volta-a-portugal-no-geres-e-pede-suspensao-da-etapa-2026081111344648856"]],"stat":"The only well-preserved native oak forest in Portugal's only National Park","link":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/08/11/mata-de-albergaria-no-geres-nao-e-lugar-para-a-passagem-da-volta-a-portugal-em-bicicleta/","linkL":"See Quercus's position →"},"pszaer":{"corpo":"<p>Renewable Energy Acceleration Zones (ZAER), under the EU RED III directive, exempt solar and wind projects within them from individual environmental impact assessment, based on a strategic environmental assessment of the whole zone carried out before any project exists.</p>","fontes":[["Green Savers: Government guarantees municipalities total autonomy in defining renewable acceleration zones (17 Jul 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/governo-garante-total-autonomia-dos-municipios-na-definicao-de-zonas-de-aceleracao-de-renovaveis/"],["SAPO: pre-approval of over 800 ZAER zones","https://sapo.pt/artigo/governo-anuncia-pre-aprovacao-de-mais-de-800-areas-de-aceleracao-de-energias-renovaveis-6a87370cd0cbd78bc72e9fee"],["RTP: \"Black Desert\": Quercus issues unfavourable opinion on PSZAER","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/pais/deserto-negro-quercus-da-parecer-desfavoravel-ao-programa-setorial-das-zonas-de-aceleracao-das-energias-renovaveis_a1753539"],["Quercus","https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/07/15/quercus-emite-parecer-desfavoravel-ao-programa-setorial-das-zonas-de-aceleracao-das-energias-renovaveis/"],["Ambiente Online: public consultation ends amid criticism","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/programa-de-zonas-de-aceleracao-de-renovaveis-termina-consulta-publica-sob-criticas-de-quercus-e-municipios"],["Macedo Vitorino: legal note on ZAER","https://www.macedovitorino.com/conhecimento/insights/Governo-coloca-as-ZAER-em-consulta/6960/"],["Jornal Nordeste","https://jornalnordeste.com/2026/06/23/nordeste-vivo-prepara-novas-acoes-apos-primeira-sessao-de-esclarecimento-sobre-megaprojetos-energeticos/"]],"stat":"800+ ZAER zones · ~170 municipalities · ~1% of territory","link":"https://sapo.pt/artigo/governo-anuncia-pre-aprovacao-de-mais-de-800-areas-de-aceleracao-de-energias-renovaveis-6a87370cd0cbd78bc72e9fee","linkL":"Read on SAPO","cronologia":[{"data":"2026-06-17","texto":"Public consultation on the Sectoral Programme for Renewable Energy Acceleration Zones, with 1,302 candidate zones (792 solar and 510 wind).","fonte":"https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/programa-de-zonas-de-aceleracao-de-renovaveis-termina-consulta-publica-sob-criticas-de-quercus-e-municipios","dataFim":"2026-07-15"},{"data":"2026-06-23","texto":"Plataforma Nordeste Vivo prepares new actions against zones overlapping conservation areas in the north-east.","fonte":"https://jornalnordeste.com/2026/06/23/nordeste-vivo-prepara-novas-acoes-apos-primeira-sessao-de-esclarecimento-sobre-megaprojetos-energeticos/"},{"data":"2026-07-15","texto":"Quercus issues an unfavourable opinion, which it calls \"Black Desert\": the proposal covered about 7% of mainland territory, with maps at a scale useless for analysis.","fonte":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2026/07/15/quercus-emite-parecer-desfavoravel-ao-programa-setorial-das-zonas-de-aceleracao-das-energias-renovaveis/"},{"data":"2026-07-17","texto":"The Secretary of State for Energy guarantees municipalities \"total autonomy\" to choose the zones, up to 1% of their territory; the consultation received more than 9,000 submissions.","fonte":"https://greensavers.sapo.pt/governo-garante-total-autonomia-dos-municipios-na-definicao-de-zonas-de-aceleracao-de-renovaveis/"},{"data":"2026-08-20","texto":"The Government announces the pre-approval of more than 800 zones (about 500 solar and 300 wind) in about 170 municipalities, about 1% of mainland territory, with exemption from project-specific environmental impact assessment.","fonte":"https://sapo.pt/artigo/governo-anuncia-pre-aprovacao-de-mais-de-800-areas-de-aceleracao-de-energias-renovaveis-6a87370cd0cbd78bc72e9fee"}],"contexto":"Renewable Energy Acceleration Zones (ZAER), under the EU RED III directive, exempt solar and wind projects within them from individual environmental impact assessment, based on a strategic environmental assessment of the whole zone carried out before any project exists."},"alqueva-solar-flutuante":{"corpo":"<p>In 2022, EDP Renováveis won the largest lot in Portugal's national floating solar auction, securing the right to install 70 megawatts of photovoltaic capacity on the Alqueva reservoir, bidding a negative price of €4 per megawatt-hour. The project, named \"Grande Lago\", envisaged a hybrid plant of up to 154 MW, combining floating panels, additional solar capacity and a wind farm, across an area that would have covered 250 hectares of the reservoir's surface, spanning the municipalities of Moura, Portel and Reguengos de Monsaraz.</p>\n<p>In November 2025, the mayors of Moura, Reguengos de Monsaraz, Portel, Alandroal and Mourão met with the Minister of Environment and Energy to oppose the project, warning that a reservoir \"packed with solar panels\" would harm tourism and navigability in the region and bring \"no added value\" to the municipalities involved.</p>\n<p>On 6 August 2026, EDP announced it was dropping the project, citing profitability concerns after the Portuguese Environment Agency rejected the environmental impact study, notably over the impact of the grid connection line on birds of prey habitats. The case adds to a string of floating solar projects rejected on environmental grounds in Portuguese reservoirs since the 2022 auction.</p>","fontes":[["ECO","https://eco.sapo.pt/2025/11/28/cinco-camaras-contestam-nova-central-fotovoltaica-flutuante-no-alqueva/"],["Ambiente Online","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/edp-ganha-maior-lote-no-leilao-solar-flutuante-e-vai-instalar-mega-central-no-alqueva"],["Observador","https://observador.pt/2026/08/06/grupo-edp-deixa-cair-central-solar-flutuante-no-alqueva-por-questoes-de-rentabilidade-e-apos-chumbo-de-estudo-ambiental/"],["Observador: especial solar flutuante","https://observador.pt/especiais/solar-flutuante-com-escala-ainda-e-uma-miragem-porque-estao-a-ser-chumbadas-as-centrais-em-cima-de-barragens/"]],"stat":"154 MW cancelled","link":"https://eco.sapo.pt/2025/11/28/cinco-camaras-contestam-nova-central-fotovoltaica-flutuante-no-alqueva/","linkL":"Read on ECO"},"valtreixal":{"corpo":"<p>The Valtreixal mining project, in Calabor, in the Spanish province of Zamora, planned an open-pit operation a few kilometres from the Portuguese border, next to Montesinho Natural Park.</p>\n<p>Movimento UIVO, created in 2021 by residents on both sides of the border, mobilized against the project, warning of contamination risk to watercourses shared between Portugal and Spain.</p>\n<p>The regional government of Castile and León refused the project's environmental permit, a result the movement considers significant for the whole cross-border region, while it remains alert to possible appeals from the developer.</p>\n<p>The mine would have been a few kilometres from Montesinho Natural Park. According to the ICNF's description of the park, accessed on 27 September 2026, Montesinho Natural Park is home to around 250 vertebrate species and 70% of the land mammal species found in Portugal, around 10% of which are listed as threatened in the Portuguese Red Book of Vertebrates. It holds one of the most important Iberian wolf populations and the only viable populations of freshwater pearl mussel (Margaritifera margaritifera) known in Portugal, and is part of the \"Montesinho-Nogueira\" Site of Community Importance and Special Protection Area of the Natura 2000 network.</p>","fontes":[["Esquerda.net","https://www.esquerda.net/artigo/incongruencias-do-estudo-de-impacto-ambiental-da-mina-em-calabor-preocupam-movimento-uivo"],["Notícias ao Minuto","https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/2994018/espanha-trava-mina-perto-de-braganca-e-do-parque-de-montesinho"],["Jornal Nordeste","https://jornalnordeste.com/2026/05/24/junta-de-castela-e-leao-trava-exploracao-mineira-junto-a-fronteira-de-braganca/"],["Diário de Trás-os-Montes","https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/junta-de-castela-e-leao-impede-exploracao-mineira-em-calabor-a-5-km-de-braganca"],["eldiario.es (Espanha)","https://www.eldiario.es/castilla-y-leon/castilla-leon-niega-licencia-ambiental-mina-wolframio-fronteriza-levanto-fuerte-rechazo-portugal_1_13218822.html"],["ICNF: Montesinho Natural Park, description (in Portuguese, accessed 27 Sep 2026)","https://resources.natural.pt/uploads/additional-information/2019/06/12/08/Msm1aTmOfwIWzjc2.pdf"]],"stat":"Permit refused","link":"https://www.esquerda.net/artigo/incongruencias-do-estudo-de-impacto-ambiental-da-mina-em-calabor-preocupam-movimento-uivo","linkL":"Read on esquerda.net"},"pedreira-cerro-meio-tavira":{"corpo":"<p>The Tavira Court ordered the immediate and permanent closure of the \"Cerro do Meio\" quarry, operated by Miner Blanc, Lda. (Verdasca group), in the Luz de Tavira and Santo Estêvão parish union. A group of residents had filed a special personality-rights protection case asking for the activity (suspended since 2013 and resumed in 2025) to be shut down entirely.</p><p>Residents' complaints centred on excessive noise, vibration and dust. The court also found that vibrations and earthmoving in the area could damage an essential water-supply pipeline for the eastern Algarve that runs near the quarry.</p><p>The company was given 24 hours to halt operations, on pain of a disobedience offence.</p>","fontes":[["Jornal do Algarve: Tribunal de Tavira dá razão a moradores e condena empresa a encerrar pedreira","https://jornaldoalgarve.pt/tribunal-de-tavira-da-razao-a-moradores-e-condena-empresa-a-encerrar-pedreira/"],["Correio da Manhã: Tribunal manda encerrar pedreira após queixas de excesso de ruído e poeiras","https://www.cmjornal.pt/sociedade/detalhe/tribunal-manda-encerrar-pedreira-apos-queixas-de-excesso-de-ruido-e-poeiras"],["Postal: Pedreira de Tavira encerrada após tribunal considerar violados direitos dos moradores","https://postal.pt/algarve/pedreira-de-tavira-encerrada-apos-tribunal-considerar-violados-direitos-dos-moradores/"]],"stat":"Immediate court-ordered closure by the Tavira Court","link":"https://jornaldoalgarve.pt/tribunal-de-tavira-da-razao-a-moradores-e-condena-empresa-a-encerrar-pedreira/","linkL":"See Jornal do Algarve report →"},"fanal-madeira":{"corpo":"<p>Fanal, within Madeira Natural Park (created in 1982), is classified as a Rest and Silence Zone, a protection category that, by definition, should limit motorised traffic and reserve the space for \"quiet recreation\". It is known for its centuries-old til trees, emblematic of the Laurissilva forest, a UNESCO World Heritage Site.</p>\n<p>In September 2025, the Madeira Regional Branch of Quercus warned of a \"slow death\" of this protected zone: cattle grazing freely devour the shoots of the centuries-old til trees, and excessive visitor numbers lead to parking that exceeds the capacity of the two existing car parks, with rental and off-road vehicles crowding the road verges. Dozens of visitors trample the reserve's soil with no marked trails, compacting it to the point that herbaceous plants no longer grow in some areas, exposing tree roots.</p>\n<p>A year earlier, in September 2024, the same association had already criticised the Institute of Forests and Nature Conservation (IFCN) for authorising a wedding with over 200 guests inside this Rest and Silence Zone, complete with a marquee and litter left on site, a case the GNR police went on to investigate.</p>\n<p>Quercus proposes defining the area's carrying capacity, creating marked and signposted footpaths, strengthening surveillance, evaluating parking alternatives and limiting grazing in sensitive areas. The Regional Government acknowledged the problem of excessive visitation and recommended alternative routes to tour operators, a measure the association considers insufficient given the severity of the situation.</p>","fontes":[["Quercus: \"The slow death of Fanal\"","https://quercus.pt/blog/2025/09/09/a-morte-lenta-do-fanal/"],["Público: Quercus reports trampling and grazing in Fanal's protected zone","https://www.publico.pt/2025/09/10/azul/noticia/quercus-denuncia-morte-lenta-fanal-critica-pisoteio-pastoreio-zona-protegida-madeira-2146634"],["JM Madeira: Fanal wedding: Quercus \"does not understand\" IFCN decision","https://jm-madeira.pt/regiao/casamento-fanal-quercus-nao-compreende-decisao-do-ifcn-JC16639743"],["DNoticias: GNR investigates wedding at Fanal","https://www.dnoticias.pt/2024/9/16/420006-gnr-averigua-casamento-no-fanal/"]],"stat":"","link":"https://quercus.pt/blog/2025/09/09/a-morte-lenta-do-fanal/","linkL":"Read the Quercus statement"},"porto-santo-areia":{"corpo":"<p>Porto Santo's beach, around nine kilometres long and often cited as one of the most beautiful in Europe, has repeatedly lost sand for decades. Experts and local officials point to the construction of the Porto Santo Shelter Port, which interrupts the natural flow of water and the circulation of sediment along the coast, a problem worsened by past commercial sand extraction and the 1990 oil spill.</p>\n<p>In December 2024, the beach was once again left bare of sand and covered in pebbles, repeating a winter \"thinning\" cycle that, according to residents and former officials such as Alberto João Jardim, has been worsening over the years.</p>\n<p>In September 2026, redevelopment and dredging works at Porto Santo Marina, carried out by the infrastructure's new concessionaires, removed sand and sediment from the harbour basin to increase its draught. Photographs showed brownish sediment being deposited just metres from the beach and the waterline, in a Blue Flag-classified area, a classification that, under the law, should prevent this kind of intervention outside the closed season. Sediment removed from inside ports frequently accumulates organic waste, heavy metals, fuel and oil, which is why environmental law requires physical-chemical and microbiological laboratory analysis before any dredging or deposition, to ensure the material is not contaminated.</p>\n<p>As of now, it is not publicly known whether those analyses have been disclosed.</p>","fontes":[["DNoticias: Porto Santo has less and less sand because of the Shelter Port","https://www.dnoticias.pt/2022/7/29/322006-praia-do-porto-santo-tem-cada-vez-menos-areia-devido-ao-porto-de-abrigo/"],["DNoticias: Porto Santo beach once again bare of sand and covered in pebbles","https://www.dnoticias.pt/2024/12/18/431396-praia-do-porto-santo-novamente-despida-de-areia-e-coberta-com-calhaus/"],["Funchal Notícias: Sand removed from Porto Santo marina deposited in Blue Flag area","https://funchalnoticias.net/2026/09/02/areias-retiradas-da-marina-do-porto-santo-depositadas-em-zona-de-bandeira-azul/"]],"stat":"","link":"https://funchalnoticias.net/2026/09/02/areias-retiradas-da-marina-do-porto-santo-depositadas-em-zona-de-bandeira-azul/","linkL":"Read on Funchal Notícias"},"mineracao-mar-profundo-acores":{"corpo":"<p>The deep waters around the Azores include hydrothermal fields and seamounts with endemic species and still poorly studied ecosystems, which environmental organisations identify as particularly vulnerable to deep-sea mining: the extraction of polymetallic nodules, crusts and sulphides from the ocean floor. In 2024, organisations including Sciaena, ANP|WWF and the Azores Ocean Observatory (OMA) warned that this activity is \"highly threatening\" to the region's marine biodiversity, and criticised the Azores Maritime Spatial Plan for being silent on an effective ban.</p>\n<p>In May 2023, the Legislative Assembly of the Autonomous Region of the Azores approved a resolution recommending that the regional government apply a moratorium on deep-sea mining in maritime zones under the Region's management, until 1 January 2050. Pressure from these organisations, including a petition delivered to the Azores Parliament by Natureza Portugal/WWF and Sciaena, helped bring the issue to the national Parliament.</p>\n<p>On 14 March 2025, the Assembly of the Republic approved a national moratorium on deep-sea mining until 2050. The law was enacted by the President of the Republic on 21 March and published as Law 36/2025 in the official gazette on 31 March, entering into force on 1 April 2025. It bans the activity in all maritime zones under national jurisdiction, including Azorean waters, until 1 January 2050, making Portugal the first country in the world to adopt a legally binding moratorium on this activity.</p>","fontes":[["Público: Azores give green light to moratorium until 2050 on deep-sea mining","https://www.publico.pt/2023/05/26/azul/noticia/acores-dao-luz-verde-moratoria-ate-2050-mineracao-mar-profundo-2051051"],["Observador: Mining in Azorean waters is \"highly threatening\" to marine biodiversity","https://observador.pt/2024/07/27/mineracao-no-mar-dos-acores-e-altamente-ameacadora-da-biodiversidade-marinha-dizem-ambientalistas/"],["Público: Parliament approves moratorium on deep-sea mining until 2050","https://www.publico.pt/2025/03/14/azul/noticia/parlamento-aprova-moratoria-mineracao-mar-profundo-ate-2050-2125972"],["Público: President enacts moratorium on deep-sea mining until 2050","https://www.publico.pt/2025/03/22/azul/noticia/marcelo-promulga-moratoria-mineracao-mar-profundo-ate-2050-2127033"],["Público: Official: Portugal is the first country to ban deep-sea mineral extraction until 2050","https://www.publico.pt/2025/04/01/azul/noticia/oficial-portugal-pais-proibir-extraccao-minerais-fundo-mar-ate-2050-2128018"]],"stat":"","link":"https://www.publico.pt/2025/04/01/azul/noticia/oficial-portugal-pais-proibir-extraccao-minerais-fundo-mar-ate-2050-2128018","linkL":"Read on Público"},"prospecao-valongo-2":{"corpo":"<p>The \"Valongo 2\" application (MNPPP614), by Braga-based GMR - Consultores, seeks prospecting and exploration rights for nickel, cobalt, copper and platinum-group metals over 105 km2 on the northern slope of Serra da Nogueira, between Bragança and Vinhais. The area overlaps the Natura 2000 network (Montesinho-Nogueira) and the Meseta Ibérica Transboundary Biosphere Reserve.</p>","fontes":[["Mensageiro de Bragança: Bragança Council and parishes oppose mining prospecting (26 Nov 2024) (in Portuguese)","https://www.mdb.pt/noticia/camara-de-braganca-e-juntas-de-freguesia-emitem-posicao-desfavoravel-prospecao-mineira-no"],["Mensageiro de Bragança: mining prospecting projects in protected areas of Montesinho Natural Park and Serra da Nogueira mobilise protests (in Portuguese)","https://www.mdb.pt/noticia/projetos-de-prospecao-mineira-em-areas-protegidas-do-parque-natural-de-montesinho-e-da"],["Público: Bragança and Vinhais against metal prospecting in the region (in Portuguese)","https://www.publico.pt/2025/01/02/azul/noticia/braganca-vinhais-prospeccao-metais-regiao-2117360"],["Participa.pt: official case file for Valongo 2 (MNPPP614, in Portuguese)","https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/pedido-de-atribuicao-de-direitos-de-prospecao-e-pesquisa-valongo-2"],["ICNF: Montesinho Natural Park, description (in Portuguese, accessed 27 Sep 2026)","https://resources.natural.pt/uploads/additional-information/2019/06/12/08/Msm1aTmOfwIWzjc2.pdf"]],"stat":"886 submissions in the public consultation · 105 km2 area · 11 parishes covered","link":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/pedido-de-atribuicao-de-direitos-de-prospecao-e-pesquisa-valongo-2","linkL":"See the official case file on participa.pt (in Portuguese) →","cronologia":[{"data":"2024-09-23","texto":"Public consultation on the Valongo 2 application on the Participa portal, which receives 886 submissions.","fonte":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/pedido-de-atribuicao-de-direitos-de-prospecao-e-pesquisa-valongo-2","dataFim":"2024-11-04"},{"data":"2024-11","texto":"It emerges that ICNF has issued a negative opinion on the prospecting; Vinhais Council's executive decides to oppose the application.","fonte":"https://www.mdb.pt/noticia/projetos-de-prospecao-mineira-em-areas-protegidas-do-parque-natural-de-montesinho-e-da"},{"data":"2024-11-23","texto":"Seven parishes of Bragança covered by the application take a position against it.","fonte":"https://www.mdb.pt/noticia/camara-de-braganca-e-juntas-de-freguesia-emitem-posicao-desfavoravel-prospecao-mineira-no"},{"data":"2024-11-25","texto":"Bragança Council decides to issue an unfavourable opinion, considering the activities that would follow prospecting \"totally incompatible\" with the municipality's natural, cultural, social and economic values.","fonte":"https://www.mdb.pt/noticia/camara-de-braganca-e-juntas-de-freguesia-emitem-posicao-desfavoravel-prospecao-mineira-no"},{"data":"2025-03-27","texto":"The participation process is formally closed; the Directorate-General for Energy and Geology has not made a final decision public.","fonte":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/pedido-de-atribuicao-de-direitos-de-prospecao-e-pesquisa-valongo-2"}],"contexto":"The \"Valongo 2\" application (MNPPP614), by Braga-based GMR - Consultores, seeks prospecting and exploration rights for nickel, cobalt, copper and platinum-group metals over 105 km2 on the northern slope of Serra da Nogueira, between Bragança and Vinhais. The area overlaps the Natura 2000 network (Montesinho-Nogueira) and the Meseta Ibérica Transboundary Biosphere Reserve."},"prospecao-revelhe":{"corpo":"<p>The \"Revelhe\" request (MNPPP613), filed by the same company, GMR - Consultores, Lda., asks for prospecting and research rights over gold, silver, copper, lead, zinc and associated mineral deposits across a 37.8 km2 area in five parishes of Vinhais: Santalha, Tuizelo, Candedo, Vilar de Ossos and the Sobreiró de Baixo e Alvaredos union of parishes. The area lies inside Montesinho Natural Park and the UNESCO-recognised Transboundary Biosphere Reserve of Meseta Ibérica.</p><p>The ICNF and the Bragança and Vinhais town councils issued unfavourable opinions on the request. The public consultation, open from 16 September to 25 October 2024, gathered 157 submissions on the participa.pt portal and formally closed on 25 February 2025, with no final decision made public so far by the Directorate-General for Energy and Geology.</p><p>Sara Riso, spokesperson for the UIVO movement, says the ICNF's unfavourable opinion was only filed on the last day of the Revelhe consultation, when it should have been available from the start, and questions the absence of an environmental mitigation plan or a benefit-sharing strategy with local communities. Streams that supply water to communities in the region rise within the project area, in a district already under tight irrigation management because of drought.</p><p>For mobilised residents, the two requests, Revelhe and Valongo 2, cover roughly 140 km2 combined and represent the opening of a \"Pandora's box\" toward a future mining phase, incompatible with the nature-tourism and young-family-retention strategy pursued by the Terras de Trás-os-Montes Intermunicipal Community.</p><p>The requested area lies inside Montesinho Natural Park. According to the ICNF's description of the park, accessed on 27 September 2026, Montesinho Natural Park is home to around 250 vertebrate species and 70% of the land mammal species found in Portugal, around 10% of which are listed as threatened in the Portuguese Red Book of Vertebrates. It holds one of the most important Iberian wolf populations and the only viable populations of freshwater pearl mussel (Margaritifera margaritifera) known in Portugal, and is part of the \"Montesinho-Nogueira\" Site of Community Importance and Special Protection Area of the Natura 2000 network.</p>","fontes":[["Mensageiro de Bragança: mining prospecting projects in protected areas of Montesinho Natural Park and Serra da Nogueira mobilise protests (in Portuguese)","https://www.mdb.pt/noticia/projetos-de-prospecao-mineira-em-areas-protegidas-do-parque-natural-de-montesinho-e-da"],["Observador: Bragança municipality issues unfavourable opinion on mining prospecting request (in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2024/11/26/municipio-de-braganca-emite-parecer-desfavoravel-a-pedido-de-prospecao-mineira/"],["Público: Bragança and Vinhais against metal prospecting in the region (in Portuguese)","https://www.publico.pt/2025/01/02/azul/noticia/braganca-vinhais-prospeccao-metais-regiao-2117360"],["Participa.pt: official case file for Revelhe (MNPPP613, in Portuguese)","https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/pedido-de-atribuicao-de-direitos-de-prospecao-e-pesquisa-revelhe"],["ICNF: Montesinho Natural Park, description (in Portuguese, accessed 27 Sep 2026)","https://resources.natural.pt/uploads/additional-information/2019/06/12/08/Msm1aTmOfwIWzjc2.pdf"]],"stat":"157 submissions in the public consultation · 37.8 km2 area · 5 parishes covered","link":"https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/pedido-de-atribuicao-de-direitos-de-prospecao-e-pesquisa-revelhe","linkL":"See the official case file on participa.pt (in Portuguese) →"},"up12-albandeira":{"corpo":"<p>Planning Unit 12 (UP12) provides for hotels, aparthotels and tourist villas with 1,030 beds on the coastal strip between Praia da Marinha and Nossa Senhora da Rocha, in Lagoa, next to the Pedra do Valado Marine Protected Area. The ATE A1 detailed plan received unfavourable opinions from the Environment Agency, ICNF, CCDR-Algarve and DGT.</p>","fontes":[["STOP UP12: UP12 history","https://stopup12.com/up12-history/"],["Stop UP12 Lagoa: the movement's official website (also in English)","https://stopup12.com/"],["Sul Informação: chef João Marreiros joins STOP UP12 to defend the Albandeira area, in Lagoa (in Portuguese)","https://www.sulinformacao.pt/2026/03/chef-joao-marreiros-junta-se-ao-stop-up12-para-defender-area-de-albandeira-em-lagoa/"],["diariOnline Região Sul: defending the Algarve coast, STOP UP12 challenges Lagoa Council (in Portuguese)","https://regiao-sul.pt/ambiente/em-defesa-do-litoral-algarvio-stop-up12-contesta-camara-de-lagoa/744345"],["Lagoa Municipal Council: Elaboration of the Albandeira ATE A1 detailed plan (in Portuguese)","https://www.cm-lagoa.pt/noticia/elaboracao-do-plano-de-pormenor-de-albandeira-ate-a1"],["Lagoa Municipal Council: Decision to start/restart the Albandeira ATE A2 detailed plan (in Portuguese)","https://www.cm-lagoa.pt/noticia/decisao-de-inicio-reinicio-da-elaboracao-do-plano-de-pormenor-de-albandeira-ate-a2"],["Portugal Resident: environmental group launches first legal action to halt Lagoa's Albandeira plan (Jan 2026)","https://www.portugalresident.com/environmental-group-launches-first-legal-action-to-halt-lagoas-albandeira-plan/"],["STOP UP12: Albandeira, project description and UP12 history","https://stopup12.com/albandeira/"]],"stat":"1,030 beds planned · 220 hectares covered · court injunction has blocked the process since 23 Jan 2026","link":"https://stopup12.com/","linkL":"Visit the STOP UP12 movement's website →","cronologia":[{"data":"1991","texto":"The Algarve Regional Spatial Plan is approved; Lagoa Council includes the tourist development areas in UP12.","fonte":"https://stopup12.com/up12-history/"},{"data":"2008-02-08","texto":"The UP12 land-use conditions that still apply today are set.","fonte":"https://stopup12.com/up12-history/"},{"data":"2011","texto":"Lagoa Council grants Obriverca a permit for the \"Resort Praia da Marinha\" tourist development.","fonte":"https://stopup12.com/up12-history/"},{"data":"2020-10-21","texto":"Lagoa Council and the Predicapital fund sign preliminary contracts for the ATE A1 and ATE A2 areas.","fonte":"https://stopup12.com/up12-history/"},{"data":"2023-12-15","texto":"Lagoa Council decides to draw up the Albandeira detailed plan for ATE A1.","fonte":"https://www.cm-lagoa.pt/noticia/elaboracao-do-plano-de-pormenor-de-albandeira-ate-a1"},{"data":"2024-07-18","texto":"The decision is published in the Official Journal, with 15 working days for public participation.","fonte":"https://www.cm-lagoa.pt/noticia/elaboracao-do-plano-de-pormenor-de-albandeira-ate-a1"},{"data":"2025-10-07","texto":"Lagoa Council decides to start or restart the detailed plan for ATE A2, with an 18-month deadline.","fonte":"https://www.cm-lagoa.pt/noticia/decisao-de-inicio-reinicio-da-elaboracao-do-plano-de-pormenor-de-albandeira-ate-a2"},{"data":"2025-12-24","texto":"Preliminary public participation period of 15 working days, over the Christmas and New Year holidays.","fonte":"https://www.cm-lagoa.pt/noticia/decisao-de-inicio-reinicio-da-elaboracao-do-plano-de-pormenor-de-albandeira-ate-a2","dataFim":"2026-01-16"},{"data":"2026-01-05","texto":"STOP UP12 files an action at the Loulé Administrative Court against the Council's decision to restart the Albandeira detailed plan.","fonte":"https://www.portugalresident.com/environmental-group-launches-first-legal-action-to-halt-lagoas-albandeira-plan/"}],"contexto":"Planning Unit 12 (UP12) provides for hotels, aparthotels and tourist villas with 1,030 beds on the coastal strip between Praia da Marinha and Nossa Senhora da Rocha, in Lagoa, next to the Pedra do Valado Marine Protected Area. The ATE A1 detailed plan received unfavourable opinions from the Environment Agency, ICNF, CCDR-Algarve and DGT."},"muda-defesa-arvores":{"corpo":"<p>MUDA (Movimento Muda de Árvore, also known as the Movement for the Union in Defence of Trees) denounces the systematic felling of trees along roadsides and railways across the country, carried out by Infraestruturas de Portugal (IP) and by local municipalities, often without prior notice or environmental impact assessment.</p>\n<p>In March 2024, the movement joined 17 other environmental associations in a public petition that described the felling as an “ecocide” and called for intervention by the Government, municipal councils, ICNF and APA. In Rio Maior, a group of citizens even took a case over tree felling on the EN 114 road to court.</p>\n<p>In March 2025, MUDA held a protest on Avenida 5 de Outubro in Lisbon, hanging banners against the felling of jacaranda trees to make way for an underground car park, a case that gathered over 54,000 signatures and became the most-supported citizen petition in the city's history. Spokesperson Rui Mourão pointed to “serious procedural irregularities” by Lisbon City Council, namely regarding Law 59/2021, the municipal tree management regulation and ICNF's code of good practice.</p>\n<p>MUDA is calling for compliance with Law 59/2021, which regulates tree felling in public space, is compiling a map of municipalities in breach of it, and has asked Parliament to finally regulate the penalties set out in the law, which the Government has still not defined more than four years on.</p>","fontes":[["Esquerda.net: Environmentalists launch petition against mass tree felling by IP","https://www.esquerda.net/artigo/ambientalistas-lancam-peticao-contra-abate-massivo-de-arvores-pela-ip/90351"],["Região de Rio Maior: Citizens against tree felling on the EN 114","https://regiaoriomaior.pt/cidadaos-contra-abate-de-arvores-na-en-114/"],["PÚBLICO (opinion, by Rui Mourão): Warning, there's an ecocide wherever it goes!","https://www.publico.pt/2024/04/15/opiniao/opiniao/alerta-ha-ecocidio-onde-passa-2086974"],["Notícias ao Minuto/Lusa: Lisbon City Council began planting jacaranda trees, but opposition continues","https://www.noticiasaominuto.com/pais/2756379/camara-de-lisboa-comecou-a-plantar-jacarandas-mas-contestacao-mantem-se"],["Time Out Lisboa: Disillusioned citizens demand consequences for tree felling in Lisbon","https://www.timeout.pt/lisboa/pt/noticias/descrentes-e-desiludidos-cidadaos-pedem-consequencias-para-abate-de-arvores-em-lisboa-072926"],["Public Petition","https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=PT120154"]],"stat":"","link":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/movimentodefesaarvores","linkL":"Learn more on MUDA's Facebook"},"sintra-sem-herbicidas":{"corpo":"<p>The Sintra sem Herbicidas movement reports the use of glyphosate and other herbicides in public spaces in Sintra and calls for a nationwide ban in urban public spaces.</p>","fontes":[["Esquerda.net (2017): Sintra, eradication of herbicides in public space, a promise still unmet","https://www.esquerda.net/opiniao/sintra-erradicacao-de-herbicidas-no-espaco-publico-promessa-por-cumprir/50944"],["Sintra Notícias (2019): Sintra eliminates glyphosate from public space","https://sintranoticias.pt/2019/06/17/sintra-elimina-glifosato-do-espaco-publico/"],["Jornal de Mafra (2019): Quercus, complaints about glyphosate use in Mafra, Sintra and Torres Vedras reach the GNR","https://jornaldemafra.pt/quercus-queixas-sobre-utilizacao-de-glifosato-em-mafra-sintra-e-torres-vedras-chegam-a-gnr/"],["Quercus: Municipalities Without Glyphosate/Herbicides Campaign","https://quercus.pt/campanha-autarquias-sem-glifosato-herbicidas/"],["Portuguese Parliament/Participa: Petition 102/XVII/1.ª for the prohibition of dangerous herbicides in urban public spaces in Portugal (archived, in Portuguese)","https://participacao.parlamento.pt/initiatives/5269"],["Sintra sem Herbicidas: statement on the mailing campaign to parliamentary groups and other bodies (Sep 2026, in Portuguese)","https://sintrasemherbicidas.wordpress.com/apoioproibicao/"]],"stat":"","link":"https://sintrasemherbicidas.wordpress.com/","linkL":"Learn more at sintrasemherbicidas.wordpress.com","cronologia":[{"data":"2015","texto":"Sintra Council adopts a plan to phase out glyphosate in public spaces.","fonte":"https://www.esquerda.net/opiniao/sintra-erradicacao-de-herbicidas-no-espaco-publico-promessa-por-cumprir/50944"},{"data":"2019-03","texto":"Quercus reports complaints about glyphosate use in several municipalities to the GNR, calling the situation \"particularly serious in the municipality of Sintra\".","fonte":"https://jornaldemafra.pt/quercus-queixas-sobre-utilizacao-de-glifosato-em-mafra-sintra-e-torres-vedras-chegam-a-gnr/"},{"data":"2019-06-17","texto":"Sintra Council announces it has eliminated glyphosate from public spaces, replacing it with a pelargonic acid-based herbicide.","fonte":"https://sintranoticias.pt/2019/06/17/sintra-elimina-glifosato-do-espaco-publico/"},{"data":"2026-02","texto":"A rapporteur is appointed in Parliament for the national petition to ban hazardous herbicides in urban public spaces (Petition 102/XVII/1).","fonte":"https://participacao.parlamento.pt/initiatives/5269"},{"data":"2026-06","texto":"The petitioner is heard by the Agriculture and Fisheries Committee, together with the president of Quercus; the petition is later archived.","fonte":"https://participacao.parlamento.pt/initiatives/5269"},{"data":"2026-09","texto":"The Sintra sem Herbicidas movement launches a mailing campaign to parliamentary groups and other public bodies so that the issue is not dropped.","fonte":"https://sintrasemherbicidas.wordpress.com/apoioproibicao/"}],"contexto":"The Sintra sem Herbicidas movement reports the use of glyphosate and other herbicides in public spaces in Sintra and calls for a nationwide ban in urban public spaces."},"aterro-barlavento":{"corpo":"<p>The Barlavento Sanitary Landfill is located in Porto de Lagos, Portimão municipality, bordering Silves, and is run by Algar, the company that manages urban waste for the Algarve's 16 municipalities. The site is close to maximum capacity, and residents of Odelouca, Porto de Lagos and Rasmalho have lived for months with unbearable smell and swarms of flies.</p>\n<p>On 12 March 2026, the Associação de Moradores de Odelouca, Porto de Lagos e Rasmalho organised a protest outside the landfill, covered by national broadcaster RTP and the local press. One resident told the Portugal Resident that her kitchen floor and counters were completely covered with flies, and that “it becomes impossible to cook”. Environmentalist António Lambe, from Ação Ambiental para o Barlavento, who has followed Algarve landfill projects since the 1990s, said the problem is not an isolated case and stressed the importance of educating younger generations about the impacts of poor waste management.</p>\n<p>Instead of considering closure, Algar plans to expand the site with a new cell, Cell E, covering around 98,900 m² with capacity for 150,000 tonnes of waste a year. In November 2025, ZERO accused Algar of breaching the law by continuing to dump untreated organic waste, around 40% of what enters the landfill, a practice banned under Decree-Law 24/2024. According to ZERO, Algar's own environmental impact study admits the landfill is responsible for 55% of greenhouse gas emissions in Portimão municipality.</p>\n<p>In 2024, Algar had already tried to expropriate land in Silves to expand the landfill. Silves Municipal Council unanimously opposed the move, backed by PSD and PS councillors, recalling that it had also unanimously opposed a similar attempt in 1995, at the time accompanied by strong popular mobilisation.</p>","fontes":[["Portugal Resident: “Enough!”: Dozens protest outside Portimão landfill","https://www.portugalresident.com/enough-dozens-protest-outside-portimao-landfill/"],["RTP: Aterro Sanitário do Barlavento a atingir a capacidade máxima gera protesto","https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/pais/aterro-sanitario-do-barlavento-a-atingir-a-capacidade-maxima-gera-protesto_v1725741"],["Terra Ruiva: Algar quer expropriar para ampliar Aterro Sanitário do Barlavento para o concelho de Silves","https://www.terraruiva.pt/2024/10/13/algar-quer-expropriar-para-ampliar-aterro-sanitario-do-barlavento-para-o-concelho-de-silves/"],["GEOTA: TerraSeixe Project, partnership with Ação Ambiental para o Barlavento","https://www.geota.pt/projetos/terraseixe"]],"stat":"","link":"","linkL":""},"pinhal-freiras-seixal":{"corpo":"<p>The Pinhal das Freiras, in Mata de Belverde, Seixal municipality, is a forested area that forms part of the Fernão Ferro/Lagoa de Albufeira Special Conservation Area (ZEC), protected under the Natura 2000 network since 2000. Plans to urbanise the area date back at least to the 1990s, but gained new urgency in 2024: on 26 June, Seixal Municipal Council decided to start drafting the UOPG 33 Pinhal das Freiras Urban Development Plan, with a 24-month deadline and a preliminary public participation period between August and October 2024. The Salvar a Floresta do Seixal movement describes the project as a 2.5 million m² development on the site, excluding green spaces from the design.</p>\n<p>The citizens' movement Salvar a Floresta do Seixal, which has opposed the plan since then, estimates the loss of around 50,000 trees, 2.5 km² of forest, and 200 km of trails and cycle paths from the municipality's trail network, which had received more than €72,000 in European funding through POSEUR. According to the movement, the planned building complex, up to 19 metres tall, could have capacity for more than 90,000 new residents, with serious impacts on the quality of life of those already living in the area.</p>\n<p>In March 2025, residents formalised the environmental association Seixal+Verde, which launched a petition to the Portuguese Parliament against the urbanisation of Pinhal das Freiras (UOPG 33), asking that the area be turned into a Nature Reserve or Natural Park, or that strict environmental rules be applied to the plan. The petition, delivered with more than 7,700 signatures, was admitted as petition no. 166/XVII/1, with a rapporteur appointed in June 2026, awaiting review by the Environment and Energy Committee. It is currently closed to new signatures.</p>\n<p>Seixal+Verde met with Seixal Municipal Council in 2025 and 2026, and organised a public protest outside the council offices on 1 September 2026, calling for the project to be revised.</p>\n<p>On 17 June 2026, Seixal Municipal Council approved a 24-month extension of the deadline for drafting the UOPG 33 Pinhal das Freiras Urban Development Plan (Resolution no. 196/2026), published in the Diário da República on 24 July 2026. The plan is therefore still being drafted.</p>","fontes":[["Time Out Lisboa: Câmara do Seixal acusada de destruir “o último pulmão da Margem Sul”","https://www.timeout.pt/lisboa/pt/noticias/cidadaos-mobilizam-se-contra-urbanizacao-em-area-florestal-do-seixal-121624"],["PÚBLICO: Um grupo de moradores quer salvar o “último pulmão verde” do Seixal","https://www.publico.pt/2025/03/22/azul/noticia/grupo-moradores-quer-salvar-ultimo-pulmao-verde-seixal-2126896"],["Portuguese Parliament: Petition 166/XVII/1, Pela Defesa da Biodiversidade no Pinhal das Freiras","https://participacao.parlamento.pt/initiatives/5637"],["Seixal+Verde: official website","https://www.seixalmaisverde.org/"],["Seixal Municipal Council: UOPG 33 Pinhal das Freiras Urban Development Plan (16 Aug 2024) (in Portuguese)","https://www.cm-seixal.pt/noticia/plano-de-urbanizacao-da-uopg-33-pinhal-das-freiras-0"],["Seixal Municipal Council: Deadline for the Pinhal das Freiras Urban Development Plan extended (28 Jul 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.cm-seixal.pt/noticia/prorrogado-prazo-do-plano-de-urbanizacao-do-pinhal-das-freiras"]],"stat":"","link":"https://www.seixalmaisverde.org/","linkL":"Saber mais em seixalmaisverde.org"},"eolicas-serra-ossa":{"corpo":"<p>Serra d'Ossa, in the municipality of Estremoz, is one of the most emblematic landscapes of Central Alentejo, with cork oak woodland, protected birds of prey and bats, and megalithic, Roman and medieval remains. At its foot lies the environmental legacy of the former Mostardeira mine.</p>","fontes":[["Petição Pública: Não às Eólicas na Serra d'Ossa (public petition)","https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=PT132905"],["ODigital.pt: Estremoz declara de Interesse Municipal a instalação de parque eólico no concelho","https://odigital.sapo.pt/estremoz-declara-de-interesse-municipal-a-instalacao-de-parque-eolico-no-concelho/"],["Rádio Campanário, 21 Sep 2026: Possible wind farm on Serra d'Ossa sparks opposition (in Portuguese)","https://www.radiocampanario.com/possivel-parque-eolico-na-serra-dossa-gera-contestacao-moradores-pedem-travao-aos-estudos-para-eventual-instalacao/"],["Rádio Campanário, 26 Sep 2026: Estremoz Municipal Assembly rejects wind project on Serra d'Ossa (in Portuguese)","https://www.radiocampanario.com/assembleia-municipal-de-estremoz-chumba-projeto-eolico-na-serra-dossa/"]],"stat":"","link":"","linkL":"","cronologia":[{"data":"2025-03","texto":"The Mayor of Estremoz confirms that a wind project for Serra d'Ossa did not get approval for measuring towers; another project, at Herdade da Fonte Figueira, is declared of municipal interest.","fonte":"https://odigital.sapo.pt/estremoz-declara-de-interesse-municipal-a-instalacao-de-parque-eolico-no-concelho/"},{"data":"2026-09-15","texto":"A public petition is launched against wind farms in Serra d'Ossa, also calling for it to be classified as a protected area.","fonte":"https://peticaopublica.com/pview.aspx?pi=PT132905"},{"data":"2026-09-18","texto":"The agenda of the Estremoz Municipal Assembly includes a declaration of municipal interest for wind-measuring masts in Serra d'Ossa, a preparatory step for an Akuo wind farm that could have 13 turbines.","fonte":"https://www.radiocampanario.com/possivel-parque-eolico-na-serra-dossa-gera-contestacao-moradores-pedem-travao-aos-estudos-para-eventual-instalacao/"},{"data":"2026-09-21","texto":"A group of residents writes to the municipal groups asking for rejection, citing impacts on cork oak woodland, protected birds of prey and bats.","fonte":"https://www.radiocampanario.com/possivel-parque-eolico-na-serra-dossa-gera-contestacao-moradores-pedem-travao-aos-estudos-para-eventual-instalacao/"},{"data":"2026-09-25","texto":"Estremoz Municipal Assembly rejects the wind-measuring masts proposal, with 26 votes against, 3 in favour and 1 abstention.","fonte":"https://www.radiocampanario.com/assembleia-municipal-de-estremoz-chumba-projeto-eolico-na-serra-dossa/"}],"contexto":"Serra d'Ossa, in the municipality of Estremoz, is one of the most emblematic landscapes of Central Alentejo, with cork oak woodland, protected birds of prey and bats, and megalithic, Roman and medieval remains. At its foot lies the environmental legacy of the former Mostardeira mine."},"amianto-vale-milhacos-seixal":{"corpo":"<p>Vale de Milhaços Primary and Middle School, head of a cluster of 10 schools and kindergartens in Corroios, Seixal, still has asbestos-cement panels on the roofs of some areas where pupils and staff spend long periods.</p>","fontes":[["O Setubalense/Lusa: Over a dozen schools in Seixal closed due to protest (12 Mar 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://osetubalense.com/local/seixal/mais-de-uma-dezena-de-escolas-no-concelho-do-seixal-fechadas-devido-a-protesto"],["S.TO.P. union: letter to the Ministry of Education and Seixal City Council (20 Mar 2026, in Portuguese)","https://stop-sindicato.pt/s-to-p-envia-carta-ao-meci-e-cm-do-seixal-exigindo-a-remocao-de-amianto-e-a-resolucao-de-outros-problemas-no-ae-de-vale-de-milhacos/"],["ADN, Agência de Notícias, Mar 2026: Asbestos, leaks and decay: Seixal school awaits funding for works (in Portuguese)","https://www.adn-agenciadenoticias.com/2026/03/amianto-infiltracoes-e-degradacao.html"],["S.TO.P.: S.TO.P. and Vale de Milhaços school staff met Seixal City Council (6 Apr 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://stop-sindicato.pt/s-to-p-e-profissionais-de-educacao-do-ae-de-vale-de-milhacos-reuniram-com-a-camara-municipal-do-seixal/"],["Saúde+ TV/Lusa: Seixal education staff demanded asbestos removal and more operational assistants (22 Apr 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://www.saudemais.tv/noticia/64074-profissionais-de-educacao-do-seixal-exigiram-retirada-de-amianto-e-mais-assistentes-operacionais"],["O Setubalense/Lusa: Seixal education staff rally in Lisbon to demand asbestos removal (20 May 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://osetubalense.com/local/seixal/profissionais-de-educacao-do-seixal-concentram-se-em-lisboa-para-exigir-remocao-de-amianto"]],"stat":"10 schools in the group, more than half closed in protest","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/03/12/seixal-varias-escolas-fechadas-devido-a-protesto/","linkL":"Read on Observador","cronologia":[{"data":"2026-03-12","texto":"More than a hundred staff of the school cluster protest at the main school against the failure to remove the asbestos roofing and the lack of support staff; more than half of the 10 schools close that morning.","fonte":"https://osetubalense.com/local/seixal/mais-de-uma-dezena-de-escolas-no-concelho-do-seixal-fechadas-devido-a-protesto"},{"data":"2026-03","texto":"Seixal Council says the school, built in 1988, urgently needs refurbishment and that the project to remove the asbestos is ready but not yet funded.","fonte":"https://www.adn-agenciadenoticias.com/2026/03/amianto-infiltracoes-e-degradacao.html"},{"data":"2026-03-20","texto":"S.TO.P. sends a letter to the Ministry of Education and Seixal Council asking for dates and deadlines to deal with the asbestos, leaks and the lack of a sports hall.","fonte":"https://stop-sindicato.pt/s-to-p-envia-carta-ao-meci-e-cm-do-seixal-exigindo-a-remocao-de-amianto-e-a-resolucao-de-outros-problemas-no-ae-de-vale-de-milhacos/"},{"data":"2026-04-06","texto":"A delegation of the union and staff meets the councillor for Education; according to the union, the Council has not applied for funding for this school.","fonte":"https://stop-sindicato.pt/s-to-p-e-profissionais-de-educacao-do-ae-de-vale-de-milhacos-reuniram-com-a-camara-municipal-do-seixal/"},{"data":"2026-04-22","texto":"Staff protest outside Seixal Council; the Mayor says the criteria for choosing which schools to refurbish were never explained to the Council.","fonte":"https://www.saudemais.tv/noticia/64074-profissionais-de-educacao-do-seixal-exigiram-retirada-de-amianto-e-mais-assistentes-operacionais"},{"data":"2026-05-20","texto":"About 30 Seixal school staff gather outside the Ministry of Education in Lisbon to demand the removal of the asbestos.","fonte":"https://osetubalense.com/local/seixal/profissionais-de-educacao-do-seixal-concentram-se-em-lisboa-para-exigir-remocao-de-amianto"}],"contexto":"Vale de Milhaços Primary and Middle School, head of a cluster of 10 schools and kindergartens in Corroios, Seixal, still has asbestos-cement panels on the roofs of some areas where pupils and staff spend long periods."},"rio-lis-poluicao":{"corpo":"<p>On 12 August 2025, a breakdown at the Monte Real pumping station in Leiria municipality, run by the company Águas do Centro Litoral (AdCL), forced the discharge of thousands of cubic metres of untreated effluent into the Lis river, which flows out at Vieira Beach in Marinha Grande municipality, and into irrigation channels. The Portuguese Environment Agency estimated that between 20,000 and 25,000 m³ of raw sewage were released into the river. At the time, swimming was banned at Vieira Beach for three days, and Leiria Municipality advised against irrigation, swimming and fishing in the stretch of river downstream of Monte Real.</p>\n<p>Marinha Grande City Council set up a support service for those affected by the discharge. In August 2026, AdCL confirmed it had received 12 claims from potential claimants, totalling around €256,000, with individual amounts ranging from €400 to €160,000, covering mostly agriculture, fishing, catering and retail. The compensation process is being handled by AdCL's insurer, with no payment made as of the report's date.</p>\n<p>AdCL says it has, since the breakdown, reinforced the ultraviolet disinfection system at the Coimbrão wastewater treatment plant and repaired the pumping system at the Monte Real station, and has under way a project to redirect effluent from the Vieira de Leiria plant to Coimbrão for treatment, plus an investment of around €1 million to reinforce the resilience of four pumping stations after storm damage in early 2026. A remodelling of the Coimbrão plant is also planned, with an estimated investment of €32 million.</p>\n<p>In September 2026, the environmental association Oikos, as part of the \"Lis River Basin: Acting to Know, Protect and Value\" project, collected water samples at 18 points across the river basin in June 2026, together with the Leiria Local Health Unit's Health Authority. Results remained within the historical range for most points, but the association flagged a pollution hotspot with \"concerning\" levels on the Lena river, a Lis tributary, in the Parque Verde area of Leiria.</p>","fontes":[["Região de Leiria/Lusa news agency: Lesados reclamam 256 mil euros por danos após avaria que provocou poluição no rio Lis (10 Aug 2026, in Portuguese)","https://www.regiaodeleiria.pt/2026/08/lesados-reclamam-256-mil-euros-por-danos-apos-avaria-que-provocou-poluicao-no-rio-lis/"],["Diário de Leiria: Rio Lena no Parque Verde com valores de poluição \"preocupantes\" (10 Sep 2026, in Portuguese)","https://www.diarioleiria.pt/2026/09/10/rio-lena-no-parque-verde-com-valores-de-poluicao-preocupantes/"]],"stat":"20,000 to 25,000 m³ of raw sewage discharged (Aug. 2025)","link":"https://www.regiaodeleiria.pt/2026/08/lesados-reclamam-256-mil-euros-por-danos-apos-avaria-que-provocou-poluicao-no-rio-lis/","linkL":"Read on Região de Leiria"},"cluster-alqueva-chint":{"corpo":"<p>In June 2026, Chint Solar submitted a scoping proposal, the initial step of environmental licensing, for the \"Alqueva Cluster\": the São Gião (564 MW), Tapada Grande (580 MW) and Monte Santos (111 MW) solar plants, with battery systems totalling 895 MW, and about 50 MW of wind power, in Portel and Vidigueira.</p><p>According to Jornal Económico, the cluster would have more than 2.1 million solar panels and produce 1,868 GWh a year. The investment value has not been made public.</p>","fontes":[["Portugal Resident: Chinese developer advances another hybrid energy project in Alentejo","https://www.portugalresident.com/chinese-developer-advances-another-hybrid-energy-project-in-alentejo/"],["Jornal Económico: Chinese group with 1.3 gigawatts of solar and wind projects in Alentejo (in Portuguese)","https://jornaleconomico.sapo.pt/noticias/chineses-com-projetos-solares-e-eolicos-de-13-gigas-no-alentejo/"],["A Planície: Chinese firms invest in three solar and wind plants in Vidigueira and Portel (in Portuguese)","https://planicie.pt/noticias/chineses-investem-em-tres-centrais-solares-e-eolicas-em-vidigueira-e-portel"]],"stat":"~1,300 MW · more than 2.1 million panels · Portel and Vidigueira","link":"https://jornaleconomico.sapo.pt/noticias/chineses-com-projetos-solares-e-eolicos-de-13-gigas-no-alentejo/","linkL":"Read on Observador"},"aterro-castelo-branco-biosmart":{"corpo":"<p>The Castelo Branco non-hazardous industrial waste landfill, in Vedulho de Baixo, opened in 2003 and is run by BioSmart, Soluções Ambientais, S.A.. The expansion project, in public consultation on the Participa portal between 13 July and 21 August 2026, involves building a third cell, raising total deposition capacity from 488,750 tonnes (425,000 m³) to 639,250 tonnes (565,000 m³).</p>\n<p>In a statement on 8 September 2026, the ZERO association issued a negative opinion on the project, saying it did not understand how CCDR Centro could have put it out for public consultation given it was \"clearly illegal\". According to ZERO, the environmental impact study allowed for the possibility of the new cell receiving organic waste, whose landfill deposition has been banned since 1 January 2026 under the Legal Regime for Waste Landfill Deposition, which requires prior treatment and stabilisation of the organic fraction before deposition.</p>\n<p>ZERO is asking CCDR Centro not to license the new cell until organic waste is removed from the list of waste the site is authorised to receive, citing as precedent the Resilei landfill in Leiria, where CCDR Centro refused to authorise organic waste deposition in a similar situation. The landfill has faced previous controversies, including environmental infractions recorded in 2018 over receiving asbestos-containing construction materials.</p>","fontes":[["Participa.pt: official public consultation record for the BioSmart Castelo Branco landfill expansion, 3rd cell (in Portuguese)","https://participa.pt/pt/consulta/projeto-de-ampliacao-do-aterro-de-residuos-nao-perigosos-de-castelo-branco-da-biosmart-3a-celula"],["Observador/Lusa news agency: Zero critica ampliação de aterro de resíduos não perigosos em Castelo Branco (8 Sep 2026, in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2026/09/08/zero-critica-ampliacao-de-aterro-de-residuos-nao-perigosos-em-castelo-branco/"]],"stat":"639,250 t planned total capacity","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/09/08/zero-critica-ampliacao-de-aterro-de-residuos-nao-perigosos-em-castelo-branco/","linkL":"Read on Observador"},"aterro-lustosa-lousada":{"corpo":"<p>The Lustosa non-hazardous industrial waste landfill, in the Union of the Lustosa and Barrosas parishes, Lousada municipality, is run by RIMA, a company held by Mota-Engil Ambiente e Serviços, SUMA (Serviços Urbanos e Meio Ambiente), Lousada Municipality and IDAMBI, Estudos e Projetos do Ambiente. It operates under an environmental licence renewed in 2017.</p>\n<p>In September 2026, CCDR Norte opened a public consultation, running until 30 September, on the landfill's alteration project, which involves reconfiguring already-licensed, operating cells, including infrastructure for a new cell 2. Lousada Municipal Council opposes the proposed changes.</p>\n<p>The landfill has drawn controversy before: in 2020, it was confirmed to be receiving non-hazardous industrial waste imported from Italy, prompting the Bloco de Esquerda to question the Government about the origin, quantity and type of that waste, and about the annual environmental reports RIMA is required to submit to the Portuguese Environment Agency and CCDR Norte.</p>","fontes":[["SAPO/Lusa news agency: Câmara de Lousada contesta alterações no aterro de Lustosa em consulta pública (Sep 2026, in Portuguese)","https://sapo.pt/artigo/camara-de-lousada-contesta-alteracoes-no-aterro-de-lustosa-em-consulta-publica-6aac2bb47a663ca5d3de0b3b"],["Bloco de Esquerda, Porto district: parliamentary question on waste imported from Italy to the Lustosa landfill (historical context, 2020, in Portuguese)","https://santotirso.bloco.org/iniciativas-dos-deputados/bloco-questiona-governo-sobre-o-lixo-importado-de-italia-depositado-no-ate"]],"stat":"Public consultation until 30 Sep 2026","link":"https://sapo.pt/artigo/camara-de-lousada-contesta-alteracoes-no-aterro-de-lustosa-em-consulta-publica-6aac2bb47a663ca5d3de0b3b","linkL":"Read on SAPO"},"hotel-vale-olival-armacao-pera":{"corpo":"<p>Silves Municipal Council issued, on 3 December 2025, the building permit for a four-star hotel in Vale do Olival, Armação de Pêra, with 250 rooms, capacity for 500 guests, indoor and outdoor pools, and technical and parking areas. The architecture project was approved under the Armação de Pêra Detailed Plan and received favourable opinions from Turismo de Portugal and the Portuguese Environment Agency. The investment is estimated at 50 million euros, with a 36-month construction schedule.</p><p>The process sparked strong local controversy, especially on social media, because the plot occupies one of the last vacant beachfront spaces in Armação de Pêra and sits on a cliff considered unstable, on top of worsening existing parking problems in the area. A public petition against the project gathered several hundred signatures.</p><p>Facing the backlash, Silves Municipal Council held a public information session on 18 December 2025 at the \"Os Armacenenses\" football club in Armação de Pêra to explain the licensing process. Site preparation works had already started before that session and continued as of September 2026.</p>","fontes":[["Silves Municipal Council official site: hotel construction licensing in Vale do Olival, Armação de Pêra (5 Dec 2025, in Portuguese)","https://www.cm-silves.pt/pt/noticias/32620/licenciamento-das-obras-de-construcao-de-empreendimento-turistico-no-vale-do-olival-em-armacao-de-pera.aspx"],["Algarve Marafado: information session on controversial hotel construction in Armação de Pêra (12 Dec 2025, in Portuguese)","https://www.algarvemarafado.com/2025/12/12/sessao-de-esclarecimento-sobre-construcao-de-polemico-hotel-em-armacao-de-pera/"],["Mais Algarve: Silves | Vale do Olival hotel licensing (Armação de Pêra) (5 Dec 2025, in Portuguese)","https://maisalgarve.pt/2025/12/05/silves-licenciamento-hotel-no-vale-olival-a-pera/"]],"stat":"50-million-euro investment, 250 rooms","link":"https://www.algarvemarafado.com/2025/12/12/sessao-de-esclarecimento-sobre-construcao-de-polemico-hotel-em-armacao-de-pera/","linkL":"Read on Algarve Marafado"},"poluicao-rio-tejo-protejo":{"corpo":"<p>proTEJO, the Movement for the Tagus, reported on 2 June 2026 a resurgence of pollution in the Tagus river, which it attributes to effluent discharges from Vila Velha de Ródão, in the Upper Tagus, down to Chamusca, in the Tagus Lezíria. In a statement, the movement reported episodes of abundant foam and dark waters, now yellowish in tone, recorded near the Belver dam and at points such as Ortiga (Mação), Abrantes, Constância and Vila Nova da Barquinha.</p><p>According to proTEJO, the pattern is the same one the movement has documented and denounced for over a decade: already in January 2026 it had reported to IGAMAOT abundant foam between the Fratel dam and Barca da Amieira, and in May new images near the Belver dam again confirmed the situation. The movement notes that, since at least 2015, the Tagus has been cyclically affected by intense pollution episodes originating in the Upper Tagus, and that in 2018 the Portuguese Environment Agency itself confirmed cellulose fibre levels thousands of times above recommended values, linked to discharges from the Celtejo pulp mill in Vila Velha de Ródão.</p><p>proTEJO is demanding immediate full water-quality testing upstream and downstream of the Vila Velha de Ródão river pier, regular inspection of discharges including at night, public disclosure of monitoring-station data, the review or suspension of effluent discharge licences in cases of proven non-compliance, and the urgent scheduling of a meeting of the Tagus River Pollution Monitoring Committee with the Ministry of Environment and Energy, APA, IGAMAOT and civil society representatives. The movement also criticises the failure to deliver on a promise made in 2019 to modernise the National Water Resources Information System for real-time data, similar to Spain's SAIH system.</p>","fontes":[["Observador/Lusa news agency: Movimento denuncia ressurgimento de poluição no Tejo e exige medidas urgentes (2 Jun 2026, in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2026/06/02/movimento-denuncia-ressurgimento-de-poluicao-no-tejo-e-exige-medidas-urgentes/"],["Médio Tejo: Movimento proTEJO denuncia ressurgimento de poluição e exige medidas urgentes (2 Jun 2026, in Portuguese)","https://mediotejo.net/movimento-protejo-denuncia-ressurgimento-de-poluicao-e-exige-medidas-urgentes/"]],"stat":"Pollution documented by proTEJO since at least 2015","link":"https://observador.pt/2026/06/02/movimento-denuncia-ressurgimento-de-poluicao-no-tejo-e-exige-medidas-urgentes/","linkL":"Read on Observador"},"rio-alviela-poluicao":{"corpo":"<p>The Alviela river, a tributary of the Tagus in the Santarém district, has suffered polluting discharges for decades. In 1976 the Commission for the Fight against the Pollution of the Alviela (CLAPA), one of the first environmental associations in the country, was founded in Pernes; its founder, Joaquim Jorge Duarte, had already taken bottles of river water to Parliament in 1970 to show the pollution.</p>\n<p>In December 2025, a new pollution episode in Pernes, with \"abundant foam and a foul smell\", according to residents and CLAPA, led nine organisations (CLAPA, GEOTA, proTEJO, WWF Portugal, FAPAS, ZERO, SPEA, LPN and Quercus) to denounce the lack of structural responses. According to the organisations, the Alcanena wastewater treatment plant, upstream, lacks the capacity to cope after heavy rain, and wastewater reaches the river untreated. They warned that these discharges are incompatible with the ecological restoration of the river under the Rios Livres programme, led by GEOTA since 2022, and asked the Government for political commitment, identified structural solutions, public monitoring of water quality and participation of communities and associations in decisions. CLAPA's president, Penélope de Melo, said it is unacceptable that, \"after half a century of struggle\", the Alviela continues to suffer unpunished environmental attacks.</p>\n<p>On 11 February 2026, on a rainy day, the river again showed brown foam and a foul smell in Pernes, which CLAPA attributed to effluent from livestock farms upstream of the village. The association says it has repeatedly reported the problem without any response from the authorities; residents complained that the GNR's environmental unit (SEPNA) only takes reports by phone between 9 am and 5 pm. The mayor of Santarém, João Leite, asked the Government to invest in environmental inspection and monitoring.</p>\n<p>In March 2026, CLAPA, now CLAPA, Associação Popular Ecológica, became active again with a new board, to monitor pollution, raise public awareness and work with public and scientific bodies to protect the Alviela.</p>","fontes":[["Mais Ribatejo/Lusa: Environmental organisations denounce chronic pollution of the Alviela river and demand structural solutions (16 Dec 2025) (in Portuguese)","https://maisribatejo.pt/poluicao-rio-alviela-alerta-ambientalistas-santarem/"],["SAPO: Alviela suffers another polluting discharge on a rainy day (11 Feb 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://sapo.pt/artigo/alviela-volta-a-sofrer-descarga-poluente-em-dia-de-chuva-698c695a857341060c3dca41"],["O Mirante: Historic environmental association of Pernes becomes active again (Mar 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://omirante.pt/semanario/2026-03-01/sociedade/2026-03-04-historica-associacao-ambientalista-de-pernes-volta-ao-activo-038359a5"]],"stat":"50 years of struggle against the pollution of the Alviela","link":"https://maisribatejo.pt/poluicao-rio-alviela-alerta-ambientalistas-santarem/","linkL":"Read on Mais Ribatejo (in Portuguese)"},"rio-maior-vala-real-poluicao":{"corpo":"<p>The Maior river rises in the municipality of Rio Maior and crosses the municipalities of Santarém, Cartaxo and Azambuja, where it is known as the Vala Real, before flowing into the Tagus. According to the region's environmental movements, it receives polluting discharges every year at the start of the tomato season, a situation they say has been happening since 1965 and which has been reported several times to the Portuguese Environment Agency (APA), the General Inspectorate for Agriculture, Sea, Environment and Spatial Planning (IGAMAOT) and Rio Maior Council. \"The lezíria is dying\", warns José Lousa, from EcoCartaxo, in a documentary by the PÓLEN collective.</p>\n<p>In August 2023, after reports of discharges with a \"red, pasty colour\" and a strong smell, APA took samples at the discharge point of a tomato processing company in São João da Ribeira and in the river, upstream and downstream, to check compliance with the conditions of the company's wastewater discharge licence and the effects on the river.</p>\n<p>On 19 September 2025, Movimento Cívico Ar Puro, EcoCartaxo and Movimento Ecologista do Vale de Santarém, members of proTEJO, reported new discharges in São João da Ribeira, coinciding with the start of the tomato season. According to the movements, the discharges were made through a stretch of ditch not visible from the public road, on private land covered by a building and vegetation, which flows into the Maior river about 800 metres downstream; with extreme drought and very low flow, the river becomes an \"open sewer\" every year. They asked APA and IGAMAOT to stop the discharges and hold polluters accountable, to include the Maior river in the Tagus River Basin Management Plan (2022/2027) and to reactivate the Tagus pollution monitoring commission, inactive since 2018. The only tomato processing plant in the parish declined to comment; APA and the council did not respond to Lusa.</p>","fontes":[["Observador/Lusa: Environmentalists warn of discharges into the Maior river and blame the tomato industry (19 Sep 2025) (in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2025/09/19/ecologistas-alertam-para-descargas-no-rio-maior-e-responsabilizam-industria-do-tomate/"],["Ambiente Online: Civic movements warn of persistent pollution of the Maior river by agro-industry (19 Sep 2025) (in Portuguese)","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/movimentos-civicos-alertam-para-poluicao-persistente-do-rio-maior-pela-agroindustria"],["Entroncamento Online: Environmental movements report new polluting discharge into the Maior river and demand action (19 Sep 2025) (in Portuguese)","https://www.entroncamentoonline.pt/portal/movimentos-ecologistas-denunciam-nova-descarga-poluente-no-rio-maior-e-exigem-acao-das-autoridades/"],["Ambiente Online: APA checks compliance of discharges by a tomato processing company in Rio Maior (30 Aug 2023) (in Portuguese)","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/noticias/apa-averigua-cumprimento-das-descargas-de-empresa-de-processamento-de-tomate-em-rio-maior"],["PÓLEN (YouTube): Guardians of the Tagus, Vala Real (in Portuguese)","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n_oI9hDZcTU"]],"stat":"Discharges reported since 1965","link":"https://observador.pt/2025/09/19/ecologistas-alertam-para-descargas-no-rio-maior-e-responsabilizam-industria-do-tomate/","linkL":"Read on Observador (in Portuguese)"},"obra-laso-vale-sao-giao-milharado":{"corpo":"<p>In Vale de São Gião, in the parish of Milharado, Mafra municipality, next to the Cabeço de Montachique Municipal Park (Loures municipality), the transport company LASO bought architect Pardal Monteiro's former estate and Casal do Alfaiate, a former branch of the Freixial poultry farms, demolished the buildings and razed the hill and its trees. The two watercourses crossing the properties were merged into one.</p>","fontes":[["oRegiões: Asbestos buried \"on the sly\" in Vale de São Gião puts residents at risk (Alfredo Miranda, 14 Jul 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://oregioes.pt/exclusivo-amianto-soterrado-a-ma-fila-no-vale-de-sao-giao-coloca-em-risco-moradores/"],["Jornal de Mafra, readers' letters: The Pardal Monteiro estate has disappeared (24 Jun 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://jornaldemafra.pt/voz-do-leitor-a-quinta-pardal-monteiro-desapareceu/"],["Milharado Parish Council: Minutes of the Parish Assembly of 23 June 2026 (PDF, in Portuguese)","https://www.milharado.pt/ficheiros/fic37_1783675000.PDF"],["LASO Transportes: About LASO","https://www.laso.pt/en/about-laso/"],["Loures Municipality: Cabeço de Montachique Municipal Park (in Portuguese)","https://www.cm-loures.pt/AreaConteudo.aspx?DisplayId=994"]],"stat":"Asbestos buried next to diverted watercourses","link":"https://oregioes.pt/exclusivo-amianto-soterrado-a-ma-fila-no-vale-de-sao-giao-coloca-em-risco-moradores/","linkL":"Read the report on oRegiões (in Portuguese)","cronologia":[{"data":"2024","texto":"At the end of the year, LASO buys the estate that belonged to architect Porfírio Pardal Monteiro; within about a month the buildings are demolished and the woodland destroyed. According to oRegiões, SEPNA issued fines and the works, unlicensed, stopped for some months.","fonte":"https://oregioes.pt/exclusivo-amianto-soterrado-a-ma-fila-no-vale-de-sao-giao-coloca-em-risco-moradores/"},{"data":"2026-06-23","texto":"At the Milharado Parish Assembly, the Vale de São Gião residents' association raises the case; the parish president says he has complained to Mafra Council and did not know of the building project.","fonte":"https://www.milharado.pt/ficheiros/fic37_1783675000.PDF"},{"data":"2026-06-24","texto":"A reader's letter in Jornal de Mafra reports that \"the mountain was razed\" and that trees and asbestos-cement roofing were buried next to an altered watercourse.","fonte":"https://jornaldemafra.pt/voz-do-leitor-a-quinta-pardal-monteiro-desapareceu/"},{"data":"2026-06-30","texto":"The case is raised at the Mafra Municipal Assembly.","fonte":"https://oregioes.pt/exclusivo-amianto-soterrado-a-ma-fila-no-vale-de-sao-giao-coloca-em-risco-moradores/"},{"data":"2026-07-14","texto":"oRegiões reports that, according to residents and a Council source, asbestos roofing was demolished and buried next to diverted watercourses; residents complained to ICNF, the Environment Agency, SEPNA, the GNR and the Council, and the project for the plots was submitted without being licensed.","fonte":"https://oregioes.pt/exclusivo-amianto-soterrado-a-ma-fila-no-vale-de-sao-giao-coloca-em-risco-moradores/"}],"contexto":"In Vale de São Gião, in the parish of Milharado, Mafra municipality, next to the Cabeço de Montachique Municipal Park (Loures municipality), the transport company LASO bought architect Pardal Monteiro's former estate and Casal do Alfaiate, a former branch of the Freixial poultry farms, demolished the buildings and razed the hill and its trees. The two watercourses crossing the properties were merged into one."},"estufas-odemira-parque-natural-sudoeste":{"corpo":"<p>The Mira Irrigation Perimeter, about 12,000 hectares in Odemira and Aljezur supplied by the Santa Clara dam, lies inside the Southwest Alentejo and Vicentine Coast Natural Park. Intensive farming in plastic greenhouses and tunnels, mainly of berries, has grown there.</p>","fontes":[["Juntos pelo Sudoeste (Facebook)","https://www.facebook.com/juntospelosudoeste/"],["ZERO: Agricultura intensiva sem controlo no Parque Natural do Sudoeste Alentejano e Costa Vicentina (2017, atualizado em 2023) (in Portuguese)","https://zero.ong/noticias/agricultura-intensiva-sem-controlo-no-parque-natural-do-sudoeste-alentejano-e-costa-vicentina/"],["Rádio Pax: Juntos pelo Sudoeste entregou petição na Assembleia da República (3 mar. 2020) (in Portuguese)","https://www.radiopax.com/juntos-pelo-sudoeste-entregou-peticao-na-assembleia-da-republica/"],["Agroportal: Juntos pelo Sudoeste, a favor do Parque Natural, contra as estufas (21 mai. 2021) (in Portuguese)","https://www.agroportal.pt/juntos-pelo-sudoeste-a-favor-do-parque-natural-contra-as-estufas/"],["Correio de Lagos: Juntos pelo Sudoeste saúda a mega-operação do ICNF no Parque Natural (24 jan. 2023) (in Portuguese)","https://correiodelagos.com/politica-ambiente/movimento-juntos-pelo-sudoeste-sauda-a-mega-operacao-do-icnf-no-parque-natural-do-sudoeste-alentejano-e-costa-vicentina-e/"],["Correio de Lagos: Juntos pelo Sudoeste, água decide o futuro em Odemira (2023) (in Portuguese)","https://correiodelagos.com/politica-ambiente/juntos-pelo-sudoeste-agua-decide-o-futuro-em-odemira/"],["Green Savers: Juntos pelo Sudoeste contesta alívio de restrições à agricultura em barragem de Odemira (17 abr. 2025) (in Portuguese)","https://greensavers.sapo.pt/juntos-pelo-sudoeste-contesta-alivio-de-restricoes-a-agricultura-em-barragem-de-odemira/"],["SAPO/Lusa: Odemira prevê mais água para agricultura no perímetro de rega do Mira em 2026 (27 dez. 2025) (in Portuguese)","https://sapo.pt/artigo/odemira-preve-mais-agua-para-agricultura-no-perimetro-de-rega-do-mira-em-2026-694fe4a52c7b75270a56e87d"]],"stat":"Up to 30% of the perimeter may be under greenhouses","link":"","linkL":"","contexto":"The Mira Irrigation Perimeter, about 12,000 hectares in Odemira and Aljezur supplied by the Santa Clara dam, lies inside the Southwest Alentejo and Vicentine Coast Natural Park. Intensive farming in plastic greenhouses and tunnels, mainly of berries, has grown there.","cronologia":[{"data":"2017-08-25","texto":"ZERO warns of uncontrolled intensive farming in the Natural Park: the park authority says it does not know the area covered by greenhouses and tunnels, in a perimeter where the legal limit is 30%.","fonte":"https://zero.ong/noticias/agricultura-intensiva-sem-controlo-no-parque-natural-do-sudoeste-alentejano-e-costa-vicentina/"},{"data":"2019","texto":"A Council of Ministers resolution (no. 179/2019) creates a transitional regime for the Mira Irrigation Perimeter that allows the plastic-covered area to triple.","fonte":"https://www.radiopax.com/juntos-pelo-sudoeste-entregou-peticao-na-assembleia-da-republica/"},{"data":"2020-03-02","texto":"The Juntos pelo Sudoeste movement delivers to Parliament a petition with about 6,000 signatures, \"The Southwest Alentejo and Vicentine Coast Natural Park cannot take any more intensive farming\".","fonte":"https://www.radiopax.com/juntos-pelo-sudoeste-entregou-peticao-na-assembleia-da-republica/"},{"data":"2021-06-01","texto":"The petition is debated in Parliament. The movement estimates 1,600 hectares of greenhouses (11% of the perimeter), which could reach 4,800, and has filed complaints with the Beja court, the Ombudsman and the European Commission.","fonte":"https://www.agroportal.pt/juntos-pelo-sudoeste-a-favor-do-parque-natural-contra-as-estufas/"},{"data":"2023-01-17","texto":"An ICNF operation inspects 110 farms in the Natural Park and finds irregularities in 95; the movement welcomes it and calls for regular inspections.","fonte":"https://correiodelagos.com/politica-ambiente/movimento-juntos-pelo-sudoeste-sauda-a-mega-operacao-do-icnf-no-parque-natural-do-sudoeste-alentejano-e-costa-vicentina-e/","dataFim":"2023-01-19"},{"data":"2023","texto":"With the Santa Clara dam at 37% of capacity, the movement warns that the river no longer flows downstream and that investors keep asking for irrigation water.","fonte":"https://correiodelagos.com/politica-ambiente/juntos-pelo-sudoeste-agua-decide-o-futuro-em-odemira/"},{"data":"2025-04-08","texto":"The Government eases irrigation restrictions from the Santa Clara dam, then at 59%; Juntos pelo Sudoeste calls the measure \"hasty and isolated\".","fonte":"https://greensavers.sapo.pt/juntos-pelo-sudoeste-contesta-alivio-de-restricoes-a-agricultura-em-barragem-de-odemira/"},{"data":"2025-12-27","texto":"The Mira irrigation association plans 16 cubic hectometres for 2026, one more than in 2025, including water for new areas of annual and permanent crops.","fonte":"https://sapo.pt/artigo/odemira-preve-mais-agua-para-agricultura-no-perimetro-de-rega-do-mira-em-2026-694fe4a52c7b75270a56e87d"}]},"captacao-pomarao-guadiana-algarve":{"corpo":"<p>Águas do Algarve wants to abstract water from the Guadiana estuary near Pomarão (Mértola) and carry it through a pipeline of about 40 kilometres to the Odeleite dam, in Castro Marim, to reinforce the Algarve's supply.</p>","fontes":[["Plataforma Água Sustentável","https://plataformaaguasustentavel.wordpress.com/"],["Barlavento: Zero contesta captação de água do Guadiana no Pomarão para o Algarve (3 mai. 2024) (in Portuguese)","https://www.barlavento.pt/zero-contesta-captacao-de-agua-do-guadiana-no-pomarao-para-o-algarve/"],["Ambiente Online: Plataforma Água Sustentável contesta reforço do abastecimento de água ao Algarve através do Pomarão (8 mai. 2024) (in Portuguese)","https://www.ambienteonline.pt/exclusivos/plataforma-agua-sustentavel-contesta-reforco-do-abastecimento-de-agua-ao-algarve-atraves-do-pomarao"],["Rádio Pax: Projeto de milhões ameaça secar o Alentejo para abastecer o Algarve (26 set. 2024) (in Portuguese)","https://www.radiopax.com/projeto-de-milhoes-ameaca-secar-o-alentejo-para-abastecer-o-algarve/"],["ODigital: Associação de Mértola contesta em tribunal captação de água no Pomarão (28 nov. 2024) (in Portuguese)","https://odigital.sapo.pt/associacao-de-mertola-contesta-em-tribunal-captacao-de-agua-no-pomarao/"],["Governo: Lançado concurso público para a Tomada de Água do Pomarão no valor de 109 milhões de euros (13 dez. 2024) (in Portuguese)","https://www.portugal.gov.pt/pt/gc24/comunicacao/comunicado?i=lancado-concurso-publico-para-a-tomada-de-agua-do-pomarao-no-valor-de-109-milhoes-de-euros"],["Jornal PT Green: Captação de água no Pomarão avança com concurso público de 122,2 milhões (8 jul. 2026) (in Portuguese)","https://jornalptgreen.pt/noticia/captacao-de-agua-no-pomarao-avanca-com-concurso-publico-de-1222-milhoes/"]],"stat":"Up to 30 hm³ a year","link":"","linkL":"","contexto":"Águas do Algarve wants to abstract water from the Guadiana estuary near Pomarão (Mértola) and carry it through a pipeline of about 40 kilometres to the Odeleite dam, in Castro Marim, to reinforce the Algarve's supply.","cronologia":[{"data":"2024-05-03","texto":"ZERO contests the project: increasing abstraction of a scarce resource lets the region's agriculture maintain or increase consumption, and the study downplays impacts on the Guadiana estuary.","fonte":"https://www.barlavento.pt/zero-contesta-captacao-de-agua-do-guadiana-no-pomarao-para-o-algarve/"},{"data":"2024-05-08","texto":"The Plataforma Água Sustentável, with 13 associations, contests the works for allowing \"the increase of intensive farming, polluting and wasteful of the scarce resource\".","fonte":"https://www.ambienteonline.pt/exclusivos/plataforma-agua-sustentavel-contesta-reforco-do-abastecimento-de-agua-ao-algarve-atraves-do-pomarao"},{"data":"2024-09-26","texto":"Mértola Council contests the project and EDIA, the Alqueva company, warns that there may not be water available for this new abstraction.","fonte":"https://www.radiopax.com/projeto-de-milhoes-ameaca-secar-o-alentejo-para-abastecer-o-algarve/"},{"data":"2024-10","texto":"At the Portuguese-Spanish summit, Portugal and Spain set a maximum of 30 cubic hectometres a year for the abstraction.","fonte":"https://odigital.sapo.pt/associacao-de-mertola-contesta-em-tribunal-captacao-de-agua-no-pomarao/"},{"data":"2024-11","texto":"The Amigos da Formôa association files an action at the Beja Administrative and Tax Court to annul the Environmental Impact Statement, citing risks to the Guadiana and to threatened species such as the saramugo.","fonte":"https://odigital.sapo.pt/associacao-de-mertola-contesta-em-tribunal-captacao-de-agua-no-pomarao/"},{"data":"2024-12-13","texto":"The Government launches a 109 million euro international tender and states that the water is exclusively for human consumption in the Algarve.","fonte":"https://www.portugal.gov.pt/pt/gc24/comunicacao/comunicado?i=lancado-concurso-publico-para-a-tomada-de-agua-do-pomarao-no-valor-de-109-milhoes-de-euros"},{"data":"2026-07-08","texto":"Águas do Algarve launches a 122.23 million euro tender for the first phase: intake, pumping station, pipeline and reservoir in Mértola, Alcoutim and Castro Marim.","fonte":"https://jornalptgreen.pt/noticia/captacao-de-agua-no-pomarao-avanca-com-concurso-publico-de-1222-milhoes/"}]},"incendio-carrazeda-ansiaes-protecao-civil":{"corpo":"<p>According to the Lusa news agency, the fire broke out on 15 August 2026 in the municipality of Torre de Moncorvo and spread the next day to Carrazeda de Ansiães, where it burned for several days and consumed about 4,000 hectares of scrub and farmland. JN describes a fire that lasted five days, starting in Cabeça Boa, and left \"at least three thousand hectares burned, and heavy agricultural losses\". On 10 September, the Secretary of State for Civil Protection, Rui Rocha, gave an estimate of more than 3,600 hectares burned across the two municipalities, a figure still to be confirmed.</p>\n<p>On 26 August, JN reported that residents of Vilarinho da Castanheira and Pinhal do Douro, in Carrazeda de Ansiães, were calling for accountability, circulating a petition to send with a complaint to the Ministry of Internal Administration, and organising a protest against the \"lack of coordination\" of resources in fighting the fire.</p>\n<p>On 30 August, the spokesperson for the \"Isto Não Fica Assim\" movement, Pedro Correia, told Lusa that residents are \"outraged and indignant\" with the National Emergency and Civil Protection Authority (ANEPC), which they believe \"failed\" because it did not know the area. He said that on the night of 15 to 16 August he told the command that resources had been withdrawn from a fire front near the village's water mills, and that his suggestion was ignored; the area around the mills burned. He criticised the Douro sub-regional command for the resources it deployed and for what he sees as a \"let it burn\" policy, but stressed: \"We have nothing to say against the firefighters. The firefighters were the ones who kept the tragedy from being even bigger\". \"The land was almost entirely burned, we lost our cork oaks, we lost many olive trees, almond trees, vines\", he said. The movement wants to be compensated \"for the damage caused to us by the command's incompetence\" and is calling for prevention measures such as firebreaks and planting cork oaks and more resistant trees. It is running a petition, online and on paper, to deliver to the Minister of Internal Administration, and threatened to hold a protest if the Government did not listen.</p>\n<p>On 10 September, after a meeting with local mayors, Rui Rocha said ANEPC is analysing the timeline of the fire, which was fought between 16 and 19 August: \"It is legitimate for a group of citizens to protest and to bring us their concerns about this fire\". He said he was waiting for the petition to be delivered and that an assessment would be made to understand \"whether anything did not go well, or went really badly\".</p>","fontes":[["Diário de Trás-os-Montes/Lusa: Residents of Carrazeda de Ansiães question Civil Protection's response (30 Aug. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/moradores-em-carrazeda-de-ansiaes-poem-em-causa-atuacao-da-protecao-civil"],["Mensageiro de Bragança: Authorities assessing the timeline of the Carrazeda de Ansiães fire (10 Sept. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://www.mdb.pt/noticia/autoridades-estao-avaliar-fita-do-tempo-do-fogo-de-carrazeda-de-ansiaes"],["JN: Carrazeda residents protest against how the major fire was fought (26 Aug. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://www.jn.pt/pais/artigo/populacao-de-carrazeda-protesta-contra-forma-como-foi-combatido-o-grande-fogo/18119814"]],"stat":"More than 3,600 hectares burned in Torre de Moncorvo and Carrazeda de Ansiães (Government estimate)","link":"https://www.diariodetrasosmontes.com/noticia/moradores-em-carrazeda-de-ansiaes-poem-em-causa-atuacao-da-protecao-civil","linkL":"Read in Diário de Trás-os-Montes (in Portuguese)"},"eucalipto-lei-plantacao-nacional":{"corpo":"<p>After the 2017 wildfires, the law banned new eucalyptus plantations, allowing only the replanting of areas previously occupied by the species. According to the National Forest Inventory (2015 data), cited by Quercus, eucalyptus covers about 844,000 hectares, close to 26% of the mainland's forest area.</p>\n<p>On 13 January 2026, Quercus warned that more than two thirds of burned eucalyptus plantations are hidden from national statistics, because young, regenerating or recently felled eucalyptus stands are classified as \"scrubland\" in satellite data. It gave the 2024 Arouca fire and the Pedrógão Grande fire as examples, and called for the classification protocols to be corrected, for eucalyptus plantations to require a licence, and for them to be georeferenced on public platforms.</p>\n<p>On 22 May 2026, Navigator's chief executive, João Lé, called for a review of the legislation limiting eucalyptus planting, so that \"national regulation moves from a purely prohibitive and punitive paradigm to a model that fosters and encourages investment\". \"Portugal urgently needs an RJAR [Legal Regime for Afforestation and Reforestation] that is an instrument of promotion and not of blockage\", he said, arguing for the afforestation of scrubland with productive potential.</p>\n<p>On 29 July 2026, according to Lusa, the Floresta do Futuro (Forest of the Future) movement accused the Government of funding eucalyptus plantations while Europe burns: under the new rules of the Floresta Ativa programme, announced by the Secretary of State for Forests, Rui Ladeira, and relaunched with four million euros from the Environmental Fund, all species, including eucalyptus, can now apply, and eucalyptus plantations can receive up to 800 euros per hectare. The movement says that, at the same time, those who planted native species struggle to recover the money invested in fuel management.</p>\n<p>On 20 August 2026, Quercus and the international Environmental Paper Network demanded a \"moratorium on new afforestation and reforestation with eucalyptus\", binding targets to reduce eucalyptus area by 2030, more inspections, a tax on the pulp and biomass industries, and gradual replacement with native species such as oaks, cork oaks, chestnuts and holm oaks.</p>","fontes":[["Jornal Económico/Lusa: Navigator wants review of legislation limiting eucalyptus planting (22 May 2026, in Portuguese)","https://jornaleconomico.sapo.pt/noticias/navigator-quer-revisao-da-legislacao-que-limita-plantacao-de-eucaliptos/"],["Agroportal/Lusa: Floresta do Futuro movement accuses Government of funding eucalyptus plantations while Europe burns (29 Jul. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://www.agroportal.pt/movimento-floresta-do-futuro-acusa-governo-de-financiar-eucaliptais-enquanto-europa-arde/"],["Mais Ribatejo: Quercus and environmental network call for moratorium on new eucalyptus plantations (20 Aug. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://maisribatejo.pt/quercus-moratoria-eucalipto-portugal/"],["SAPO/Canal Alentejo: Quercus warns burned eucalyptus is hidden in statistics and calls for corrections (13 Jan. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://sapo.pt/artigo/quercus-alerta-ocultacao-de-eucaliptal-ardido-e-pede-correcoes-6966c7aaf3fe72dfb23955ac"]],"stat":"About 844,000 hectares of eucalyptus, close to 26% of mainland forest (National Forest Inventory, 2015)","link":"https://maisribatejo.pt/quercus-moratoria-eucalipto-portugal/","linkL":"Read in Mais Ribatejo (in Portuguese)"},"incendios-outubro-2017-casas-por-reconstruir":{"corpo":"<p>The wildfires of 15 October 2017 hit Portugal's Centre Region. The Midões Fire Victims Support Association (MAAVIM), in Tábua, defends people harmed by those fires.</p>\n<p>In October 2023, according to Lusa, MAAVIM appealed to the Supreme Court of Justice after the Coimbra Court of Appeal refused to let it join, as an assisting party, the criminal case over the October 2017 fires in Coimbra district, which the Public Prosecutor had closed. The courts found that the movement lacks standing because it is not an environmental protection association. \"We want to make sure there is a trial and that this does not end with the case being closed\", the movement's spokesperson said at the time.</p>\n<p>On 4 May 2026, according to MAAVIM figures reported by JN, about 20 families in the Centre Region, in the Coimbra, Viseu and Guarda districts, were still waiting for their main homes to be rebuilt. According to the movement, in some cases the works were contracted, with contracts signed, companies paid and supervision in place, but the houses were never built. Some delays are due to legalisation problems or to victims being unable to deal with the paperwork. Some families are living with relatives and others have left the country. The spokesperson, Nuno Tavares Pereira, told Renascença the families \"are willing to do anything\", after so much time \"without answers\": \"There is no reason for these cases not to have been done, when others were done where nobody lived and the homes were rebuilt\". MAAVIM is considering a complaint against the Portuguese State at the European Court of Human Rights once national remedies are exhausted, and had a meeting scheduled for 19 May with the Parliamentary Inquiry Committee on the Rural Fires Business.</p>\n<p>According to ZAP, citing JN, the Centre Regional Coordination and Development Commission received 1,340 applications for support, of which 849 qualified under the Permanent Housing Recovery Support Programme, has cases pending in Pampilhosa da Serra, Poiares and Vouzela, and says it is working to complete them by 2026.</p>","fontes":[["Renascença: 2017 wildfires. Families still without homes consider going to court (4 May 2026, in Portuguese)","https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2026/05/04/incendios-de-2017-familias-que-continuam-sem-casa-ponderam-ir-para-tribunal/469399/"],["ZAP: There are still families without homes after the 2017 wildfires. They want to sue the State (4 May 2026, in Portuguese)","https://zap.aeiou.pt/ainda-ha-familias-sem-casa-devido-aos-incendios-de-2017-querem-processar-o-estado-740827"],["Agroportal/Lusa: Movement appeals to Supreme Court to join the October 2017 fires case (25 Oct. 2023, in Portuguese)","https://www.agroportal.pt/?p=1044051"]],"stat":"About 20 families still without a home, almost ten years after the fires","link":"https://rr.pt/noticia/pais/2026/05/04/incendios-de-2017-familias-que-continuam-sem-casa-ponderam-ir-para-tribunal/469399/","linkL":"Read on Renascença (in Portuguese)"},"mina-litio-argemela":{"corpo":"<p>The Serra da Argemela lies between the municipalities of Covilhã and Fundão, near the villages of Barco, Coutada, Silvares and Lavacolhos, and was mined for tin for decades. In 2019, according to Diário Digital Castelo Branco, the Group for the Preservation of Serra da Argemela (GPSA) and local people already opposed open-pit mining (\"Open-pit, no!\"), and on 21 May that year the Government rejected a request for experimental mining by PANNN, Consultores de Geociências, because no environmental impact assessment had been submitted.</p>\n<p>On 28 October 2021, a concession contract was signed to mine lithium and other minerals over an area of 403.7 hectares, with Neomia, Minérios Argemela (Almina Group).</p>\n<p>In an opinion dated 30 December 2024 and made public in April 2025, the Portuguese Environment Agency (APA) rejected outright the request for an environmental impact assessment of the mine, because the study did not have \"the level of detail needed for the execution project stage\" and showed \"gaps in the project and in key environmental factors\". The president of GPSA, Gabriela Margarido, said she hoped the Government would \"recognise, once and for all, the mistake that authorising mining in Argemela would be\".</p>\n<p>On 17 April 2025, the Secretary of State for Energy, Jean Barroca, told Rádio Covilhã that, to start mining the concession, the company \"will have to restart a process\" of assessment, with a new public consultation, and that there is no deadline for doing so. As of October 2026, we found no news of a new environmental impact study.</p>","fontes":[["Ambiente Online: Argemela mine environmental impact study rejected, says APA (Apr. 2025, in Portuguese)","https://ambienteonline.pt/destaques/estudo-de-impacte-ambiental-da-mina-da-argemela-foi-indeferido-avanca-a-apa"],["Rádio Covilhã: Argemela: concession holder must start a new Environmental Impact Study (17 Apr. 2025, in Portuguese)","https://radio-covilha.pt/2025/04/noticias/argemela-concessionaria-obrigada-a-iniciar-novo-estudo-de-impacte-ambiental/"],["Diário Digital Castelo Branco: Local people reject open-pit mining for lithium in the Serra da Argemela (1 Aug. 2019, in Portuguese)","https://www.diariodigitalcastelobranco.pt/noticia/50473/reportagem-fundao-covilha-populacoes-recusam-exploracao-mineira-a-ceu-aberto-na-procura-de-litio-na-serra-da-argemela"]],"stat":"403.7 hectares under lithium concession between Covilhã and Fundão","link":"https://ambienteonline.pt/destaques/estudo-de-impacte-ambiental-da-mina-da-argemela-foi-indeferido-avanca-a-apa","linkL":"Read in Ambiente Online (in Portuguese)"},"barragens-terges-cobres-carreiras-guadiana":{"corpo":"<p>In June 2026, the Alqueva Development and Infrastructure Company (EDIA) opened a public tender for the design and environmental impact study of the Terges e Cobres dam, in the municipalities of Beja and Mértola, worth 990,000 euros (plus VAT), and announced a tender for the Carreiras dam, in Mértola. Both projects, on the Terges, Cobres and Carreiras streams, tributaries of the Guadiana downstream of the Alqueva-Pedrógão system, are part of the national \"Água que Une\" (Water that Unites) strategy. EDIA's president, José Pedro Salema, argues that the dams will \"ensure ecological flows in the lower Guadiana, relieving pressure on Alqueva\".</p>\n<p>On 20 June 2026, according to Lusa, ZERO demanded that the tenders be suspended, an independent post-assessment of the Alqueva Multi-Purpose Project before any new works, and \"a formal commitment from the Government not to build new dams on the Guadiana's tributaries\", saying that \"desertification and water scarcity may be causing hallucinations among policymakers\". According to ZERO, these streams have no flow in summer, in a region forecast to get less rain; the Guadiana basin already has a water exploitation index (WEI+) of 51%, among the highest in the country; about 95% of the water distributed by Alqueva serves private economic activities, and about 80% of the irrigated area is olive groves, in a country that already produces twice the olive oil it consumes. For the association, the dams serve to keep expanding agriculture.</p>\n<p>On 24 June 2026, the Association of Alqueva Landowners and Beneficiaries (APBA) disputed ZERO's position, which it says shows a \"disconnect between desk activism and the reality of a territory at risk\", and argued that holding back floodwater \"is not an attack on nature, but the only effective shield\" against climate change. Mértola municipal council supports the investments.</p>","fontes":[["barlavento/Lusa: Zero association against new Alqueva dams on Guadiana tributaries (20 Jun. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://www.barlavento.pt/associacao-zero-contra-barragens-alqueva-afluentes-guadiana/"],["Agroportal: ZERO demands immediate suspension of projects for new dams on the Guadiana (22 Jun. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://www.agroportal.pt/zero-exige-a-suspensao-imediata-dos-projetos-para-novas-barragens-no-guadiana/"],["Rádio Planície: APBA defends new dams in Alentejo against criticism from Zero (24 Jun. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://radioplanicie.com/noticias/apba-defende-novas-barragens-no-alentejo-contra-criticas-da-associacao-zero"]],"stat":"990,000 euros just for the design and impact study of Terges e Cobres","link":"https://www.barlavento.pt/associacao-zero-contra-barragens-alqueva-afluentes-guadiana/","linkL":"Read in barlavento (in Portuguese)"},"aterro-sotavento-cortelha-loule":{"corpo":"<p>The Sotavento Landfill, run by Algar, is in Cortelha, in the interior of Loulé municipality, and takes waste from Alcoutim, Castro Marim, Faro, Loulé, Olhão, São Brás de Alportel, Tavira and Vila Real de Santo António. According to barlavento, it receives about 150,000 tonnes a year and the cell in use was close to full.</p>\n<p>In May 2022, ZERO accused the landfill of operating \"illegally since 2017\", because its expansion with cell C, built in 2017 and 2018, had not undergone an Environmental Impact Assessment. The CCDR Algarve replied that the APA environmental licence was valid until 16 August 2026 and that ICNF had found it unnecessary to subject cell C to an assessment.</p>\n<p>From 23 December 2025 to 4 February 2026, the environmental impact study for a new Cell D, promoted by Algar, was under public consultation. According to ZERO, 152 of the submissions (97.44%) opposed the project.</p>\n<p>On 22 June 2026, Loulé Municipal Assembly unanimously approved a motion from the PS demanding that the landfill close for good after Cell D, a written commitment to that effect, a study to move waste management out of the municipality, an environmental rehabilitation plan for Cortelha, and independent monitoring of groundwater and soils. According to Algarve Marafado, residents complain of a \"nauseating smell, growing lorry traffic and a constant threat to water resources, flora and fauna\".</p>\n<p>The CCDR Algarve's Environmental Impact Declaration for Cell D, made public in October 2026, is conditionally favourable and provides for capacity for about 875,000 tonnes, 150,000 tonnes a year and an estimated life of five to eight years. The declaration notes that landfilling waste with an unstabilised organic fraction is illegal under the legal regime for landfill. ZERO, which opposes the incinerator planned for the Algarve, argues that \"the new Cell D will have to be the end of the line for waste, not the destination for mixed waste\", and proposes expanding mechanical-biological treatment at Algar's plants.</p>","fontes":[["Algarve Marafado: Loulé politicians unite to demand the end of the landfill in the municipality (23 Jun. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://www.algarvemarafado.com/2026/06/23/lixo-politicos-de-loule-unem-se-para-exigir-o-fim-do-aterro-sanitario-no-concelho/"],["Jornal do Algarve/Lusa: Association backs mechanical-biological waste treatment and rejects incineration (6 Oct. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://jornaldoalgarve.pt/associacao-defende-tratamento-mecanico-e-biologico-dos-residuos-e-rejeita-incineracao/"],["ZERO: Mechanical-biological treatment, not incineration, is the immediate solution for Algarve waste (7 Oct. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://zero.ong/noticias/tratamento-mecanico-e-biologico-e-solucao-imediata-para-os-residuos-do-algarve-nao-a-incineracao/"],["Postal do Algarve: CCDR Algarve explains the situation of the Sotavento landfill (7 May 2022, in Portuguese)","https://postal.pt/nacional/ccdr-algarve-explica-situacao-do-aterro-sanitario-do-sotavento-que-associacao-zero-diz-funcionar-ilegalmente-desde-2017/"],["barlavento: Sotavento Landfill nears capacity limit (in Portuguese)","https://www.barlavento.pt/aterro-sanitario-do-sotavento-aproxima-se-do-limite-de-capacidade/"]],"stat":"97.44% of consultation submissions against Cell D (according to ZERO)","link":"https://www.algarvemarafado.com/2026/06/23/lixo-politicos-de-loule-unem-se-para-exigir-o-fim-do-aterro-sanitario-no-concelho/","linkL":"Read in Algarve Marafado (in Portuguese)"},"porto-cruz-foz-jamor-oeiras":{"corpo":"<p>The Detailed Plan for the Right Bank of the Mouth of the Jamor River was published in 2014, by decision of Oeiras Municipal Assembly, and frames the licensing application for the Porto Cruz subdivision, on the site of former factories at the mouth of the Jamor, in Cruz Quebrada, by the Tagus and the Jamor National Sports Centre.</p>\n<p>In February 2021, with the subdivision under public consultation, Oeiras council said the marina was essential to the development: according to New in Oeiras, the project includes five plots with six residential buildings, a hotel, offices and shops, the tallest with 19 storeys, and 1,639 parking spaces. The association warned of flood risk, more traffic and the impact on the landscape of the Jamor valley.</p>\n<p>On 30 March 2021, the Public Prosecutor announced it had brought an administrative action and, at the same time, an injunction to have provisions of the Detailed Plan declared illegal; the court provisionally suspended those provisions and the activities carried out under them, and the public consultation on the subdivision was halted. In February 2025, the council resumed the public consultation on the subdivision, requested by Aziprime Property Developer, SA.</p>\n<p>On 20 February 2026, according to Lusa, the association called on the council to back away from developing the right bank of the Jamor, which would bring \"towers of 17 and 19 storeys, 355 homes and more than 1,600 parking spaces\" to an area the Municipal Master Plan identifies as \"floodplain, estuary protection strip and erosion risk\". It recalled that the Public Prosecutor \"asked for the whole detailed plan to be declared illegal\", accused the mayor of holding back the results of the public consultation \"for 11 months\", and argued that recent coastal overtopping and floods show that dense urban development is incompatible with safety in the area.</p>\n<p>In August 2026, according to Lusa, trees and vegetation were cut on the former Gist-Brocades site, between the EN6 road and Cruz Quebrada station. The association criticised the indiscriminate felling of more than 30 native trees, including pines and plane trees, and warned that moving all that vegetation \"can carry sediments with it, which is harmful to public health\". The Working Conditions Authority said it found no breaches of labour law and would not say whether asbestos removal had been requested. Oeiras council confirmed that the subdivision \"has not been submitted to the municipal executive\", and that the public consultation report had been sent to the developers.</p>","fontes":[["Public Prosecutor: Detailed Plan for the Right Bank of the Mouth of the Jamor River (30 Mar. 2021, in Portuguese)","https://dcceicd.ministeriopublico.pt/destaque/plano-de-pormenor-da-margem-direita-da-foz-do-rio-jamor"],["Diário de Coimbra/Lusa: Vamos Salvar o Jamor association calls for retreat from floodplain development (20 Feb. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://www.diariocoimbra.pt/2026/02/20/associacao-vamos-salvar-o-jamor-apela-para-recuo-na-urbanizacao-em-leito-de-cheia/"],["Observador/Lusa: Tree and vegetation felling at the mouth of the Jamor without labour law breaches (28 Aug. 2026, in Portuguese)","https://observador.pt/2026/08/28/corte-de-arvoredo-e-vegetacao-na-foz-do-jamor-sem-infracoes-a-legislacao-laboral/"],["New in Oeiras: Oeiras council says marina is essential to Cruz Quebrada megaproject (17 Feb. 2021, in Portuguese)","https://newinoeiras.nit.pt/fora-de-casa/camara-de-oeiras-diz-que-marina-e-indispensavel-no-megaprojeto-na-cruz-quebrada"]],"stat":"17- and 19-storey towers, 355 homes and over 1,600 parking spaces on a floodplain","link":"https://www.diariocoimbra.pt/2026/02/20/associacao-vamos-salvar-o-jamor-apela-para-recuo-na-urbanizacao-em-leito-de-cheia/","linkL":"Read in Diário de Coimbra (in Portuguese)"}};

